Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.4 Modern epoch: a static auxiliary space", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14068019-de7d-384f-8063-15579d3a00ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When the auxiliary space has stopped evolving (b = b0, Hb = 0) the Lovelock \
tensors reduce to E^(1) = diag(3Ha\.b2, 2Ha\[Prime] + 3Ha\.b2, 3Ha\[Prime] + \
6Ha\.b2), E^(2) = diag(0, 0, \[Minus]12 Ha\.b2(Ha\[Prime] + Ha\.b2)), E^(3) = \
0 (entries 00, 11, 44). The 00 and 11 equations are the Friedmann equations \
of ordinary cosmology, 3Ha\.b2 = \[Kappa] \[Epsilon] + \[CapitalLambda], 2Ha\
\[Prime] + 3Ha\.b2 = \[Minus]\[Kappa] pa + \[CapitalLambda], with the \
four-dimensional Newton constant G4 = G8/V\[UpTee], where V\[UpTee] = \
b0\:2074 Vc is the proper volume of the auxiliary space (Vc its coordinate \
volume; \[Epsilon]8 = \[Epsilon]4/V\[UpTee] for matter confined to, or \
smeared over, ordinary space). The 44 equation then FIXES the stress that \
must hold b constant: \[Kappa] pb = \[CapitalLambda] \[Minus] 3Ha\[Prime] \
\[Minus] 6Ha\.b2 + 12 \[Alpha]_2 Ha\.b2(Ha\[Prime] + Ha\.b2). A field of \
momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["q", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c835f37e-1707-b147-8f19-766b1355cf7d"],
 " along the auxiliary space behaves in ordinary space as a particle of mass \
\[Sqrt](m\.b2 + |",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["q", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e719d1ae-fa21-274e-921a-56a43b07c668"],
 "|\.b2/b0\.b2) (a Kaluza\[Dash]Klein tower when the auxiliary space is a \
torus of coordinate period Lc, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["q", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "adb4b7a5-8bdf-f441-b5e7-fe8af0318265"],
 " = 2\[Pi] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["n", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "653da410-6c64-2a46-947a-00f310dd8d53"],
 "/Lc). The present expansion rate H0 \[TildeTilde] 1.4 \[Times] 10\:207b\
\:2074\.b2 GeV is so small that pair creation today is suppressed by exp(\
\[Minus]2\[Pi]m/H0) (section 14.5)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"265dc1d3-e127-2946-8212-f1d4ea5ae1fc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
modH = Table[Simplify[toH[ECos[[k + 1, c, c]]] /. {Hb -> 0, dHb -> 0}], {k, \
1, 3}, {c, {1, 2, 5}}];
check[\"static auxiliary space (Hb = 0): E^(1) = (3Ha^2, 2Ha' + 3Ha^2, 3Ha' + \
6Ha^2), E^(2) = (0, 0, -12 Ha^2 (Ha' + Ha^2)), E^(3) = 0\",
  Expand[modH - {{3 Ha^2, 2 dHa + 3 Ha^2, 3 dHa + 6 Ha^2}, {0, 0, -12 Ha^2 \
(dHa + Ha^2)}, {0, 0, 0}}] == ConstantArray[0, {3, 3}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[700]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e0685afc-255f-fd47-8be8-1e4746e2ebb2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"static auxiliary space (Hb = 0): E^(1) = (3Ha^2, 2Ha' + 3Ha^2, \
3Ha' + 6Ha^2), E^(2) = (0, 0, -12 Ha^2 (Ha' + Ha^2)), E^(3) = 0\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021916772837944`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[701]=",ExpressionUUID->"15af84af-7d37-8445-b21d-54079d5be4fc"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
14.5 Far future: de Sitter expansion and thermal pair creation\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f0774b78-6009-9441-ae82-7e871c604c39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two de Sitter solutions: (a) eight-dimensional de Sitter a = b = e^{H x0}, \
an exact VACUUM solution of the Einstein\[Dash]Lovelock equations when 21 \
\[Alpha]_1 H\.b2 \[Minus] 420 \[Alpha]_2 H\:2074 + 2520 \[Alpha]_3 H\:2076 = \
\[CapitalLambda] (all E^(k) are then proportional to \[Delta]^\[Mu]_\[Nu]); \
(b) de Sitter expansion of ordinary space over a static auxiliary space, a = \
e^{H x0}, b = b0, with E^(1) = diag(3, 3, 6) H\.b2, E^(2) = diag(0, 0, \
\[Minus]12) H\:2074, E^(3) = 0. In both, a mode of dirac16complex obeys i \
dc/dx0 = (k e^{\[Minus]H x0} \[Sigma]1 + M \[Sigma]3) c with M = m in (a) and \
the Kaluza\[Dash]Klein mass M = \[Sqrt](m\.b2 + |",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["q", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e8ef9748-09b9-fe47-a3a8-46f0f767c3b9"],
 "|\.b2/b0\.b2) in (b). Starting from the adiabatic vacuum at early times, \
the number of created pairs per mode is EXACTLY the Fermi\[Dash]Dirac \
occupation at the Gibbons\[Dash]Hawking temperature H/(2\[Pi]):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1607a598-a252-154a-af30-941776d65f1d"],

Cell["      |\[Beta]|\.b2 = 1/(exp(2\[Pi] M/H) + 1),", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"346976bc-62c0-9f4d-8bdc-f710280c3f5a"],

Cell["\<\
independent of the momentum k. The check integrates the mode equation \
numerically (H = 1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf0ec514-af40-f644-abbd-b004c37b71fe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
dS8H = Table[Simplify[toH[ECos[[k + 1, c, c]]] /. {Ha -> hdS, Hb -> hdS, dHa \
-> 0, dHb -> 0}], {k, 1, 3}, {c, {1, 2, 5}}];
check[\"8D de Sitter: E^(1) = 21 H^2, E^(2) = -420 H^4, E^(3) = 2520 H^6 (all \
diagonal entries)\", dS8H == {{21, 21, 21} hdS^2, {-420, -420, -420} hdS^4, \
{2520, 2520, 2520} hdS^6}]
dS4H = Table[Simplify[toH[ECos[[k + 1, c, c]]] /. {Ha -> hdS, Hb -> 0, dHa -> \
0, dHb -> 0}], {k, 1, 3}, {c, {1, 2, 5}}];
check[\"de Sitter over a static auxiliary space: E^(1) = (3, 3, 6) H^2, E^(2) \
= (0, 0, -12) H^4, E^(3) = 0\", dS4H == {{3, 3, 6} hdS^2, {0, 0, -12} hdS^4, \
{0, 0, 0}}]
dSbeta = Table[bogoliubov[Function[t, Exp[-t] pauli[[1]] + mH pauli[[3]]], \
-Log[2000.], Log[10.^6/mH^2]][[1]], {mH, {0.25, 0.5, 1.}}];
check[\"de Sitter pair creation: |beta|^2 == 1/(Exp[2 Pi M/H] + 1) to 10^-7, \
M/H = 0.25, 0.5, 1\",
  And @@ MapThread[Abs[#1 - 1/(Exp[2 Pi #2] + 1)] < 10^-7 &, {dSbeta, {0.25, \
0.5, 1.}}]]
lzBeta = Table[bogoliubov[Function[t, Sqrt[k2] pauli[[1]] + t pauli[[3]]], \
-150., 150.][[1]], {k2, {0.1, 0.5, 1.}}];
check[\"integrator benchmark (Landau-Zener): |beta|^2 == Exp[-Pi kappa^2] to \
10^-6\", And @@ MapThread[Abs[#1 - Exp[-Pi #2]] < 10^-6 &, {lzBeta, {0.1, \
0.5, 1.}}]]
{\"dS beta2 M/H=0.25\" -> dSbeta[[1]], \"dS beta2 M/H=0.5\" -> dSbeta[[2]], \
\"dS beta2 M/H=1\" -> dSbeta[[3]], \"FD 0.25\" -> N[1/(Exp[2 Pi 0.25] + 1)],
 \"Landau-Zener\" -> lzBeta}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[702]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0688fd6d-a1e1-9b4c-ab6e-78f045cea4f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"8D de Sitter: E^(1) = 21 H^2, E^(2) = -420 H^4, E^(3) = 2520 \
H^6 (all diagonal entries)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191677300123*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[703]=",ExpressionUUID->"2aab6231-15cc-784b-af50-2f27603f265a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"de Sitter over a static auxiliary space: E^(1) = (3, 3, 6) H^2, \
E^(2) = (0, 0, -12) H^4, E^(3) = 0\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191677302128*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[705]=",ExpressionUUID->"7b2761cc-1c0a-724f-aacb-ee3dbb806870"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"de Sitter pair creation: |beta|^2 == 1/(Exp[2 Pi M/H] + 1) to \
10^-7, M/H = 0.25, 0.5, 1\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191677681122*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[707]=",ExpressionUUID->"9730d4cd-d378-0d4b-99c4-6a2dc0c15dec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"integrator benchmark (Landau-Zener): |beta|^2 == Exp[-Pi \
kappa^2] to 10^-6\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191681803873*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[709]=",ExpressionUUID->"687b0d1d-63aa-c349-b567-c66df216091d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"dS beta2 M/H=0.25\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.17210291921007925`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"dS beta2 M/H=0.5\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.0414238844788973`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"dS beta2 M/H=1\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.0018639774636152915`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"FD 0.25\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.1721028986836638`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Landau-Zener\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "0.7304027306401534`", ",", "0.20787954528124913`", ",", 
      "0.043213919275807096`"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191681806473*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[710]=",ExpressionUUID->"1717c3ee-74d0-fe45-988a-6b15c3941923"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
15. The generalized self-coupling of dirac16complex: all nine ranks\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0fea2448-484f-5f40-b79b-40bfb846af06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["About sections 15\[Dash]16. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Section 8 coupled dirac16complex to itself through four contact \
interactions (scalar, pseudoscalar, vector, axial). The 256 products of \
section 8.6 contain nine Lorentz-invariant classes, one for each rank r = 0, \
1, \[Ellipsis], 8 (the number of different Dirac matrices in the product), so \
the most general contact self-coupling without derivatives has nine couplings \
g0, \[Ellipsis], g8. Section 15 builds it, shows that the four couplings of \
section 8 are four of the nine, and computes the 9\[Times]9 Fierz matrix that \
turns every exchange (Fock) term into direct terms. Section 16 writes the \
Kohn\[Dash]Sham theory of the self-coupled field in a gravitational field \
(using the spin connection of section 13) and solves it in the three epochs \
of section 14, including the back-reaction of the Kohn\[Dash]Sham matter on \
the expansion through the Einstein\[Dash]Lovelock equations."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e03b1e4e-e4d3-b744-be60-4917f5d10dcf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["15.1 The nine channels", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3fdfcb3f-6bcc-7e45-8a7c-6cef4c4f01cd"],

Cell["\<\
For a strictly increasing multi-index K = (A1 < A2 < \[Ellipsis] < Ar) of \
rank r let \[CapitalGamma]^K = \[CapitalGamma]17up[A1].\[Ellipsis].\
\[CapitalGamma]17up[Ar] (\[CapitalGamma]^() = ID16) and\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"74d279de-705d-5e4c-b500-b700b31a9bac"],

Cell["\<\
      \[CapitalTheta]^K = i^\[Sigma]r \[CapitalGamma]^K,   \[Sigma]r = (r(r\
\[Minus]1)/2) mod 2,      \[CapitalTheta]_K = \[Eta]K \[CapitalTheta]^K,   \
\[Eta]K = \[Eta]17_A1A1 \[CenterEllipsis] \[Eta]17_ArAr.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40a93a8c-8ca6-134c-a892-7224bdbef954"],

Cell["\<\
Here \[Eta]17 = diag(+1, \[Minus]1, \[Ellipsis], \[Minus]1) is, as everywhere \
in this notebook, simply the squares of the octonion basis (e[0]\.b2 = +1 for \
the time direction x0, e[i]\.b2 = \[Minus]1 for the seven space directions), \
so \[Eta]K = (\[Minus]1)^(number of space indices in K). The phase makes \
every bilinear \[Psi]bar \[CapitalTheta]^K \[Psi] real (\[CapitalGamma]17[0].\
\[CapitalTheta]^K is Hermitian), and \[CapitalTheta]_K.\[CapitalTheta]^K = \
ID16, tr(\[CapitalTheta]_K.\[CapitalTheta]^J) = 16 \[Delta]KJ. The invariant \
of rank r and the general self-coupling are\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b50b70d-0001-1348-9310-99ecc6538455"],

Cell["\<\
      I_r = \[CapitalSigma]_{|K| = r} (\[Psi]bar \[CapitalTheta]_K \[Psi])(\
\[Psi]bar \[CapitalTheta]^K \[Psi]) = \[CapitalSigma]_{|K| = r} \[Eta]K (\
\[Psi]bar \[CapitalTheta]^K \[Psi])\.b2,      L_self = \[Minus](1/2) \
\[CapitalSigma]_{r=0}^{8} g_r I_r.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e17f801-88b7-1340-a2e9-bc1b77deb199"],

Cell["\<\
The ranks have 1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 56, 28, 8, 1 members. The couplings of \
section 8 are g0 = gS, g1 = gV, g7 = \[Minus]gA, g8 = \[Minus]gP (I_8 = \
\[Minus](\[Psi]bar i\[Chi]17 \[Psi])\.b2, I_7 = \[Minus](axial invariant)); \
g2 \[Ellipsis] g6 are new (tensor channels of ranks 2 to 6). Each I_r is \
invariant under every local Lorentz transformation \[Psi] \[RightArrow] S \
\[Psi], \[Psi]bar \[RightArrow] \[Psi]bar S\:207b\.b9, so in a gravitational \
field it is written with the frame matrices exactly as in flat spacetime; \
\[CapitalTheta]^K \[Omega]17 is, up to a phase, \[CapitalTheta] of the \
complementary multi-index (Hodge duality).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70b94fdb-18c2-6e40-8242-ae6787400568"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
mIdx = Flatten[Table[Subsets[Range[0, 7], {r}], {r, 0, 8}], 1];
rk[K_] := Length[K];
\[CapitalTheta]up[K_List] := \[CapitalTheta]up[K] = I^Mod[rk[K] (rk[K] - \
1)/2, 2] (Dot @@ Join[{ID16}, Table[\[CapitalGamma]17up[A], {A, K}]]);
\[Eta]K[K_List] := Product[\[Eta]17[[A + 1, A + 1]], {A, K}];
\[CapitalTheta]dn[K_List] := \[CapitalTheta]dn[K] = \[Eta]K[K] \
\[CapitalTheta]up[K];
check[\"256 multi-indices in 9 ranks with 1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 56, 28, 8, 1 \
members\", Length[mIdx] == 256 && Table[Count[mIdx, K_ /; rk[K] == r], {r, 0, \
8}] == {1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 56, 28, 8, 1}]
check[\"every bilinear psibar Theta^K psi is real: Gamma17[0].Theta^K \
Hermitian for all 256 K\",
  AllTrue[mIdx, ConjugateTranspose[\[CapitalGamma]17[0].\[CapitalTheta]up[#]] \
== \[CapitalGamma]17[0].\[CapitalTheta]up[#] &]]
check[\"Theta_K.Theta^K == ID16 and Tr[Theta_K.Theta^J] == 16 delta_KJ\",
  AllTrue[mIdx, \[CapitalTheta]dn[#].\[CapitalTheta]up[#] == ID16 &] && \
Table[Tr[\[CapitalTheta]dn[K].\[CapitalTheta]up[J]], {K, mIdx}, {J, mIdx}] == \
16 IdentityMatrix[256]]
check[\"Hodge duality: Theta^K.omega17 == (phase) Theta^(complement of K), \
|phase| = 1\",
  AllTrue[mIdx, \
Abs[Tr[ConjugateTranspose[\[CapitalTheta]up[Complement[Range[0, 7], #]]].\
\[CapitalTheta]up[#].\[Omega]17]]/16 == 1 &]]
SeedRandom[1508];
rndSpinor[] := RandomInteger[{-4, 4}, 16] + I RandomInteger[{-4, 4}, 16];
{psR, pbR} = {rndSpinor[], rndSpinor[]};
Ichan[r_, pb_, ps_] := Sum[\[Eta]K[K] (pb.\[CapitalTheta]up[K].ps)^2, {K, \
Select[mIdx, rk[#] == r &]}];
bilR[o_] := pbR.o.psR;
check[\"the couplings of section 8 are four of the nine: I_0 == (psibar \
psi)^2, I_1 == (psibar Gamma^A psi)(psibar Gamma_A psi), I_8 == -(psibar i \
chi17 psi)^2, I_7 == -(axial invariant)\",
  Ichan[0, pbR, psR] == bilR[ID16]^2 && Ichan[1, pbR, psR] == Sum[bilR[\
\[CapitalGamma]17up[A]] bilR[\[CapitalGamma]17[A]], {A, 0, 7}] &&
  Ichan[8, pbR, psR] == -bilR[I \[Chi]17]^2 && Ichan[7, pbR, psR] == \
-Sum[bilR[\[CapitalGamma]17up[A].\[Chi]17] \
bilR[\[CapitalGamma]17[A].\[Chi]17], {A, 0, 7}]]
wLL = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {8, 8}]; wLL = wLL - Transpose[wLL];
sLL = MatrixExp[0.3 Sum[wLL[[A + 1, B + 1]] (\[CapitalGamma]17up[A].\
\[CapitalGamma]17up[B] - \[CapitalGamma]17up[B].\[CapitalGamma]17up[A])/4, \
{A, 0, 7}, {B, 0, 7}]/2];
sLLi = Inverse[sLL];
check[\"local Lorentz invariance: I_r(S psi, psibar S^-1) == I_r(psi, psibar) \
for r = 0..8 (random finite Lorentz transformation), and S^-1 == \
Gamma17[0].S^dagger.Gamma17[0]\",
  And @@ Table[Abs[Ichan[r, pbR.sLLi, sLL.psR] - Ichan[r, pbR, psR]] < 10^-8 \
Abs[Ichan[r, pbR, psR]] + 10^-8, {r, 0, 8}] &&
  Norm[sLLi - \
\[CapitalGamma]17[0].ConjugateTranspose[sLL].\[CapitalGamma]17[0]] < 10^-10]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[711]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c18d473b-1008-de40-8e96-49a342636447"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"256 multi-indices in 9 ranks with 1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 56, 28, 8, \
1 members\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021916818249035`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[716]=",ExpressionUUID->"c3e5335b-7291-e148-9314-32738894adc1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"every bilinear psibar Theta^K psi is real: Gamma17[0].Theta^K \
Hermitian for all 256 K\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191681854515*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[717]=",ExpressionUUID->"83e92151-9601-6942-bfed-8764c024f964"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Theta_K.Theta^K == ID16 and Tr[Theta_K.Theta^J] == 16 \
delta_KJ\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021916843398914`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[718]=",ExpressionUUID->"f9620887-9151-6f4e-9b97-ad0d5ccc4079"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Hodge duality: Theta^K.omega17 == (phase) Theta^(complement of \
K), |phase| = 1\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191684357477*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[719]=",ExpressionUUID->"9d19f469-d374-9c40-b4df-ff3a553e5f9d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the couplings of section 8 are four of the nine: I_0 == (psibar \
psi)^2, I_1 == (psibar Gamma^A psi)(psibar Gamma_A psi), I_8 == -(psibar i \
chi17 psi)^2, I_7 == -(axial invariant)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191684366066*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[725]=",ExpressionUUID->"5088e0cd-2293-7e4c-83ec-9821e9336c3b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"local Lorentz invariance: I_r(S psi, psibar S^-1) == I_r(psi, \
psibar) for r = 0..8 (random finite Lorentz transformation), and S^-1 == \
Gamma17[0].S^dagger.Gamma17[0]\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021916843772507`*^9},
