Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
22.2 Radion decay, the moduli problem and the Kaluza\[Dash]Klein channels\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fad17fa3-3d7c-8041-961a-bdf78aa38ad0"],

Cell["\<\
In physical units (M8 = 10 TeV, reduced M_Pl = 2.435 \[Times] 10\.b9\:2078 \
GeV, V\[UpTee] = M_Pl\.b2/M8\:2076) the radion couples to the brane fields \
through L = (\[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl)) T^\[Mu]_\[Mu] (section 20.3). For a \
fermion of mass m_f (N_c colours) and, through the trace anomaly \
T^\[Mu]_\[Mu] \[Superset] \[Minus](b_QCD \[Alpha]_s/(8\[Pi])) G^a_\[Mu]\[Nu] \
G^a\[Mu]\[Nu] (b_QCD = 11 \[Minus] 2n_f/3, the first coefficient of the QCD \
beta function), for two gluons:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6884a255-9fb2-3140-b58c-77d3013e8d97"],

Cell["\<\
      \[CapitalGamma](\[Phi] \[RightArrow] f f\:0304) = N_c m_f\.b2 m_r (1 \
\[Minus] 4m_f\.b2/m_r\.b2)^(3/2)/(24\[Pi] M_Pl\.b2),   \[CapitalGamma](\[Phi] \
\[RightArrow] gg) = b_QCD\.b2 \[Alpha]_s\.b2 m_r\.b3/(96\[Pi]\.b3 M_Pl\.b2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"926395d3-2e9a-ee44-af70-4c8a94d82a32"],

Cell["\<\
For m_r = 10 GeV (b, c, \[Tau], \[Mu] pairs and gluons, \[Alpha]_s = 0.18, \
n_f = 5) the brane channels give \[CapitalGamma]_brane \[TildeTilde] 4.6 \
\[Times] 10\:207b\.b3\:2077 GeV, a lifetime of 1.4 \[Times] 10\.b9\.b2 s, and \
would reheat the brane only to T_RH = [\[CapitalGamma]_brane M_Pl/\[Sqrt](\
\[Pi]\.b2 g*/90)]^(1/2) \[TildeTilde] 10\:207b\:2079 GeV (g* = 10.75), far \
below the 4 MeV that nucleosynthesis needs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0f5bc99-7ac5-1449-af3f-3f77df070724"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Decay into the bulk. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The radion also couples to every Kaluza\[Dash]Klein mode of the bulk \
fields. A mode of dirac16complex with Kaluza\[Dash]Klein momentum \[Mu]_n = 2\
\[Pi]|n|/",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] (n in Z\:2074, ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] = V\[UpTee]^(1/4) the size of the auxiliary torus) has, in the \
four-dimensional Einstein frame (h = e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]) g_E), the mass M_E \
= e^(\[Minus]2\[Beta]) (m\.b2 + \[Mu]_n\.b2 e^(\[Minus]2\[Beta]))^(1/2); it \
therefore couples to \[Phi] = \[Sqrt]12 M_Pl \[Beta] with g_n = (2M_n + \
\[Mu]_n\.b2/M_n)/(\[Sqrt]12 M_Pl), M_n = (m\.b2 + \[Mu]_n\.b2)^(1/2). For m \
\[LessLess] \[Mu]_n each Kaluza\[Dash]Klein level (four brane Dirac spinors) \
gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ed6c55d6-fe1d-c942-98f4-84954b020050"],

Cell["\<\
      \[CapitalGamma]_n = 4 g_n\.b2 m_r (1 \[Minus] \
4M_n\.b2/m_r\.b2)^(3/2)/(8\[Pi]) = 3 \[Mu]_n\.b2 m_r (1 \[Minus] \
4\[Mu]_n\.b2/m_r\.b2)^(3/2)/(8\[Pi] M_Pl\.b2),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fcbd539f-2fc0-b240-a0e7-f294c7225a2f"],

Cell["\<\
and the sum over the 1.17 \[Times] 10\.b9\.b3 momenta with 2\[Mu]_n < m_r, \
done shell by shell with the number r_4(k) = 8\[Sigma](k) \[Minus] \
32\[Sigma](k/4) of lattice vectors with |n|\.b2 = k (\[Sigma] the divisor \
sum, \[Sigma](k/4) = 0 unless 4 divides k), agrees with its continuum limit\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85c27a21-73aa-8345-9199-9c65b2060f85"],

Cell["\<\
      \[CapitalGamma]_bulk = \[CapitalSigma]_n \[CapitalGamma]_n \
\[TildeTilde] (3 m_r/(8\[Pi] M_Pl\.b2)) (V\[UpTee]/(8\[Pi]\.b2)) \
(m_r/2)\:2076 B(3, 5/2)/2 \[TildeTilde] 6.0 \[Times] 10\:207b\.b2\:2074 GeV   \
(lifetime 0.11 s):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9e54c49-8103-4341-87ca-b41602112313"],

Cell["\<\
thirteen orders of magnitude faster than the brane channels (the \
Kaluza\[Dash]Klein gravitons add channels of the same strength; for m > m_r/2 \
the dirac16complex channels close). The radion decays into the BULK: its \
energy goes to Kaluza\[Dash]Klein modes, which return it to the brane only \
through couplings suppressed by the volume (a Kaluza\[Dash]Klein graviton of \
mass M decays into brane fields at a rate of order M\.b3/M_Pl\.b2). This is \
the cosmological moduli problem of the minimal model in the form it takes \
with large extra dimensions. The minimal model therefore needs the radion and \
bulk energy left at the end of regime I to be removed before nucleosynthesis \
(for example by a later period of inflation on the brane, not part of the \
model); sections 22.3\[Dash]22.4 start after such a reheating, below the \
normalcy temperature T* \[TildeTilde] (M8\:2076/M_Pl)^(1/5) \[TildeTilde] 13 \
GeV.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fcba62d-702f-1b4b-805d-5e09bff1f2c8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rIIMPl = 2.435 10^18; rIIM8 = 10.^4; rIIVp = rIIMPl^2/rIIM8^6; rIIhbar = \
6.582119569 10^-25;
rIIgff[mphi_, mf_, nc_] := If[4 mf^2 < mphi^2, nc mf^2 mphi (1 - 4 \
mf^2/mphi^2)^(3/2)/(24 Pi rIIMPl^2), 0];
rIIggg[mphi_, as_, nf_] := (11 - 2 nf/3)^2 as^2 mphi^3/(96 Pi^3 rIIMPl^2);
rIIgam = rIIgff[10., 4.183, 3] + rIIgff[10., 1.273, 3] + rIIgff[10., 1.77693, \
1] + rIIgff[10., 0.1056583755, 1] + rIIggg[10., 0.18, 5];
rIITRH = Sqrt[rIIgam rIIMPl/Sqrt[Pi^2 10.75/90]];
rIINKK = rIIVp (Pi^2/2) (10./2)^4/(2 Pi)^4;
check[\"through brane fields alone a 10 GeV radion would decay far too late: \
T_RH < 10^-6 GeV (nucleosynthesis needs 4 10^-3 GeV); 10^13 Kaluza-Klein \
channels below m_r/2\",
  rIITRH < 10^-6 && 10^13 < rIINKK < 2 10^13]
rIIkmax = Floor[(10. rIIVp^(1/4)/(4 Pi))^2];                        (* |n|^2 \
= k <= kmax  <=>  2 mu_n < m_r *)
rIIsig = DivisorSigma[1, Range[rIIkmax]];
rIIr4 = 8 rIIsig; rIIr4[[4 ;; ;; 4]] -= 32 rIIsig[[1 ;; Floor[rIIkmax/4]]];   \
    (* r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) - 32 sigma(k/4) *)
rIImuK = 2 Pi Sqrt[N[Range[rIIkmax]]]/rIIVp^(1/4);
rIIgBulk = 3 10./(8 Pi rIIMPl^2) Total[rIIr4 rIImuK^2 (1 - 4 \
rIImuK^2/100.)^(3/2)];
rIIgBulkC = 3 10./(8 Pi rIIMPl^2) rIIVp/(8 Pi^2) 5.^6 Beta[3, 5/2]/2;
check[\"the number of lattice vectors with |n|^2 = k is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) - \
32 sigma(k/4) (direct count for k <= 60)\",
  With[{nn = Total[Tuples[Range[-8, 8], 4]^2, {2}]}, Table[Count[nn, kk], \
{kk, 60}]] == rIIr4[[1 ;; 60]]]
check[\"the radion decays into the bulk: the lattice sum over the \
Kaluza-Klein modes of dirac16complex (m << m_r/2) equals its continuum limit \
to 10^-6, the number of momenta to 10^-5, and Gamma_bulk/Gamma_brane > 10^12\",
  Abs[rIIgBulk/rIIgBulkC - 1] < 10^-6 && Abs[Total[rIIr4]/rIINKK - 1] < 10^-5 \
&& rIIgBulk/rIIgam > 10^12]
{\"Gamma (GeV), lifetime (s), T_RH (GeV)\" -> {rIIgam, rIIhbar/rIIgam, \
rIITRH}, \"Kaluza-Klein momenta below m_r/2\" -> rIINKK,
 \"radion into bulk dirac16complex pairs (m << m_r/2): Gamma_bulk lattice, \
continuum (GeV), lifetime (s), Gamma_bulk/Gamma_brane\" -> {rIIgBulk, \
rIIgBulkC, rIIhbar/rIIgBulk, rIIgBulk/rIIgam},
 \"V_perp (GeV^-4), l_perp (m), 2 Pi/l_perp (GeV)\" -> {rIIVp, rIIVp^(1/4) \
1.973269804 10^-16, 2 Pi/rIIVp^(1/4)}, \"normalcy temperature \
(M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) (GeV)\" -> (rIIM8^6/rIIMPl)^(1/5)}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1036]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ee1169ff-dcea-824c-80e8-cd02ca2894f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"through brane fields alone a 10 GeV radion would decay far too \
late: T_RH < 10^-6 GeV (nucleosynthesis needs 4 10^-3 GeV); 10^13 \
Kaluza-Klein channels below m_r/2\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
