Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24.6 Verdict", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b55f888a-dccc-b54c-b330-dd947b9b3c2c"],

Cell["\<\
The table collects the findings. dirac16complex has every property that the \
solutions of sections 21\[Dash]23 and the observations demand of dark matter \
\[LongDash] it is cold, dark, collisionless, and enters the late-universe \
solution exactly as \[CapitalOmega]_c \[LongDash] provided the auxiliary \
space is stabilized and the Yukawa portal is very weak or absent. The minimal \
model does not, however, produce the observed abundance: its primordial gas \
and its radion make far too much (which the dilution required by the moduli \
problem must remove), and after that dilution its portals with couplings of \
natural size make far too little \[LongDash] the Higgs portal would need c_P \
\[TildeTilde] 150. The origin of the abundance is therefore OPEN. As dark \
energy dirac16complex fails: as matter it never has w < \[Minus]0.06 in a \
stable state, and as vacuum energy or condensate it is only one more \
contribution to \[CapitalLambda]4, with w = \[Minus]1 exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05811e18-ef9a-d549-be84-b043cda78440"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Grid[{{\"claim\", \"status\", \"basis\"},
  {\"dirac16complex behaves as cold matter (w = 0) and can be Omega_c of the \
late-universe solution\", \"DERIVED\", \"sections 20.2, 22.1, 22.4, 24.2\"},
  {Row[{\"its effect on the radion is negligible (delta beta = \", \
ScientificForm[dkDbeta, 2], \")\"}], \"DERIVED\", \"sections 20.3, 24.2\"},
  {\"as dark matter it needs the stabilizing potential (otherwise \
decompactification)\", \"DERIVED\", \"section 21.3\"},
  {Row[{\"dark: sigma_SI = \", ScientificForm[dkSigSI[1, 40.], 2], \" cm^2 << \
LZ; collisionless: sigma/m = \", ScientificForm[dkSigM[1, 1.], 2], \" \
cm^2/g\"}], \"ESTIMATE\", \"volume dilution, section 24.3\"},
  {Row[{\"stable over the age of the universe if m < \", NumberForm[1000 \
dkMmax, 2], \" MeV c_y^(-2/3) (absolutely stable without the Yukawa \
portal)\"}], \"ESTIMATE\", \"section 24.3\"},
  {Row[{\"mass window: m > 5.7 keV (Lyman-alpha), > \", NumberForm[dkPauli, \
2], \" keV (Pauli, g = 16)\"}], \"data\", \"section 24.1\"},
  {Row[{\"primordial gas and radion decay overproduce dirac16complex (O = \", \
ScientificForm[dkOver[1.], 2], \" T_RH/GeV; brane share \", \
ScientificForm[rIIgam/rIIgBulk, 2], \")\"}], \"DERIVED from the solutions; \
ESTIMATE for O\", \"sections 21.3, 22.1, 22.2, 24.4\"},
  {Row[{\"Yukawa portal: the Kaluza-Klein tower is overproduced unless c_y < \
\", ScientificForm[dkCyTow, 2]}], \"ESTIMATE\", \"section 24.4\"},
  {Row[{\"Higgs portal: the observed abundance needs c_P = \", \
NumberForm[dkCpNeed[mHb/dkTstar], 3], \" (T_RH = T*)\"}], \"ESTIMATE\", \
\"section 24.4\"},
  {\"observed abundance m Y = 4.37 10^-10 GeV produced by the minimal model \
with natural couplings\", \"OPEN (not produced)\", \"section 24.4\"},
  {\"dirac16complex matter as dark energy\", \"excluded (DERIVED: w >= -0.06; \
p < 0 only where uniform matter is unstable or metastable)\", \"sections 8.7, \
24.5\"},
  {Row[{\"dirac16complex vacuum energy or condensate as dark energy\", \" \
(Casimir: \", ScientificForm[16 dkC0/dkLp^4/dkRhoL, 2], \" rho_Lambda)\"}], \
\"not an explanation (DERIVED: a contribution to Lambda4 with w = -1)\", \
\"section 24.5\"},
  {\"evolving dark energy (DESI DR2: 2.8 to 4.2 sigma)\", \"in tension with \
the model (w = -1 exactly)\", \"section 24.5\"}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> \
Left]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1182]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d8474267-518a-a34e-91cb-b7bc6c48b522"],

