Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25. The auxiliary torus and the world brane: definitions and worked examples\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"17f1d573-038c-f64f-b67e-d4fca0207093"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["About section 25. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Section 25 was appended on 28 October 2026. The notebook as it was before \
(sections 0\[Dash]24, with the summary of all checks numbered 25; evaluated) \
is kept in the workspace as backups/7+1_2026-10-28_before_torus_brane.nb \
(excluded from the repository by .gitignore). Sections 14 and 17\[Dash]24 use \
two geometric objects, the AUXILIARY TORUS and the WORLD BRANE. This section \
defines both precisely and checks every part of the definitions with worked \
examples; nothing in sections 0\[Dash]24 is changed. Coordinates as \
everywhere: X = {x0, \[Ellipsis], x7}, x0 is time (the direction of the \
octonion unit e[0] = 1), x1, x2, x3 ordinary space, y = (x4, x5, x6, x7) the \
four auxiliary space-like coordinates. \[Eta]17 = diag(+1, \[Minus]1, \
\[Ellipsis], \[Minus]1) is simply the squares of the octonion basis (e0\.b2 = \
+1, e_i\.b2 = \[Minus]1); xAct declares the spacetime with the signature list \
{7, 1, 0}: seven space-like dimensions and one time-like dimension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f22f15b5-3d1c-cc4f-a2d9-5c56312f7358"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The auxiliary torus. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The four auxiliary coordinates are periodic: x_k \[TildeEqual] x_k + Lc n_k \
(k = 4 \[Ellipsis] 7, n_k \[Element] \:2124, Lc > 0 the coordinate period). \
The auxiliary space is therefore the four-dimensional torus T\:2074 = \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]\:2074/(Lc \:2124)\:2074 \[LongDash] a compact, flat \
space without boundary, whose fundamental domain is the hypercube [0, Lc)\
\:2074 (equivalently [\[Minus]Lc/2, Lc/2)\:2074) with opposite faces \
identified \[LongDash] and the spacetime of the model, the BULK, is \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR] (time x0) \[Times] \[DoubleStruckCapitalR]\.b3 \
(ordinary space x1, x2, x3) \[Times] T\:2074. The SIZE b of the torus is \
defined by b\:2078 = det(\[Minus]g_kl) (k, l = 4 \[Ellipsis] 7), so that the \
proper volume element of the torus is b\:2074 d\:2074y. For every metric of \
sections 11\[Dash]24, \[Minus]g_kl = b\.b2 \[Delta]_kl: each of the four \
circles has the proper circumference b\[CenterDot]Lc, and the proper volume \
is V\[UpTee] = b\:2074 Lc\:2074; today b = b0 and ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] = V\[UpTee]^(1/4) = b0\[CenterDot]Lc. Only the product b\
\[CenterDot]Lc is physical (section 25.1)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"843ecd97-e27c-9e4d-bc03-038742aa9575"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The world brane. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "W = {x4 = x5 = x6 = x7 = 0} is the 3+1-dimensional submanifold of the bulk \
through the point y = 0 of the torus. It is spanned by the time x0 and \
ordinary space x1, x2, x3; its embedding is X(x) = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, \
0), and its metric is the induced metric h_\[Mu]\[Nu] = g_AB \
\[PartialD]_\[Mu]X^A \[PartialD]_\[Nu]X^B = g_\[Mu]\[Nu](x, y = 0) (\[Mu], \
\[Nu] = 0 \[Ellipsis] 3). The Standard Model lives on W; gravity and \
dirac16complex live in the bulk and meet the Standard Model at W. In the \
counting of xAct the bulk has the signature list {7, 1, 0} and W the list {3, \
1, 0}; the flat metric diag(+1, \[Minus]1, \[Minus]1, \[Minus]1) of W is the \
squares of the basis e[0] = 1, e[1], e[2], e[3] of the quaternion subalgebra \
(section 17). In this model W is a fixed submanifold (its position is not a \
dynamical field)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d12af01f-b305-1645-a277-cb48dd4a4198"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["25.1 The auxiliary torus: size, volume and symmetries", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b1fd43b6-7ba8-9a44-9fcd-6377500381bf"],

Cell["\<\
For the cosmological metric of section 11.2 the size is b(x0), and the proper \
volume of the fundamental domain is b\:2074 Lc\:2074. The change of \
coordinates y = \[Lambda] y\[Prime] describes the SAME torus with the period \
Lc/\[Lambda] and the size \[Lambda] b, so only b\[CenterDot]Lc (and \
V\[UpTee]) can be measured. The isometries of the torus are the translations \
y \[RightArrow] y + c and the 384 = 2\:2074\[CenterDot]4! signed permutations \
of the four axes (the symmetries of the lattice Lc \:2124\:2074; an \
orthogonal matrix with integer entries is a signed permutation). The signed \
permutations fix the point y = 0, and with it the world brane. They permute \
the vectors n \[Element] \:2124\:2074 of each shell |n|\.b2 = k; vectors with \
the same multiset of |n_i| form one orbit: the shell k = 4 consists of the 8 \
vectors \[PlusMinus]2e_i and the 16 vectors (\[PlusMinus]1, \[PlusMinus]1, \
\[PlusMinus]1, \[PlusMinus]1), the shell k = 9 of the 8 vectors \
\[PlusMinus]3e_i and the 96 arrangements of (\[PlusMinus]2, \[PlusMinus]2, \
\[PlusMinus]1, 0).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69361025-7ad6-cc4e-a60c-78945265b361"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
tbG4 = Table[gCos[[k, l]], {k, 5, 8}, {l, 5, 8}]; tbDy = {tbd4, tbd5, tbd6, \
tbd7};
check[\"auxiliary torus: for the cosmological metric det(-g_kl) == b^8 (k, l \
= 4..7), and the proper volume of the fundamental domain [0, Lc)^4, \
Integrate[Sqrt[det(-g_kl)], {y, 0, Lc}^4], is b^4 Lc^4 = V_perp\",
  Simplify[Det[-tbG4] - b4[x0]^8] === 0 &&
  Simplify[Integrate[Sqrt[Det[-tbG4]], {x4, 0, tbLc}, {x5, 0, tbLc}, {x6, 0, \
tbLc}, {x7, 0, tbLc}] - b4[x0]^4 tbLc^4, b4[x0] > 0 && tbLc > 0] === 0]
check[\"only the product b Lc of the auxiliary torus is physical: y = lambda \
y' maps the torus of period Lc and size b to the one of period Lc/lambda and \
size lambda b; the line element b^2 dy.dy, the proper period b Lc and V_perp \
= b^4 Lc^4 are unchanged\",
  Simplify[tbB^2 (tbLam tbDy).(tbLam tbDy) - (tbLam tbB)^2 tbDy.tbDy] === 0 \
&& Simplify[(tbLc/tbLam) (tbLam tbB) - tbLc tbB] === 0 &&
  Simplify[(tbLc/tbLam)^4 (tbLam tbB)^4 - tbLc^4 tbB^4] === 0]
tbSP = Flatten[Table[DiagonalMatrix[s].IdentityMatrix[4][[p]], {p, \
Permutations[Range[4]]}, {s, Tuples[{1, -1}, 4]}], 1];
tbShell[k_] := Select[Tuples[Range[-3, 3], 4], #.# == k &];
tbOrbits[k_] := GatherBy[tbShell[k], Sort[Abs[#]] &];
tbOrbitQ[k_] := AllTrue[tbOrbits[k], Function[cl, Sort[Union[(#.First[cl]) & \
/@ tbSP]] == Sort[cl]]];
check[\"symmetries of the auxiliary torus that fix y = 0 (and the brane): the \
384 = 2^4 4! signed permutation matrices are distinct orthogonal integer \
matrices (they map Z^4 onto itself and preserve |n|^2); the shells |n|^2 = 1, \
2, 3, 4, 9 split into orbits of sizes {8}, {24}, {32}, {8, 16}, {8, 96}\",
  Length[tbSP] == 384 && Length[Union[tbSP]] == 384 && AllTrue[tbSP, \
#.Transpose[#] == IdentityMatrix[4] &] &&
  AllTrue[{1, 2, 3, 4, 9}, tbOrbitQ] && (Sort[Length /@ tbOrbits[#]] & /@ {1, \
2, 3, 4, 9}) == {{8}, {24}, {32}, {8, 16}, {8, 96}}]
{\"orbit sizes of the shells k = 1..12\" -> Table[Sort[Length /@ \
tbOrbits[k]], {k, 1, 12}]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1183]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3c60b65d-892b-fb40-bc89-60cbda1b52f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"auxiliary torus: for the cosmological metric det(-g_kl) == b^8 \
(k, l = 4..7), and the proper volume of the fundamental domain [0, Lc)^4, \
Integrate[Sqrt[det(-g_kl)], {y, 0, Lc}^4], is b^4 Lc^4 = V_perp\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191841864092*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1184]=",ExpressionUUID->"98eb6aa5-13a5-d94b-9c80-eb6680e7ae35"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"only the product b Lc of the auxiliary torus is physical: y = \
lambda y' maps the torus of period Lc and size b to the one of period \
Lc/lambda and size lambda b; the line element b^2 dy.dy, the proper period b \
Lc and V_perp = b^4 Lc^4 are unchanged\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191841864092*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1185]=",ExpressionUUID->"7f528b86-14b2-1748-a301-920e47ea6928"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"symmetries of the auxiliary torus that fix y = 0 (and the \
brane): the 384 = 2^4 4! signed permutation matrices are distinct orthogonal \
integer matrices (they map Z^4 onto itself and preserve |n|^2); the shells \
|n|^2 = 1, 2, 3, 4, 9 split into orbits of sizes {8}, {24}, {32}, {8, 16}, \
{8, 96}\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191841879837*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1190]=",ExpressionUUID->"85fa863e-5bbc-d047-a46a-5ded400638ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"orbit sizes of the shells k = 1..12\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "8", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "24", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "32", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"8", ",", "16"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "48", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "96", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "64", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "24", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"8", ",", "96"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"48", ",", "96"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", "96", "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"32", ",", "64"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00219184190217*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1191]=",ExpressionUUID->"46a2bbda-2e78-d449-8e08-f4a4750b8613"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.2 Fields on the torus: Fourier modes, the Laplacian and Kaluza\[Dash]Klein \
masses\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6cabdae8-8fa5-8a41-bb67-3af3952fc3d7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A field on the torus is periodic in each y_k and is therefore a Fourier \
series in the modes \[Phi]_n(y) = e^{i q_n\[CenterDot]y}/\[Sqrt]V\[UpTee], \
q_n = 2\[Pi] n/Lc, n \[Element] \:2124\:2074 (q_n is the wave vector in the \
coordinate y; the physical momentum along the torus is q_n/b). The modes are \
orthonormal for the proper volume element, \[Integral] b\:2074 d\:2074y \
\[Phi]_n* \[Phi]_m = \[Delta]_nm, and complete (Parseval: \[Integral] b\:2074 \
d\:2074y |f|\.b2 = \[CapitalSigma]_n |c_n|\.b2, c_n = \[Integral] b\:2074 d\
\:2074y \[Phi]_n* f). They are eigenfunctions of the Laplacian of the torus, \
\[Minus]b\:207b\.b2 \[CapitalSigma]_k \[PartialD]\.b2\[Phi]_n/\[PartialD]y_k\
\.b2 = (|q_n|\.b2/b\.b2) \[Phi]_n. A bulk field \[CapitalPhi] = \[Chi](x) \
\[Phi]_n(y) of mass m is, for a static torus (b = b0), a particle of mass M_n \
= (m\.b2 + \[Mu]_n\.b2)^(1/2) in ordinary spacetime, with the \
Kaluza\[Dash]Klein mass \[Mu]_n = |q_n|/b0 = 2\[Pi]|n|/",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] (for dirac16complex the same tower, four brane Dirac fermions per \
n: section 18.1)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"427561cd-5326-4644-b29c-4df6aecb213c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
tbY = {x4, x5, x6, x7}; tbV = tbB^4 tbLc^4;
tbQ[n_] := 2 Pi n/tbLc;
tbPhi[n_] := Exp[I tbQ[n].tbY]/Sqrt[tbV]; tbPhiC[n_] := Exp[-I \
tbQ[n].tbY]/Sqrt[tbV];
tbInt[f_] := Simplify[Integrate[tbB^4 f, {x4, 0, tbLc}, {x5, 0, tbLc}, {x6, \
0, tbLc}, {x7, 0, tbLc}], tbLc > 0 && tbB > 0];
check[\"Fourier modes of the auxiliary torus: phi_n = Exp[I \
q_n.y]/Sqrt[V_perp] with q_n = 2 Pi n/Lc (n in Z^4) are orthonormal for the \
proper volume element b^4 d^4y (exact integrals: n = m = (1, 0, -2, 3); n = \
(1, 0, -2, 3), m = (1, 1, -2, 3); n = 0, m = (0, 2, 0, 0))\",
  {tbInt[tbPhiC[{1, 0, -2, 3}] tbPhi[{1, 0, -2, 3}]], tbInt[tbPhiC[{1, 0, -2, \
3}] tbPhi[{1, 1, -2, 3}]], tbInt[tbPhiC[{0, 0, 0, 0}] tbPhi[{0, 2, 0, 0}]]} \
== {1, 0, 0}]
tbF = Product[Cos[Pi tbY[[k]]/tbLc]^2, {k, 4}];
tbW1[j_] := If[j == 0, 1/2, 1/4];
tbCoef[n_] := Sqrt[tbV] Times @@ (tbW1 /@ n);
check[\"Parseval on the auxiliary torus: f(y) = Prod_k cos^2(Pi y_k/Lc) = \
Prod_k (1/2 + (1/4) e^(2 Pi I y_k/Lc) + (1/4) e^(-2 Pi I y_k/Lc)) has the 81 \
non-zero coefficients c_n = Sqrt[V_perp] Prod_k w(n_k), w(0) = 1/2, w(+-1) = \
1/4 (three of them checked by integration), and Sum_n |c_n|^2 == Int b^4 d^4y \
f^2 == (3/8)^4 V_perp\",
  AllTrue[{{0, 0, 0, 0}, {1, 0, -1, 0}, {1, 1, 1, -1}}, \
Simplify[tbInt[tbPhiC[#] tbF] - tbCoef[#], tbLc > 0 && tbB > 0] === 0 &] &&
  Simplify[Total[tbCoef[#]^2 & /@ Tuples[{-1, 0, 1}, 4]] - tbInt[tbF^2], tbLc \
> 0 && tbB > 0] === 0 && Simplify[tbInt[tbF^2] - (3/8)^4 tbV, tbLc > 0 && tbB \
> 0] === 0]
check[\"the Laplacian of the auxiliary torus: -(1/b^2) Sum_k d^2 phi_n/dy_k^2 \
== (|q_n|^2/b^2) phi_n (n = (2, -1, 0, 3))\",
  Simplify[-Sum[D[tbPhi[{2, -1, 0, 3}], tbY[[k]], tbY[[k]]], {k, 4}]/tbB^2 - \
(tbQ[{2, -1, 0, 3}].tbQ[{2, -1, 0, 3}]/tbB^2) tbPhi[{2, -1, 0, 3}]] === 0]
tbGS = DiagonalMatrix[{1, -1, -1, -1, -tbB^2, -tbB^2, -tbB^2, -tbB^2}];       \
   (* a static torus of size b0 = tbB *)
tbBox[f_] := With[{gi = Inverse[tbGS], sg = Sqrt[-Det[tbGS]]}, Sum[D[sg \
gi[[A, A]] D[f, X[[A]]], X[[A]]], {A, 8}]/sg];
tbWave = Exp[-I tbE x0 + I {tbk1, tbk2, tbk3}.{x1, x2, x3} + I tbQ[{1, -2, 0, \
2}].tbY];
check[\"scalar Kaluza-Klein masses: for the static metric diag(1, -1, -1, -1, \
-b0^2, ..., -b0^2) the Klein-Gordon operator Box + m^2 (Box f = |g|^(-1/2) \
d_A(|g|^(1/2) g^AB d_B f)) on Exp[-I E x0 + I k.x + I q.y] gives (-E^2 + \
|k|^2 + |q|^2/b0^2 + m^2) times the wave: in ordinary spacetime a particle of \
mass Sqrt[m^2 + |q|^2/b0^2]\",
  Simplify[(tbBox[tbWave] + tbM^2 tbWave)/tbWave - (-tbE^2 + tbk1^2 + tbk2^2 \
+ tbk3^2 + tbQ[{1, -2, 0, 2}].tbQ[{1, -2, 0, 2}]/tbB^2 + tbM^2)] === 0]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1192]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d4d5a021-8a20-df4d-98f7-c4d26ce911fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Fourier modes of the auxiliary torus: phi_n = Exp[I \
q_n.y]/Sqrt[V_perp] with q_n = 2 Pi n/Lc (n in Z^4) are orthonormal for the \
proper volume element b^4 d^4y (exact integrals: n = m = (1, 0, -2, 3); n = \
(1, 0, -2, 3), m = (1, 1, -2, 3); n = 0, m = (0, 2, 0, 0))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918426313*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1196]=",ExpressionUUID->"0d58aa52-364a-034c-b9c7-6b78cf448d4a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Parseval on the auxiliary torus: f(y) = Prod_k cos^2(Pi y_k/Lc) \
= Prod_k (1/2 + (1/4) e^(2 Pi I y_k/Lc) + (1/4) e^(-2 Pi I y_k/Lc)) has the \
81 non-zero coefficients c_n = Sqrt[V_perp] Prod_k w(n_k), w(0) = 1/2, w(+-1) \
= 1/4 (three of them checked by integration), and Sum_n |c_n|^2 == Int b^4 \
d^4y f^2 == (3/8)^4 V_perp\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918494330425`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1200]=",ExpressionUUID->"0d76d6b3-aa2d-9242-997d-4c37f1072bdb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the Laplacian of the auxiliary torus: -(1/b^2) Sum_k d^2 \
phi_n/dy_k^2 == (|q_n|^2/b^2) phi_n (n = (2, -1, 0, 3))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191849435549*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1201]=",ExpressionUUID->"70a9ef61-ffe7-b248-8319-e6e560e8fd9e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"scalar Kaluza-Klein masses: for the static metric diag(1, -1, \
-1, -1, -b0^2, ..., -b0^2) the Klein-Gordon operator Box + m^2 (Box f = \
|g|^(-1/2) d_A(|g|^(1/2) g^AB d_B f)) on Exp[-I E x0 + I k.x + I q.y] gives \
(-E^2 + |k|^2 + |q|^2/b0^2 + m^2) times the wave: in ordinary spacetime a \
particle of mass Sqrt[m^2 + |q|^2/b0^2]\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191849446556*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1205]=",ExpressionUUID->"002267f3-6059-cd48-81e6-8c5bd0cc1d06"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.3 Counting the levels: Jacobi\[CloseCurlyQuote]s r_4(k), Weyl\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law, and the torus today\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9dcb2bb9-6df9-ef4c-be43-1bf8291a140f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Kaluza\[Dash]Klein masses depend on k = |n|\.b2 only. The number of n \
\[Element] \:2124\:2074 with |n|\.b2 = k is Jacobi\[CloseCurlyQuote]s r_4(k) \
= 8\[Sigma](k) \[Minus] 32\[Sigma](k/4) (\[Sigma] the divisor sum, \
\[Sigma](k/4) = 0 unless 4 divides k; section 22.2 computes it as rIIr4 for k \
\[LessEqual] rIIkmax). The number N(R) of n with |n| \[LessEqual] R \
approaches the volume \[Pi]\.b2R\:2074/2 of the four-dimensional ball (Weyl\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law), so the number of levels with \[Mu]_n \[LessEqual] \
\[Mu] is N(\[Mu]) \[TildeTilde] V\[UpTee] \[Mu]\:2074/(32\[Pi]\.b2) and their \
density dN = V\[UpTee] \[Mu]\.b3 d\[Mu]/(8\[Pi]\.b2). With M8 = 10 TeV (\
\[Kappa] = M8\:207b\:2076) and the reduced Planck mass M_Pl = 2.435 \[Times] \
10\.b9\:2078 GeV, V\[UpTee] = M_Pl\.b2/M8\:2076 (sections 17.5 and 22.2). For \
comparison (CODATA 2018): the proton charge radius 0.8414 fm and the Bohr \
radius 5.29177210903 \[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\.b9 m; R = ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]/(2\[Pi]) is the radius of each circle in the convention V\[UpTee] \
= (2\[Pi]R)\:2074 of the Particle Data Group, in which the model has M_D = (2\
\[Pi])^(2/3) M8 (section 24.1)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69f02eb3-9a4e-2048-991a-72fa984c49d4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Jacobi's four-square theorem: the number of n in Z^4 with |n|^2 = k \
is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) - 32 sigma(k/4) for k = 1..100 (direct count over \
{-10, ..., 10}^4)\",
  With[{nn = Total[Tuples[Range[-10, 10], 4]^2, {2}]}, Table[Count[nn, kk], \
{kk, 100}]] == rIIr4[[1 ;; 100]]]
tbNR[R_] := 1 + Total[rIIr4[[1 ;; R^2]]];
tbRs = {10, 30, 100, 300, 1000}; tbNRs = tbNR /@ tbRs; tbDev = N[tbNRs/(Pi^2 \
tbRs^4/2) - 1];
check[\"Weyl's law: the number N(R) of n in Z^4 with |n| <= R approaches the \
volume Pi^2 R^4/2 of the four-ball: N(10) = 49689, N(100) = 493490641, and \
|N(R)/(Pi^2 R^4/2) - 1| < 10^-2, 10^-3, 3 10^-5, 5 10^-6, 10^-6 for R = 10, \
30, 100, 300, 1000\",
  tbNRs[[1]] == 49689 && tbNRs[[3]] == 493490641 && And @@ MapThread[Abs[#1] \
< #2 &, {tbDev, {10^-2, 10^-3, 3*^-5, 5*^-6, 10^-6}}]]
{\"r_4(k), k = 0..16\" -> Join[{1}, rIIr4[[1 ;; 16]]], \"N(R) for R = 10, 30, \
100, 300, 1000\" -> tbNRs, \"N(R)/(Pi^2 R^4/2) - 1 for R = 10, 30, 100, 300, \
1000\" -> tbDev}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1206]:=",ExpressionUUID->"61e337a6-5961-4b4b-887d-a4e24679fb5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Jacobi's four-square theorem: the number of n in Z^4 with |n|^2 \
= k is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) - 32 sigma(k/4) for k = 1..100 (direct count over \
{-10, ..., 10}^4)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191849738785*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1206]=",ExpressionUUID->"59db38f5-9438-2748-bf9a-50c83e5ad098"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Weyl's law: the number N(R) of n in Z^4 with |n| <= R \
approaches the volume Pi^2 R^4/2 of the four-ball: N(10) = 49689, N(100) = \
493490641, and |N(R)/(Pi^2 R^4/2) - 1| < 10^-2, 10^-3, 3 10^-5, 5 10^-6, \
10^-6 for R = 10, 30, 100, 300, 1000\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918497419033`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1209]=",ExpressionUUID->"c8c958ba-8213-744a-a715-a81fd56d12cf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"r_4(k), k = 0..16\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1", ",", "8", ",", "24", ",", "32", ",", "24", ",", "48", ",", "96", ",",
       "64", ",", "24", ",", "104", ",", "144", ",", "96", ",", "96", ",", 
      "112", ",", "192", ",", "192", ",", "24"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"N(R) for R = 10, 30, 100, 300, 1000\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "49689", ",", "4000425", ",", "493490641", ",", "39972070929", ",", 
      "4934805110729"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"N(R)/(Pi^2 R^4/2) - 1 for R = 10, 30, 100, 300, 1000\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "0.00690965880082417`", ",", "0.0008093730182692216`", ",", 
      "0.000021117250719626668`", ",", "4.330657224604906`*^-6", ",", 
      "5.897266399657042`*^-7"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918497434235`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1210]=",ExpressionUUID->"321b9cd0-5e43-4342-97ab-f110ed29b237"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
tbLp = rIIVp^(1/4); tbHbarCm = 1.973269804*^-16;                  (* hbar c \
in GeV m *)
tbNmu[mu_] := rIIVp mu^4/(32 Pi^2);
check[\"the auxiliary torus today (M8 = 10 TeV, M_Pl = 2.435 10^18 GeV): \
V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6 = 5.929 10^12 GeV^-4, l_perp = V_perp^(1/4) = b0 Lc = \
1560.4 GeV^-1 = 3.079 10^-13 m, lowest Kaluza-Klein mass 2 Pi/l_perp = 4.027 \
MeV; N(mu) = V_perp mu^4/(32 Pi^2) = 1.17 10^13 levels below m_r/2 = 5 GeV \
(the lattice count of section 22.2 agrees to 10^-5) and N(M8) = M_Pl^2/(32 \
Pi^2 M8^2)\",
  Abs[rIIVp/5.929*^12 - 1] < 10^-3 && Abs[tbLp/1560.4 - 1] < 10^-4 && \
Abs[tbLp tbHbarCm/3.079*^-13 - 1] < 10^-3 && Abs[2 Pi/tbLp 10^3/4.027 - 1] < \
10^-3 &&
  Abs[(1 + Total[rIIr4])/tbNmu[5.] - 1] < 10^-5 && Abs[tbNmu[5.]/1.17*^13 - \
1] < 0.01 && Abs[tbNmu[rIIM8]/(rIIMPl^2/(32 Pi^2 rIIM8^2)) - 1] < 10^-12]
tbLevels = Table[{k, rIIr4[[k]], 4 rIIr4[[k]], 2 Pi Sqrt[k]/tbLp 10^3}, {k, \
1, 8}];
{\"V_perp (GeV^-4), l_perp (GeV^-1), l_perp (m), l_perp (fm), 2 Pi/l_perp \
(MeV)\" -> {rIIVp, tbLp, tbLp tbHbarCm, tbLp tbHbarCm 10^15, 2 Pi/tbLp 10^3},
 \"l_perp/proton radius, Bohr radius/l_perp, R = l_perp/(2 Pi) (GeV^-1, m), \
M_D = (2 Pi)^(2/3) M8 (GeV)\" -> {tbLp tbHbarCm/0.8414*^-15, \
5.29177210903*^-11/(tbLp tbHbarCm), tbLp/(2 Pi), tbLp tbHbarCm/(2 Pi), (2 \
Pi)^(2/3) rIIM8},
 \"N(mu) = V_perp mu^4/(32 Pi^2) for mu = 5 GeV, m_h, M8; lattice count below \
5 GeV\" -> {tbNmu[5.], tbNmu[mHb], tbNmu[rIIM8], 1 + Total[rIIr4]},
 \"first levels: k, r_4(k), Dirac fermions 4 r_4(k), mass 2 Pi Sqrt[k]/l_perp \
(MeV), k = 1..8\" -> tbLevels}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1211]:=",ExpressionUUID->"89aa3116-df4d-c447-b4e6-3a1f30e1948c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the auxiliary torus today (M8 = 10 TeV, M_Pl = 2.435 10^18 \
GeV): V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6 = 5.929 10^12 GeV^-4, l_perp = V_perp^(1/4) = b0 \
Lc = 1560.4 GeV^-1 = 3.079 10^-13 m, lowest Kaluza-Klein mass 2 Pi/l_perp = \
