Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.4 Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law on the torus: images and \
Kaluza\[Dash]Klein modes\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"91457acc-4b1e-284e-943d-b5f29feb4040"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In linearized eight-dimensional gravity (no stabilizing potential) a static \
mass M has the potential \[CapitalPhi] = \[Minus]5\[Kappa]M/(32\[Pi]\.b3 r\
\:2075) at the distance r (\[Kappa] = 8\[Pi]G8): the Green\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
function 1/(5 \[CapitalOmega]_6 r\:2075) of the seven-dimensional Laplacian (\
\[CapitalOmega]_6 = 16\[Pi]\.b3/15 the area of the unit six-sphere) times 8\
\[Pi]G8 (D \[Minus] 3)/(D \[Minus] 2) = (5/6) \[Kappa]. On the torus the mass \
has images at the lattice points ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] n (n \[Element] \:2124\:2074), and a second mass on the brane at \
the distance r along the brane feels \[CapitalPhi](r) = \
\[Minus](5\[Kappa]M/(32\[Pi]\.b3)) \[CapitalSigma]_n (r\.b2 + ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]\.b2 |n|\.b2)^(\[Minus]5/2). Poisson summation turns the sum over \
images into a sum over the Kaluza\[Dash]Klein modes, \[CapitalSigma]_n (r\.b2 \
+ |n|\.b2)^(\[Minus]5/2) = (4\[Pi]\.b2/(3r)) \[CapitalSigma]_m e^{\[Minus]2\
\[Pi] r |m|} (lengths in units of ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]), because the four-dimensional Fourier transform of (r\.b2 + |y|\
\.b2)^(\[Minus]5/2) is (4\[Pi]\.b2/(3r)) e^{\[Minus]p r}. Hence \
\[CapitalPhi](r) = \[Minus](5/3) G4 M \[CapitalSigma]_m e^{\[Minus]\[Mu]_m \
r}/r with G4 = G8/V\[UpTee]: every Kaluza\[Dash]Klein level (mass \[Mu]_m = 2\
\[Pi]|m|/",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]) adds a Yukawa potential, and the zero mode gives (5/3) G4 M/r. Of \
the factor 5/3, 1 is the four-dimensional graviton and 2/3 the radion \
(massless without the stabilizer), whose coupling (\[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl)) T^\
\[Mu]_\[Mu] (section 20.3) gives \[Minus](2/3) G4 M M\[Prime] e^{\[Minus]m_r \
r}/r; with the stabilizing potential the radion has the mass m_r, and at \
distances r \[GreaterGreater] ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee], 1/m_r Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law \[Minus]G4 M M\[Prime]/r \
holds. Near the source (r \[LessLess] ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]) the eight-dimensional law returns: r\:2075 S(r) \[RightArrow] 1 + \
r\:2075 Z(5/2), with Z(5/2) = \[CapitalSigma]_(n\[NotEqual]0) |n|\:207b\:2075 \
= 8(1 \[Minus] 4^(\[Minus]3/2)) \[Zeta](5/2) \[Zeta](3/2) = 7 \[Zeta](5/2) \
\[Zeta](3/2)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"242745b1-7531-c846-90db-472fa33f2238"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Newton's law in eight dimensions: Omega_6 = 2 Pi^(7/2)/Gamma(7/2) = \
16 Pi^3/15, r^-5 is harmonic away from r = 0 in seven space dimensions \
((1/r^6) d/dr (r^6 d/dr r^-5) = 0), and grad^2 Phi = 8 Pi G8 ((D - 3)/(D - \
2)) M delta^7 (D = 8) gives Phi = -(5/6) kappa M/(5 Omega_6 r^5) = -5 kappa \
M/(32 Pi^3 r^5); the same formula in D = 4 gives -G M/r\",
  Simplify[2 Pi^(7/2)/Gamma[7/2] - 16 Pi^3/15] === 0 && Simplify[D[tbr^6 \
D[tbr^-5, tbr], tbr]] === 0 &&
  Simplify[tbKap (5/6)/(5 (16 Pi^3/15)) - 5 tbKap/(32 Pi^3)] === 0 && \
Simplify[8 Pi tbGN (1/2)/(1 (2 Pi^(3/2)/Gamma[3/2])) - tbGN] === 0]
tbS[r_?NumericQ] := Module[{kk = N[Range[Length[rIIr4]]], u0 = r^2 + \
Length[rIIr4] + 1/2},
   r^-5 + Total[rIIr4 (r^2 + kk)^(-5/2)] + Pi^2 (2/Sqrt[u0] - 2 r^2/(3 \
u0^(3/2)))];      (* images: Sum over Z^4 of (r^2 + |n|^2)^(-5/2) *)
tbSkk[r_?NumericQ] := 4 Pi^2/(3 r) (1 + Total[rIIr4[[1 ;; 20000]] Exp[-2 Pi r \
Sqrt[N[Range[20000]]]]]);   (* Kaluza-Klein modes *)
tbPois = Table[With[{si = tbS[r], sk = tbSkk[r]}, {si, sk, si/sk - 1}], {r, \
{1/4, 1/2, 1, 2}}];
check[\"images = Kaluza-Klein modes (Poisson summation; lengths in units of \
l_perp): Sum_n (r^2 + |n|^2)^(-5/2) == (4 Pi^2/(3 r)) Sum_m Exp[-2 Pi r |m|] \
to 10^-8 at r = 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2 (left: shells with r_4(k) to k = 1.5 10^6 and \
the continuum tail Pi^2 Int k (r^2 + k)^(-5/2) dk; right: shells to k = \
20000)\",
  AllTrue[tbPois[[All, 3]], Abs[#] < 10^-8 &]]
tbZ52 = N[7 Zeta[5/2] Zeta[3/2], 20];
tbZ52s = Total[rIIr4 N[Range[Length[rIIr4]]]^(-5/2)] + 2 \
Pi^2/Sqrt[Length[rIIr4] + 1/2];
tbNear = Table[(r^5 tbS[r] - 1)/(r^5 tbZ52), {r, {1/20, 1/10}}];
tbFar = Table[(3 r tbSkk[r]/(4 Pi^2) - 1)/(8 Exp[-2 Pi r]), {r, {1, 2, 3}}];
check[\"near and far field: Z(5/2) = Sum_(n != 0) |n|^-5 = Sum_k r_4(k) \
k^(-5/2) = 7 zeta(5/2) zeta(3/2) = 24.531 (shell sum with tail, to 10^-8); \
near the source r^5 S(r) - 1 -> r^5 Z(5/2) (the ratio lies between 0.98 and 1 \
at r = 1/10 and 1/20, closer to 1 at 1/20): the eight-dimensional law; far \
from it 3 r S/(4 Pi^2) - 1 -> 8 Exp[-2 Pi r], the 8 lightest Kaluza-Klein \
modes (ratio 1 to 2 10^-2 at r = 2 and 3)\",
  Abs[tbZ52s/tbZ52 - 1] < 10^-8 && Abs[tbZ52 - 24.531] < 10^-3 && \
AllTrue[tbNear, 0.98 < # < 1 &] && tbNear[[1]] > tbNear[[2]] &&
  AllTrue[tbFar[[2 ;; 3]], Abs[# - 1] < 2*^-2 &]]
check[\"graviton + radion: far from the source the images add up to (5 kappa \
M/(32 Pi^3)) (4 Pi^2/(3 V_perp r)) == (5/3) G4 M/r with G4 = kappa/(8 Pi \
V_perp); the radion of section 20.3, coupled to matter by (phi/(Sqrt[3] \
M_Pl)) T, gives the potential -(1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl))^2 M M' Exp[-m_r r]/(4 Pi \
r), and (1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl))^2/(4 Pi) == (2/3) G4 (8 Pi G4 = 1/M_Pl^2): \
graviton 1 + massless radion 2/3 = 5/3\",
  Simplify[(5 tbKap/(32 Pi^3)) (4 Pi^2/(3 tbVs)) - (5/3) tbKap/(8 Pi tbVs)] \
=== 0 && Simplify[(1/(Sqrt[3] tbMP))^2/(4 Pi) - (2/3)/(8 Pi tbMP^2), tbMP > \
0] === 0]
{\"images S(r), Kaluza-Klein (4 Pi^2/(3 r)) Sum Exp[-2 Pi r |m|], relative \
difference, at r = 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2\" -> tbPois, \"Z(5/2) = 7 zeta(5/2) \
zeta(3/2), shell sum with tail\" -> {tbZ52, tbZ52s},
 \"near field (r^5 S - 1)/(r^5 Z(5/2)) at r = 1/20, 1/10; far field (3 r S/(4 \
Pi^2) - 1)/(8 Exp[-2 Pi r]) at r = 1, 2, 3\" -> Join[tbNear, tbFar]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1216]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eea6b7da-4fd6-874e-937d-331ccec2ce46"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Newton's law in eight dimensions: Omega_6 = 2 \
Pi^(7/2)/Gamma(7/2) = 16 Pi^3/15, r^-5 is harmonic away from r = 0 in seven \
space dimensions ((1/r^6) d/dr (r^6 d/dr r^-5) = 0), and grad^2 Phi = 8 Pi G8 \
((D - 3)/(D - 2)) M delta^7 (D = 8) gives Phi = -(5/6) kappa M/(5 Omega_6 \
r^5) = -5 kappa M/(32 Pi^3 r^5); the same formula in D = 4 gives -G M/r\"\>", 
  "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918497636166`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1216]=",ExpressionUUID->"c2eeaf45-6e00-8b43-a82f-defd92f6e037"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"images = Kaluza-Klein modes (Poisson summation; lengths in \
units of l_perp): Sum_n (r^2 + |n|^2)^(-5/2) == (4 Pi^2/(3 r)) Sum_m Exp[-2 \
Pi r |m|] to 10^-8 at r = 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2 (left: shells with r_4(k) to k = 1.5 \
10^6 and the continuum tail Pi^2 Int k (r^2 + k)^(-5/2) dk; right: shells to \
k = 20000)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
