Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.5 Kaluza\[Dash]Klein momentum: conserved in the bulk, not at the brane\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"0e047a00-fd5d-4640-a1db-0e0bb28c1c9f"],

Cell["\<\
The translations y \[RightArrow] y + c are isometries of the torus; their \
conserved charge is the Kaluza\[Dash]Klein momentum n. A local interaction in \
the bulk conserves it: the overlap of three modes, \[Integral] b\:2074 \
d\:2074y \[Phi]_n \[Phi]_m \[Phi]_l*, is 1/\[Sqrt]V\[UpTee] if l = n + m and \
0 otherwise. The world brane sits at the point y = 0 and is not invariant \
under the translations: there every mode has the same value \
1/\[Sqrt]V\[UpTee], so an interaction on the brane couples all modes with the \
same strength (the portals of sections 18.2 and 24.4). The delta function of \
the torus, \[Delta]\:2074(y) = Lc\:207b\:2074 \[CapitalSigma]_n e^{i q_n\
\[CenterDot]y}, contains every mode with the same weight; its average over \
the torus (its zero mode) is 1/Lc\:2074, which is why a brane source smeared \
over the torus has the eight-dimensional density \[Rho]_4/V\[UpTee] (section \
20.2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa6809b4-306e-5246-9ead-f0edecee2c7f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
tbVtx[n_, m_, l_] := tbInt[tbPhi[n] tbPhi[m] tbPhiC[l]];
check[\"Kaluza-Klein momentum is conserved in the bulk and not at the brane: \
Int b^4 d^4y phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == 1/Sqrt[V_perp] for l = n + m and 0 \
otherwise (exact: n = (1, 0, 0, 2), m = (0, 1, -1, 0), l = (1, 1, -1, 2) and \
(1, 1, -1, 1)); at y = 0, phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == V_perp^(-3/2) for every n, \
m, l\",
  Simplify[tbVtx[{1, 0, 0, 2}, {0, 1, -1, 0}, {1, 1, -1, 2}] - 1/Sqrt[tbV], \
tbLc > 0 && tbB > 0] === 0 && tbVtx[{1, 0, 0, 2}, {0, 1, -1, 0}, {1, 1, -1, \
1}] === 0 &&
  Simplify[((tbPhi[{1, 0, 0, 2}] tbPhi[{0, 1, -1, 0}] tbPhiC[{1, 1, -1, 1}]) \
/. Thread[tbY -> 0]) - tbV^(-3/2), tbLc > 0 && tbB > 0] === 0]
check[\"the delta function of the torus: Int_(-Lc/2)^(Lc/2) Exp[-I q_n y] \
delta(y) dy == 1 for every integer n, so delta^4(y) = Lc^-4 Sum_n Exp[I \
q_n.y] (every mode with the weight 1/Lc^4); a brane source rho4 \
delta^4(y)/b^4 has Int b^4 d^4y (rho4 delta^4(y)/b^4) == rho4, i.e. the \
average rho4/V_perp over the torus\",
  Simplify[Integrate[Exp[-I 2 Pi tbn y1D/tbLc] DiracDelta[y1D], {y1D, \
-tbLc/2, tbLc/2}, Assumptions -> tbLc > 0 && Element[tbn, Integers]]] === 1 &&
  Simplify[Integrate[tbB^4 tbRho DiracDelta[x4] DiracDelta[x5] DiracDelta[x6] \
DiracDelta[x7]/tbB^4, {x4, -tbLc/2, tbLc/2}, {x5, -tbLc/2, tbLc/2},
     {x6, -tbLc/2, tbLc/2}, {x7, -tbLc/2, tbLc/2}, Assumptions -> tbLc > 0]] \
=== tbRho]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1228]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3922301d-cfbd-c14d-9bb4-d00d218f9d51"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Kaluza-Klein momentum is conserved in the bulk and not at the \
brane: Int b^4 d^4y phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == 1/Sqrt[V_perp] for l = n + m and 0 \
otherwise (exact: n = (1, 0, 0, 2), m = (0, 1, -1, 0), l = (1, 1, -1, 2) and \
(1, 1, -1, 1)); at y = 0, phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == V_perp^(-3/2) for every n, \
m, l\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918528319626`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1229]=",ExpressionUUID->"532725a5-ca5e-ef48-8d8a-b74bbf644877"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the delta function of the torus: Int_(-Lc/2)^(Lc/2) Exp[-I q_n \
y] delta(y) dy == 1 for every integer n, so delta^4(y) = Lc^-4 Sum_n Exp[I \
q_n.y] (every mode with the weight 1/Lc^4); a brane source rho4 \
delta^4(y)/b^4 has Int b^4 d^4y (rho4 delta^4(y)/b^4) == rho4, i.e. the \
average rho4/V_perp over the torus\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918532932816`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1230]=",ExpressionUUID->"55efc205-26ea-c042-9737-da3fec4566c5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.6 The world brane: embedding, induced metric, volume element and extrinsic \
curvature\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"047d3c55-0beb-1d44-a020-ee6c6b959846"],

Cell["\<\
The embedding X(x) = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, 0) of W has the Jacobian J^A_\
\[Mu] = \[PartialD]X^A/\[PartialD]x^\[Mu] (an 8\[Times]4 matrix of zeros and \
ones), and the induced metric is h = J\[Transpose] g J. For the cosmological \
metric of section 11.2 the brane sees the \
Friedmann\[Dash]Robertson\[Dash]Walker metric diag(1, \[Minus]a\.b2, \
\[Minus]a\.b2, \[Minus]a\.b2): it does not see b. For the inhomogeneous test \
metric of section 11.3 it sees diag(n\.b2, \[Minus]a\.b2, \[Minus]a\.b2, \
\[Minus]a\.b2) evaluated at x4 = 0. Because g is block diagonal at the brane, \
\[Sqrt]|g| = \[Sqrt]|h| b\:2074 there, and a brane integral is an \
eight-dimensional integral with the factor \[Delta]\:2074(y)/b\:2074. How the \
brane sits in the bulk is measured by its extrinsic curvature \
K^(k)_\[Mu]\[Nu] = (1/(2b)) \[PartialD]_k g_\[Mu]\[Nu] at W (for g_\[Mu]k = 0 \
and \[Minus]g_kl = b\.b2 \[Delta]_kl at W). The Christoffel symbols {k \[Mu]\
\[Nu]} = (1/(2b\.b2)) \[PartialD]_k g_\[Mu]\[Nu] at W are the accelerations \
transverse to the brane of a free particle that moves along it: if they \
vanish, the brane is totally geodesic, and a particle that moves along the \
brane stays on it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff24fbe4-3d17-0045-abc6-1e86a85985c9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
tbJ = Table[If[A == mu, 1, 0], {A, 8}, {mu, 4}];                       (* \
dX^A/dx^mu for X = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, 0) *)
tbOnW = {x4 -> 0, x5 -> 0, x6 -> 0, x7 -> 0};
tbInduced[g_] := Simplify[Transpose[tbJ].(g /. tbOnW).tbJ];
check[\"the world brane W = {x4 = x5 = x6 = x7 = 0}: the induced metric h = \
J^T.g.J of the embedding X = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, 0) is, for the \
cosmological metric of section 11.2, the Friedmann-Robertson-Walker metric \
diag(1, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) (independent of b); for the inhomogeneous metric of \
section 11.3 it is diag(n^2, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) at x4 = 0 with n = 1 + \
x0^2/11, a = 1 + x0/3\",
  tbInduced[gCos] == DiagonalMatrix[{1, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2}] &&
  Simplify[tbInduced[gPoly] - DiagonalMatrix[{(1 + x0^2/11)^2, -(1 + x0/3)^2, \
-(1 + x0/3)^2, -(1 + x0/3)^2}]] === ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}]]
tbPt = {x0 -> 1/2, x4 -> 0};
check[\"brane integrals in eight-dimensional form: at the brane Sqrt|det g| \
== Sqrt|det h| b^4 with b^4 = Sqrt[det(-g_kl)] (cosmological metric; \
inhomogeneous metric exactly at x0 = 1/2), so Int_W d^4x Sqrt|h| L == Int \
d^8X Sqrt|g| (delta^4(y)/b^4) L; test: Int d^4y b^4 (delta^4(y)/b^4) F(y) == \
F(0) = 1 for F = Exp[x4 + 2 x5] Cos[x6 - x7]\",
  Simplify[Sqrt[-Det[gCos]] - Sqrt[-Det[tbInduced[gCos]]] Sqrt[Det[-tbG4]], \
a3[x0] > 0 && b4[x0] > 0] === 0 &&
  (Sqrt[-Det[gPoly /. tbPt]] - Sqrt[-Det[tbInduced[gPoly] /. tbPt]] \
Sqrt[Det[-(gPoly[[5 ;; 8, 5 ;; 8]] /. tbPt)]]) === 0 &&
  Simplify[Integrate[tbB^4 (DiracDelta[x4] DiracDelta[x5] DiracDelta[x6] \
DiracDelta[x7]/tbB^4) Exp[x4 + 2 x5] Cos[x6 - x7], {x4, -1, 1}, {x5, -1, 1},
     {x6, -1, 1}, {x7, -1, 1}]] === 1]
tbChrW[cv_, pt_] := Table[cv[\"chr\"][[k, mu, nu]] /. pt, {k, 5, 8}, {mu, 1, \
4}, {nu, 1, 4}];      (* {k mu nu}, k = 4..7, mu, nu = 0..3, at the brane *)
check[\"how the brane sits in the bulk: the Christoffel symbols {k mu nu} at \
the brane (k = 4..7, mu, nu = 0..3; = (1/(2 b^2)) d_k g_mu nu for these \
metrics, b times the extrinsic curvature) all vanish for the cosmological \
metric: the brane is totally geodesic, and a free particle moving along it \
stays on it. For the inhomogeneous metric at x0 = 1/2 the only non-zero one \
is {4 00} = n (d_4 n)/b^2 = 1458/58619: a free particle at rest on the brane \
is accelerated off it\",
  AllTrue[Flatten[tbChrW[cvCos, tbOnW]], # === 0 &] &&
  tbChrW[cvPoly, tbPt] == ReplacePart[ConstantArray[0, {4, 4, 4}], {1, 1, 1} \
-> 1458/58619] &&
  ((nP D[nP, x4]/bP^2) /. tbPt) == 1458/58619]
{\"Christoffel {4 00} at the brane (inhomogeneous metric, x0 = 1/2)\" -> \
N[1458/58619, 16]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1231]:=",ExpressionUUID->"72ac157c-b07d-244d-ba76-892fcd4327dc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the world brane W = {x4 = x5 = x6 = x7 = 0}: the induced metric \
h = J^T.g.J of the embedding X = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, 0) is, for the \
cosmological metric of section 11.2, the Friedmann-Robertson-Walker metric \
diag(1, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) (independent of b); for the inhomogeneous metric of \
section 11.3 it is diag(n^2, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) at x4 = 0 with n = 1 + \
x0^2/11, a = 1 + x0/3\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191853353283*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1234]=",ExpressionUUID->"ff0a6887-9ee8-4148-8926-1422b644d437"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"brane integrals in eight-dimensional form: at the brane \
Sqrt|det g| == Sqrt|det h| b^4 with b^4 = Sqrt[det(-g_kl)] (cosmological \
metric; inhomogeneous metric exactly at x0 = 1/2), so Int_W d^4x Sqrt|h| L == \
Int d^8X Sqrt|g| (delta^4(y)/b^4) L; test: Int d^4y b^4 (delta^4(y)/b^4) F(y) \
== F(0) = 1 for F = Exp[x4 + 2 x5] Cos[x6 - x7]\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191853480892*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1236]=",ExpressionUUID->"4f31810d-c1c6-3640-bd9f-d50eebdb728a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"how the brane sits in the bulk: the Christoffel symbols {k mu \
nu} at the brane (k = 4..7, mu, nu = 0..3; = (1/(2 b^2)) d_k g_mu nu for \
these metrics, b times the extrinsic curvature) all vanish for the \
cosmological metric: the brane is totally geodesic, and a free particle \
moving along it stays on it. For the inhomogeneous metric at x0 = 1/2 the \
only non-zero one is {4 00} = n (d_4 n)/b^2 = 1458/58619: a free particle at \
rest on the brane is accelerated off it\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918534838924`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1238]=",ExpressionUUID->"7c04b367-f60d-0148-89c7-001b6e343369"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
