Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
25.8 Matter on the brane, and the brane in four-dimensional physics\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"88cad1eb-76d8-9146-8bc2-a039db184cd6"],

Cell["\<\
A brane action S_W = \[Integral]_W d\:2074x \[Sqrt]|h| L_W gives the \
eight-dimensional energy\[Dash]momentum tensor T^AB = (\[Delta]\:2074(y)/b\
\:2074) T_W^\[Mu]\[Nu] \[Delta]^A_\[Mu] \[Delta]^B_\[Nu] with T_W \[Mu]\[Nu] \
= (2/\[Sqrt]|h|) \[Delta]S_W/\[Delta]h^\[Mu]\[Nu]: it has no components along \
the torus. The tension (L_W = \[Minus]f_W) has T_W \[Mu]\[Nu] = f_W h_\[Mu]\
\[Nu]: the energy density f_W and the pressure \[Minus]f_W along the brane (w \
= \[Minus]1). Smeared over the torus (\[Delta]\:2074(y) \[RightArrow] \
Lc\:207b\:2074, section 20.2) the tension gives \[Epsilon] = f_W/V\[UpTee], \
pa = \[Minus]f_W/V\[UpTee], pb = 0, and brane radiation pa = \[Epsilon]/3, pb \
= 0, while radiation in the bulk, isotropic in the seven space directions, \
has pa = pb = \[Epsilon]/7. In the static modern regime the tension is a part \
of the four-dimensional cosmological constant, \[CapitalLambda]4 = \
\[CapitalLambda] + \[Kappa]U0 + \[Kappa]f_W/V\[UpTee] (section 20.3): a \
four-dimensional vacuum energy f_W, for f_W = M8\:2074 about 4 \[Times] 10\
\:2076\.b2 times the observed dark-energy density. The brane plasma loses \
energy to the bulk by emitting Kaluza\[Dash]Klein modes, at the relative rate \
T\:2077/M8\:2076 = (number of levels V\[UpTee]T\:2074) \[Times] (rate per \
level T\.b3/M_Pl\.b2) (estimate, numerical factors omitted), which equals the \
expansion rate T\.b2/M_Pl at the normalcy temperature T* = \
(M8\:2076/M_Pl)^(1/5). Finally, a thin brane is an idealization: the \
linearized field of its tension falls like \[Kappa]f_W/(4\[Pi]\.b2|y|\.b2) \
(the Green\[CloseCurlyQuote]s function \[Minus]1/(4\[Pi]\.b2|y|\.b2) of the \
four transverse directions) and is of order one within |y| \[TildeTilde] (\
\[Kappa]f_W)^(1/2)/(2\[Pi]) = 1/(2\[Pi] M8) of the brane for f_W = M8\:2074 \
(estimate); there the thin-brane description fails, and the smeared \
description of sections 20\[Dash]23 holds far from it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54217024-99f4-fc43-b660-a858626898eb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"brane tension: for S_W = -Int d^4x Sqrt|h| f_W and h = diag(1/u0, \
-1/u1, -1/u2, -1/u3) (h^00 = u0, h^ii = -u_i), T_mu nu = (2/Sqrt|h|) \
dS_W/dh^mu nu == f_W h_mu nu, T^0_0 == f_W (energy density) and T^1_1 == f_W \
(pressure -f_W: w = -1 along the brane)\",
  Module[{sq = 1/Sqrt[tbu0 tbu1 tbu2 tbu3], t00, t11},
   t00 = (2/sq) D[-tbfW sq, tbu0]; t11 = (2/sq) (-D[-tbfW sq, tbu1]);
   Simplify[{t00 - tbfW/tbu0, t11 + tbfW/tbu1, tbu0 t00, -tbu1 t11}, tbu0 > 0 \
&& tbu1 > 0 && tbu2 > 0 && tbu3 > 0] === {0, 0, tbfW, tbfW}]]
check[\"sources smeared over the torus (W(a, b) the comoving energy, section \
20.2): the brane tension W = a^3 f_W/Lc^4 gives eps = f_W/V_perp, pa = -eps, \
pb = 0; brane radiation W = a^3 r0 a^-4/Lc^4 gives pa = eps/3, pb = 0; \
radiation of the bulk, isotropic in the seven space directions, has <cos^2 \
theta> = 3/7 and <sin^2 theta> = 4/7 for the weight cos^2 theta sin^3 theta \
of the momentum sphere, so pa = (1/3)(3/7) eps = eps/7 and pb = (1/4)(4/7) \
eps = eps/7\",
  Simplify[feStress[Function[{tbAa, tbBb}, tbAa^3 tbfW/tbLc^4]] - {tbfW/(bS^4 \
tbLc^4), -tbfW/(bS^4 tbLc^4), 0}] === {0, 0, 0} &&
  With[{st = feStress[Function[{tbAa, tbBb}, tbAa^3 tbr0 tbAa^-4/tbLc^4]]}, \
Simplify[{st[[2]] - st[[1]]/3, st[[3]]}] === {0, 0}] &&
  With[{c2 = Integrate[Cos[tbth]^4 Sin[tbth]^3, {tbth, 0, \
Pi/2}]/Integrate[Cos[tbth]^2 Sin[tbth]^3, {tbth, 0, Pi/2}]}, c2 == 3/7 && \
c2/3 == 1/7 && (1 - c2)/4 == 1/7]]
tbTstar = (rIIM8^6/rIIMPl)^(1/5);
check[\"the brane in four-dimensional physics: (i) the tension is vacuum \
energy, kappa f_W/V_perp == f_W/M_Pl^2 (V_perp = kappa M_Pl^2), and f_W = \
M8^4 is between 3 10^62 and 5 10^62 times rho_Lambda = 3 H0^2 M_Pl^2 \
Omega_Lambda (section 24.5); (ii) normalcy temperature: (T^7/M8^6)/(T^2/M_Pl) \
== 1 at T* = (M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) = 13.3 GeV, and V_perp T^4 T^3/M_Pl^2 == \
T^7/M8^6; (iii) thin brane: (1/y^3) d/dy (y^3 d/dy y^-2) == 0 and 2 Pi^2 y^3 \
d/dy y^-2 == -4 Pi^2 (the Green's function -1/(4 Pi^2 |y|^2) of the four \
transverse directions), and Sqrt[kappa f_W] == 1/M8 for f_W = M8^4\",
  Simplify[(tbKap tbfW/tbVs /. tbVs -> tbKap tbMP^2) - tbfW/tbMP^2] === 0 && \
3*^62 < rIIM8^4/dkRhoL < 5*^62 &&
  Simplify[((tbT^7/tbM8^6)/(tbT^2/tbMP)) /. tbT -> (tbM8^6/tbMP)^(1/5), tbM8 \
> 0 && tbMP > 0] === 1 && Abs[tbTstar - 13.3] < 0.05 &&
  Simplify[(tbMP^2/tbM8^6) tbT^4 tbT^3/tbMP^2 - tbT^7/tbM8^6] === 0 &&
  Simplify[D[tby^3 D[tby^-2, tby], tby]] === 0 && Simplify[2 Pi^2 tby^3 \
D[tby^-2, tby]] === -4 Pi^2 && Simplify[Sqrt[tbM8^-6 tbM8^4] - 1/tbM8, tbM8 > \
0] === 0]
{\"T* = (M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) (GeV), f_W/rho_Lambda for f_W = M8^4, 1/(2 Pi M8) \
(GeV^-1)\" -> {tbTstar, rIIM8^4/dkRhoL, 1/(2 Pi rIIM8)}}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1252]:=",ExpressionUUID->"18eaddc3-ae6f-034e-bdf7-0086b0e971e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"brane tension: for S_W = -Int d^4x Sqrt|h| f_W and h = \
diag(1/u0, -1/u1, -1/u2, -1/u3) (h^00 = u0, h^ii = -u_i), T_mu nu = \
(2/Sqrt|h|) dS_W/dh^mu nu == f_W h_mu nu, T^0_0 == f_W (energy density) and \
T^1_1 == f_W (pressure -f_W: w = -1 along the brane)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
