Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26. The radion: the size of the extra space, on the 4-torus and on the \
4-sphere\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"29113bbe-cca1-0842-b0a7-8d9c5087f043"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["About section 26. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Section 26 was appended on 28 October 2026. The notebook as it was before \
(sections 0\[Dash]25, with the summary of all checks numbered 26; evaluated) \
is kept in the workspace as backups/7+1_2026-10-28_before_radion.nb (excluded \
from the repository by .gitignore); nothing in sections 0\[Dash]25 is \
changed. The section checks the ideas of a note of the author on the radion \
(a Kaluza\[Dash]Klein ansatz with the factors e^(2\[Alpha]\[Phi]) and e^(2\
\[Beta]\[Phi]), the Einstein frame, the canonical normalization, the physical \
volume, the radion as a modulus, the fifth force, stabilization, the warped \
alternative of Randall and Sundrum with the stabilization of Goldberger and \
Wise, and the mixing of the radion with the Higgs boson on the brane), states \
the corrections that the checks require, and works every idea out for the two \
cases in which the four extra dimensions are a 4-TORUS T\:2074 (the auxiliary \
space of 7+1.nb, section 25) and a 4-SPHERE S\:2074 (for comparison). \
Coordinates as everywhere: X = {x0, \[Ellipsis], x7}, x0 is time (the \
direction of the octonion unit e[0] = 1), x1, x2, x3 ordinary space, x4 \
\[Ellipsis] x7 the four extra space-like coordinates \[LongDash] on T\:2074 \
the periodic coordinates of section 25, on S\:2074 the angles x4, x5, x6 \
\[Element] [0, \[Pi]], x7 \[Element] [0, 2\[Pi]), with the north pole at x4 = \
0. \[Eta]17 = diag(+1, \[Minus]1, \[Ellipsis], \[Minus]1) is simply the \
squares of the octonion basis; xAct declares the spacetime with the signature \
list {7, 1, 0}: seven space-like and one time-like dimension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e8ee06fd-0d11-7e40-9171-745e0857b8bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The radion. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Write the metric as ds\.b2 = e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta](x)) g_E,\[Mu]\[Nu](x) dx^\
\[Mu] dx^\[Nu] \[Minus] e^(2\[Beta](x)) \[Gamma]_ij(y) dy^i dy^j (x = (x0, \
\[Ellipsis], x3), y = (x4, \[Ellipsis], x7)), with a fixed reference metric \
\[Gamma] of the extra space: \[Gamma] = b0\.b2 \[Delta]_ij on T\:2074 (period \
Lc) and \[Gamma] = r0\.b2 \[Gamma]\:0302 on S\:2074 (\[Gamma]\:0302 the \
metric of the unit sphere, \[Gamma]\:0302 = diag(1, sin\.b2x4, sin\.b2x4 sin\
\.b2x5, sin\.b2x4 sin\.b2x5 sin\.b2x6)). The RADION is the field \[Beta](x): \
the size is b = b0 e^\[Beta] on T\:2074, the radius r = r0 e^\[Beta] on S\
\:2074, and the proper volume V = V0 e^(4\[Beta]) with V0 = b0\:2074 Lc\:2074 \
(T\:2074) or V0 = (8\[Pi]\.b2/3) r0\:2074 (S\:2074). \[Beta] is the same \
field as \[Beta] = ln(b/b0) of section 20.3. The factor e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]) \
in front of g_E puts the four-dimensional action into the EINSTEIN FRAME: the \
coefficient of the four-dimensional curvature, proportional to e^(2\
\[CenterDot](\[Minus]2\[Beta])) e^(4\[Beta]), is then constant. In the \
notation of the note, ds\.b2 = e^(2\[Alpha]\[Phi]) g + e^(2\[Beta]\[Phi]) \
\[Gamma] with 2\[Alpha] + n\[Beta] = 0 (n = 4 extra dimensions)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51e6202c-54a8-ad4a-8eae-48b2906134ad"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.1 The definition: Einstein frame, canonical normalization, physical volume\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7bc0f566-8447-fa47-9ddc-cc5a232053ab"],

Cell["\<\
A small engine for diagonal metrics in any dimension (rdChr, rdRic, rdScal, \
rdEin: Christoffel symbols, Ricci tensor, scalar curvature, mixed Einstein \
tensor G^i_i, with the curvature conventions of section 11) is checked \
against curvature[] of section 11 on the cosmological metric. The claim to be \
checked is the REDUCTION of the eight-dimensional Einstein\[Dash]Hilbert \
action (with the bulk cosmological constant \[CapitalLambda] and the \
stabilizing potential U of section 20): with M_Pl\.b2 = V0/\[Kappa],\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"28f28476-4a28-f64c-9e01-fd9938f34ae5"],

Cell["\<\
      \[Minus](1/(2\[Kappa])) \[Integral] d\:2074y \[Sqrt]|G| (R + 2\
\[CapitalLambda]) \[Minus] \[Integral] d\:2074y \[Sqrt]|G| U  =  \[Sqrt]|g_E| \
[ \[Minus](M_Pl\.b2/2) R_E + 6 M_Pl\.b2 g_E^\[Mu]\[Nu] \[PartialD]_\[Mu]\
\[Beta] \[PartialD]_\[Nu]\[Beta] \[Minus] V(\[Beta]) ]  + (a total \
derivative),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"589640fc-6448-fd4e-8745-cf4816acc27a"],

Cell["\<\
      V(\[Beta]) = e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]) [ M_Pl\.b2 \[CapitalLambda] + V0 U \
\[Minus] (M_Pl\.b2/2) R_int ],   R_int = 0 (T\:2074),   R_int = 12/(r0\.b2 \
e^(2\[Beta])) = 12/r\.b2 (S\:2074).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54e32c4e-6b3f-dd4e-bf05-8ec1e9de3723"],

Cell["\<\
The kinetic term 6 M_Pl\.b2 (\[PartialD]\[Beta])\.b2 = \.bd \
(\[PartialD]\[Phi])\.b2 defines the CANONICAL RADION \[Phi] = \[Sqrt]12 M_Pl \
\[Beta] (section 20.3); the curvature of the sphere adds the negative \
potential \[Minus]6 M_Pl\.b2 e^(\[Minus]6\[Beta])/r0\.b2. The check is done \
on the homogeneous metrics g_E = diag(N\.b2, \[Minus]a\.b2, \[Minus]a\.b2, \
\[Minus]a\.b2) with N(x0), a(x0), \[Beta](x0) arbitrary: the \
Euler\[Dash]Lagrange expressions of the difference of the two sides vanish \
identically, so the difference is a total derivative. For n extra dimensions \
(a torus T\:207f, D = 4 + n) the coefficient 6 = 12/2 becomes n(n+2)/4, i.e. \
\[Minus](M_Pl\.b2/2) R_E + (M_Pl\.b2/2)(n(n+2)/2)(\[PartialD]\[Beta])\.b2. \
The note writes \[Beta] = \[Beta]_n \[Phi] with \[Beta]_n = \
\[Sqrt](2/(n(n+2))) and states the reduced action (M_Pl\.b2/2)[R \[Minus] \
\.bd(\[PartialD]\[Phi])\.b2] (in its signature); the check shows that this \
\[Beta]_n gives (M_Pl\.b2/2)[R \[Minus] (\[PartialD]\[Phi])\.b2] \[LongDash] \
the form with \.bd needs \[Beta]_n = 1/\[Sqrt](n(n+2)). For n = 4 the note\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s values \[Alpha] = \[Minus]1/\[Sqrt]3, \[Beta] = \
1/\[Sqrt]12 satisfy 2\[Alpha] + 4\[Beta] = 0, and its \[Phi] is the canonical \
radion in units of M_Pl: M_Pl \[Phi]_note = \[Sqrt]12 M_Pl ln(b/b0) = \[Phi]; \
the physical volume is V0 e^(4\[Beta] \[Phi]_note) = V0 e^((2/\[Sqrt]3) \
\[Phi]_note) = V0 e^(2\[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl)).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5a75bd5-c997-3047-8767-76fb5bbfe758"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdChr[gd_List, xs_List] := Module[{n = Length[xs]}, Table[Which[a == b == c, \
D[gd[[a]], xs[[a]]]/(2 gd[[a]]), a == b, D[gd[[a]], xs[[c]]]/(2 gd[[a]]),
     a == c, D[gd[[a]], xs[[b]]]/(2 gd[[a]]), b == c, -D[gd[[b]], xs[[a]]]/(2 \
gd[[a]]), True, 0], {a, n}, {b, n}, {c, n}]];
rdRic[gd_List, xs_List, simp_: Simplify] := Module[{n = Length[xs], G = \
rdChr[gd, xs]},
   Table[simp[Sum[D[G[[r, m, s]], xs[[r]]] - D[G[[r, r, s]], xs[[m]]] + \
Sum[G[[r, r, l]] G[[l, m, s]] - G[[r, m, l]] G[[l, r, s]], {l, n}], {r, n}]], \
{s, n}, {m, n}]];
rdScal[gd_List, xs_List, simp_: Simplify] := Module[{ric = rdRic[gd, xs, \
simp]}, simp[Sum[ric[[i, i]]/gd[[i]], {i, Length[xs]}]]];
rdEin[gd_List, xs_List, simp_: Simplify] := Module[{ric = rdRic[gd, xs, \
simp], rs}, rs = simp[Sum[ric[[i, i]]/gd[[i]], {i, Length[xs]}]];
   Table[simp[ric[[i, i]]/gd[[i]] - rs/2], {i, Length[xs]}]];
rdEL[L_, q_] := Simplify[D[L, q[x0]] - D[D[L, q'[x0]], x0] + D[D[L, q''[x0]], \
{x0, 2}]];
rdGam4 = {1, Sin[x4]^2, Sin[x4]^2 Sin[x5]^2, Sin[x4]^2 Sin[x5]^2 Sin[x6]^2};
check[\"section 26 engine for diagonal metrics: rdScal and rdEin reproduce \
curvature[] of section 11 for the cosmological metric (R and every G^A_A)\",
  Simplify[rdScal[Diagonal[gCos], X] - cvCos[\"R\"]] === 0 && \
Simplify[rdEin[Diagonal[gCos], X] - Diagonal[cvCos[\"G\"]]] === \
ConstantArray[0, 8]]
rdRicS4 = rdRic[Join[{1, -1, -1, -1}, -rdR0^2 rdGam4], X];
check[\"the 4-sphere of radius r0: Ricci_ij = 3 gamma_ij (gamma the \
unit-sphere metric), Ricci_ij = 0 for i != j, so R(S^4) = 12/r0^2 (in the \
signature of 7+1.nb the space-like block gives R = -12/r0^2, also with \
curvature[] of section 11); the volume of the unit S^4 is 8 Pi^2/3\",
  And @@ Table[Simplify[rdRicS4[[i, i]] - 3 rdGam4[[i - 4]]] === 0, {i, 5, \
8}] && And @@ Flatten[Table[If[i != j, rdRicS4[[i, j]] === 0, True], {i, 8}, \
{j, 8}]] &&
  Simplify[curvature[DiagonalMatrix[Join[{1, -1, -1, -1}, -rdR0^2 \
rdGam4]]][\"R\"] + 12/rdR0^2] === 0 &&
  Integrate[Sin[x4]^3 Sin[x5]^2 Sin[x6], {x4, 0, Pi}, {x5, 0, Pi}, {x6, 0, \
Pi}, {x7, 0, 2 Pi}] == 8 Pi^2/3]
rdMini[gam_, rint_, v0_] := Module[{gd, rs, lj, le, re, vp, mp2},
   gd = Join[{rdLp[x0]^2 E^(-4 rdBt[x0])}, -rdSa[x0]^2 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) {1, 1, \
1}, -E^(2 rdBt[x0]) gam];
   rs = rdScal[gd, X]; mp2 = v0/rdKap;
   lj = -(1/(2 rdKap)) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) v0 (rs + 2 rdLam) \
- rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) v0 rdU[rdBt[x0]];
   re = rdScal[{rdLp[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2}, Take[X, \
4]];
   vp = E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) (mp2 rdLam + v0 rdU[rdBt[x0]]) - mp2/2 E^(-4 \
rdBt[x0]) rint;
   le = -(mp2/2) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 re + 6 mp2 rdSa[x0]^3 \
rdBt'[x0]^2/rdLp[x0] - rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 vp;
   {FreeQ[rs, x4 | x5 | x6 | x7], rdEL[lj - le, #] & /@ {rdLp, rdSa, rdBt}}];
check[\"radion on T^4: for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) (N^2 dx0^2 - a^2 dx.dx) - e^(2 \
beta) b0^2 dy.dy the reduced action -(1/(2 kappa)) Int(R + 2 Lambda) - Int U \
equals -(M_Pl^2/2) R_E + 6 M_Pl^2 (d beta)^2 - e^(-4 beta)(M_Pl^2 Lambda + V0 \
U) up to a total derivative (Euler-Lagrange expressions for N, a, beta \
vanish), M_Pl^2 = V0/kappa, V0 = b0^4 Lc^4\",
  rdMini[rdB0^2 {1, 1, 1, 1}, 0, rdB0^4 rdLc^4] === {True, {0, 0, 0}}]
check[\"radion on S^4: the same reduction for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) g_E - e^(2 \
beta) r0^2 gamma (unit-sphere gamma) holds with the additional potential \
-(M_Pl^2/2) e^(-4 beta) 12/(r0^2 e^(2 beta)) = -6 M_Pl^2 e^(-6 beta)/r0^2 \
from the curvature of the sphere, V0 = (8 Pi^2/3) r0^4; R is independent of \
the angles\",
  rdMini[rdR0^2 rdGam4, 12/(rdR0^2 E^(2 rdBt[x0])), rdR0^4 8 Pi^2/3] === \
{True, {0, 0, 0}}]
rdKinOK[n_, beta_, coef_] := Module[{xs = Join[{x0}, Table[ToExpression[\"rdY\
\" <> ToString[i]], {i, 3 + n}]], gd, lj, le, re},
   gd = Join[{rdLp[x0]^2 E^(-n beta rdPh[x0])}, -rdSa[x0]^2 E^(-n beta \
rdPh[x0]) {1, 1, 1}, Table[-E^(2 beta rdPh[x0]), {n}]];
   lj = -(1/(2 rdKap)) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-n beta rdPh[x0]) rdScal[gd, xs];
   re = rdScal[{rdLp[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2}, Take[xs, \
4]];
   le = -(1/(2 rdKap)) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 re + (1/(2 rdKap)) coef rdSa[x0]^3 \
rdPh'[x0]^2/rdLp[x0];
   AllTrue[rdEL[lj - le, #] & /@ {rdLp, rdSa, rdPh}, # === 0 &]];
rdKinC[n_] := Module[{xs = Join[{x0}, Table[ToExpression[\"rdY\" <> \
ToString[i]], {i, 3 + n}]], gd, lj, le, re, cc},
   gd = Join[{rdLp[x0]^2 E^(-n rdPh[x0])}, -rdSa[x0]^2 E^(-n rdPh[x0]) {1, 1, \
1}, Table[-E^(2 rdPh[x0]), {n}]];
   lj = -(1/(2 rdKap)) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-n rdPh[x0]) rdScal[gd, xs];
   re = rdScal[{rdLp[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2, -rdSa[x0]^2}, Take[xs, \
4]];
   le = -(1/(2 rdKap)) rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 re + (1/(2 rdKap)) cc rdSa[x0]^3 \
rdPh'[x0]^2/rdLp[x0];
   Simplify[cc /. First[Solve[rdEL[lj - le, rdLp] == 0, cc]]]];
rdKinCs = Table[rdKinC[n], {n, 4}];
check[\"n extra dimensions (torus T^n, D = 4 + n, n = 1..4, Einstein frame \
e^(-n B) g_E): the kinetic term is (M_Pl^2/2)(n(n+2)/2)(dB)^2; with the \
note's B = beta_n phi, beta_n = Sqrt[2/(n(n+2))], it is (M_Pl^2/2)(d phi)^2, \
not (M_Pl^2/2)(1/2)(d phi)^2; the form with 1/2 needs beta_n = 1/Sqrt[n(n+2)]\
\",
  rdKinCs === Table[n (n + 2)/2, {n, 4}] &&
  And @@ Table[rdKinOK[n, 1, n (n + 2)/2] && rdKinOK[n, Sqrt[2/(n (n + 2))], \
1] && ! rdKinOK[n, Sqrt[2/(n (n + 2))], 1/2] && rdKinOK[n, 1/Sqrt[n (n + 2)], \
1/2], {n, 4}]]
check[\"the note's eight-dimensional values alpha = -1/Sqrt[3], beta = \
1/Sqrt[12]: 2 alpha + 4 beta == 0 (Einstein frame), 4 beta == 2/Sqrt[3] (V = \
V0 e^(4 beta phi)), and Sqrt[12] beta == 1, so M_Pl phi_note = Sqrt[12] M_Pl \
ln(b/b0) is the canonical radion of section 20.3\",
  2 (-1/Sqrt[3]) + 4/Sqrt[12] == 0 && 4/Sqrt[12] == 2/Sqrt[3] && \
Sqrt[12]/Sqrt[12] == 1]
{\"general n: kinetic coefficient n(n+2)/2 for n = 1..4\" -> N[rdKinCs], \
\"the note's beta_n^2 = 2/(n(n+2)) and the canonical 1/(n(n+2)), n = 4\" -> \
N[{1/rdKinCs[[4]], 1/(2 rdKinCs[[4]])}]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1257]:=",ExpressionUUID->"21c9af00-28be-9343-9419-6f911b1cf0e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"section 26 engine for diagonal metrics: rdScal and rdEin \
reproduce curvature[] of section 11 for the cosmological metric (R and every \
G^A_A)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191853776457*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1263]=",ExpressionUUID->"5d4d04ae-5f84-a24e-b506-61140271f5fd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the 4-sphere of radius r0: Ricci_ij = 3 gamma_ij (gamma the \
unit-sphere metric), Ricci_ij = 0 for i != j, so R(S^4) = 12/r0^2 (in the \
signature of 7+1.nb the space-like block gives R = -12/r0^2, also with \
curvature[] of section 11); the volume of the unit S^4 is 8 Pi^2/3\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918542503414`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1265]=",ExpressionUUID->"a138a9e0-71d9-4148-b05a-4f9cae28658c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"radion on T^4: for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) (N^2 dx0^2 - a^2 dx.dx) - \
e^(2 beta) b0^2 dy.dy the reduced action -(1/(2 kappa)) Int(R + 2 Lambda) - \
Int U equals -(M_Pl^2/2) R_E + 6 M_Pl^2 (d beta)^2 - e^(-4 beta)(M_Pl^2 \
Lambda + V0 U) up to a total derivative (Euler-Lagrange expressions for N, a, \
beta vanish), M_Pl^2 = V0/kappa, V0 = b0^4 Lc^4\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918543082314`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1267]=",ExpressionUUID->"4028f5ce-be1c-8542-9073-ccdb39183124"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"radion on S^4: the same reduction for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) g_E - \
e^(2 beta) r0^2 gamma (unit-sphere gamma) holds with the additional potential \
-(M_Pl^2/2) e^(-4 beta) 12/(r0^2 e^(2 beta)) = -6 M_Pl^2 e^(-6 beta)/r0^2 \
from the curvature of the sphere, V0 = (8 Pi^2/3) r0^4; R is independent of \
the angles\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918546479855`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1268]=",ExpressionUUID->"c087de81-2bb5-f147-9710-44142eff0973"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"n extra dimensions (torus T^n, D = 4 + n, n = 1..4, Einstein \
frame e^(-n B) g_E): the kinetic term is (M_Pl^2/2)(n(n+2)/2)(dB)^2; with the \
note's B = beta_n phi, beta_n = Sqrt[2/(n(n+2))], it is (M_Pl^2/2)(d phi)^2, \
not (M_Pl^2/2)(1/2)(d phi)^2; the form with 1/2 needs beta_n = 1/Sqrt[n(n+2)]\
\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918555195656`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1272]=",ExpressionUUID->"ce14035a-9f25-414f-a9dd-48d9c0ab66c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the note's eight-dimensional values alpha = -1/Sqrt[3], beta = \
1/Sqrt[12]: 2 alpha + 4 beta == 0 (Einstein frame), 4 beta == 2/Sqrt[3] (V = \
V0 e^(4 beta phi)), and Sqrt[12] beta == 1, so M_Pl phi_note = Sqrt[12] M_Pl \
ln(b/b0) is the canonical radion of section 20.3\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918555195656`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1273]=",ExpressionUUID->"bb31fc9e-b327-9a45-b763-10e052bad93e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"general n: kinetic coefficient n(n+2)/2 for n = 1..4\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1.5`", ",", "4.`", ",", "7.5`", ",", "12.`"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"the note's beta_n^2 = 2/(n(n+2)) and the canonical \
1/(n(n+2)), n = 4\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.08333333333333333`", ",", "0.041666666666666664`"}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918555195656`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1274]=",ExpressionUUID->"b8533206-da35-fa4e-b0f9-243954193542"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.2 The potential of the radion on T\:2074 and on S\:2074, and its mass\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"21d761fe-4e2b-2e4e-bf87-2cf7e2a87834"],

Cell["\<\
Each term of the action scales with its own power of e^\[Beta] in the \
Einstein frame: the bulk cosmological constant and any energy density U(b) of \
the bulk as e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]), the curvature of the sphere and any \
gradient energy along the extra space as e^(\[Minus]6\[Beta]), a magnetic \
4-form flux through S\:2074 (a field that 7+1.nb does not contain, used here \
only as an illustration) as e^(\[Minus]12\[Beta]). With U(b) = U0 + U1 \
\[Beta] + (K_U/2) \[Beta]\.b2 (\[Beta] = ln(b/b0); section 20.3 has U1 = 0) \
the radion mass is m_r\.b2 = V\[DoublePrime](\[Phi]) = \
V\[DoublePrime](\[Beta])/(12 M_Pl\.b2). Four cases are checked, each in two \
independent ways \[LongDash] from the Einstein-frame potential V(\[Beta]), \
and from the eight-dimensional field equations: on S\:2074 the Einstein \
tensor gains (6, 6, 6, 6, 3, 3, 3, 3)/b\.b2 over the torus (for the \
cosmological metric with the sphere of radius b), R gains \[Minus]12/b\.b2, \
and the radion equation of section 20.3 becomes \[Beta]\[DoublePrime] + 3Ha \
\[Beta]\[Prime] + 4\[Beta]\[Prime]\.b2 = \[Kappa](\[Epsilon]/6 \[Minus] pa/2 \
+ pb/3) + \[CapitalLambda]/3 \[Minus] 3/b\.b2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7478dfef-8d0d-f34a-b3d6-e7a24ada3fa3"],

Cell["\<\
T\:2074 with U: a static flat four-dimensional vacuum at b = b0 needs \
\[CapitalLambda] + \[Kappa]U0 = 0 (with f_W = 0) and U1 = 0; m_r\.b2 = \
\[Kappa] K_U/12, as in section 20.3. Without U the torus is a MODULUS (V = 0 \
if \[CapitalLambda] = 0), or runs away (\[CapitalLambda] \[NotEqual] 0).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e0f49d77-36a6-c043-82f9-3cfc9ddea3d0"],

Cell["\<\
S\:2074 with U: the curvature must be balanced: \[CapitalLambda] + \[Kappa]U0 \
= 6/r0\.b2 and \[Kappa]U1 = \[Minus]12/r0\.b2, and the mass is m_r\.b2 = \
\[Kappa] K_U/12 \[Minus] 2/r0\.b2: a sphere needs a stiffer stabilizer than a \
torus.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"64a17512-dc10-2840-8d25-3de5511b6491"],

Cell["\<\
S\:2074 with \[CapitalLambda] only: dS4 \[Times] S\:2074 with r0\.b2 = 9/\
\[CapitalLambda] and H\.b2 = \[CapitalLambda]/9 = 1/r0\.b2 solves the \
eight-dimensional equations, but it sits at a MAXIMUM of V: m\.b2 = \
\[Minus]6H\.b2 (tachyonic) \[LongDash] the size of a sphere held by \
\[CapitalLambda] alone is unstable.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f2c83568-03b3-3144-a509-63c2bf62ec87"],

Cell["\<\
S\:2074 with a 4-form flux (Freund\[Dash]Rubin; illustration): Minkowski \
\[Times] S\:2074 needs \[CapitalLambda] = 9/(2r0\.b2) and \[Kappa]\[Rho]_F = \
3/(2r0\.b2) (\[Rho]_F the energy density of the flux, with pa = \
\[Minus]\[Rho]_F, pb = +\[Rho]_F), and the radion is stable, m\.b2 = 6/r0\.b2.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9de2efac-d9ec-7346-a277-9b10d9d20d70"],

Cell["\<\
The note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s eight-dimensional Goldberger\[Dash]Wise potential \
V(\[Phi]) = \[Integral]d\:2074y \[Sqrt]\[Gamma] e^(4\[Beta]\[Phi])[\.bd e^(\
\[Minus]2\[Beta]\[Phi])(\[Del]\[CapitalPhi])\.b2 + \.bd m8\.b2 \[CapitalPhi]\
\.b2] lacks the Einstein-frame factor e^(4\[Alpha]\[Phi]) = e^(\[Minus]8\
\[Beta]\[Phi]) of \[Sqrt]|G|: for a static profile \[CapitalPhi](y) the \
energy is e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta])\[Integral]d\:2074y \[Sqrt]\[Gamma] [\.bd e^(\
\[Minus]2\[Beta])|\[Del]\[CapitalPhi]|\.b2_\[Gamma] + \.bd m\.b2 \
\[CapitalPhi]\.b2] (e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]\[Phi]) in the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
notation) \[LongDash] the gradient part scales as e^(\[Minus]6\[Beta]), like \
the curvature, the mass part as e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]), like U.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d4c9fb31-aa0c-e744-8658-b2eb1a42d9e0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdES = rdEin[Join[{1, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2}, -b4[x0]^2 rdGam4], \
X]; rdET = rdEin[Diagonal[gCos], X];
check[\"the cosmological metric with the sphere of radius b(x0) (ds^2 = dx0^2 \
- a^2 dx.dx - b^2 dOmega_4^2): G^A_A = (torus value) + (6, 6, 6, 6, 3, 3, 3, \
3)/b^2 and R = (torus value) - 12/b^2\",
  toH[rdES - rdET] == {6, 6, 6, 6, 3, 3, 3, 3}/b4[x0]^2 && \
Simplify[toH[rdScal[Join[{1, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2, -a3[x0]^2}, -b4[x0]^2 \
rdGam4], X] - cvCos[\"R\"]] + 12/b4[x0]^2] === 0]
rdE00 = toH[rdES[[1]]] /. b4[x0] -> rdb; rdE11 = toH[rdES[[2]]] /. b4[x0] -> \
rdb; rdE44 = toH[rdES[[5]]] /. b4[x0] -> rdb;
rdSolS = First[Solve[{rdE11 - rdLam == -rdKap rdPa, rdE44 - rdLam == -rdKap \
rdPb}, {dHa, dHb}]];
rdRadS = Expand[(dHb /. rdSolS) /. Ha^2 -> (rdKap rdEps + rdLam - 12 Ha Hb - \
6 Hb^2 - 6/rdb^2)/3];
check[\"radion equation on S^4 (Einstein gravity; 11 and 44 equations with \
the 00 constraint): Hb' + 3 Ha Hb + 4 Hb^2 == kappa (eps/6 - pa/2 + pb/3) + \
Lambda/3 - 3/b^2\",
  Simplify[rdE00 - (3 (Ha^2 + 4 Ha Hb + 2 Hb^2) + 6/rdb^2)] === 0 && \
Simplify[rdRadS - (-3 Ha Hb - 4 Hb^2 + rdKap (rdEps/6 - rdPa/2 + rdPb/3) + \
rdLam/3 - 3/rdb^2)] === 0]
rdUq = rdU0 + rdU1 rdBe + rdKU/2 rdBe^2;
rdV[curv_, flux_] := rdMP2 (E^(-4 rdBe) (rdLam + rdKap rdUq) - curv 6 E^(-6 \
rdBe)/rdR0^2 + flux E^(-12 rdBe));
rdRHS[eps_, pa_, pb_, lam_] := rdKap (eps/6 - pa/2 + pb/3) + lam/3 - \
3/(rdR0^2 E^(2 rdBe));
rdSolT = Solve[{(rdV[0, 0] /. rdBe -> 0) == 0, (D[rdV[0, 0], rdBe] /. rdBe -> \
0) == 0}, {rdLam, rdU1}];
check[\"radion on T^4 with U = U0 + U1 beta + (K_U/2) beta^2: a flat vacuum \
at b = b0 needs Lambda + kappa U0 = 0 and U1 = 0, and m_r^2 = V''(beta)/(12 \
M_Pl^2) = kappa K_U/12 (section 20.3)\",
  Length[rdSolT] == 1 && Simplify[(rdLam /. First[rdSolT]) + rdKap rdU0] === \
0 && (rdU1 /. First[rdSolT]) === 0 &&
  Simplify[(D[rdV[0, 0], {rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0)/(12 rdMP2) /. \
First[rdSolT]] === rdKap rdKU/12]
rdSolS2 = First[Solve[{(rdV[1, 0] /. rdBe -> 0) == 0, (D[rdV[1, 0], rdBe] /. \
rdBe -> 0) == 0}, {rdLam, rdU1}]];
rdUb = rdUq /. rdSolS2; rdR2 = rdRHS[rdUb, -rdUb, -rdUb - D[rdUb, rdBe]/4, \
rdLam /. rdSolS2];
check[\"radion on S^4 with U: Lambda + kappa U0 == 6/r0^2, kappa U1 == \
-12/r0^2 and m_r^2 == kappa K_U/12 - 2/r0^2 from V(beta); the \
eight-dimensional radion equation gives the same static solution and the same \
mass\",
  Simplify[(rdLam /. rdSolS2) + rdKap rdU0 - 6/rdR0^2] === 0 && \
Simplify[rdKap (rdU1 /. rdSolS2) + 12/rdR0^2] === 0 &&
  Simplify[(D[rdV[1, 0], {rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0)/(12 rdMP2) /. rdSolS2] === \
Simplify[rdKap rdKU/12 - 2/rdR0^2] &&
  Simplify[rdR2 /. rdBe -> 0] === 0 && Simplify[-(D[rdR2, rdBe] /. rdBe -> 0) \
- (rdKap rdKU/12 - 2/rdR0^2)] === 0]
rdVL = rdV[1, 0] /. {rdU0 -> 0, rdU1 -> 0, rdKU -> 0}; rdLamL = rdLam /. \
First[Solve[(D[rdVL, rdBe] /. rdBe -> 0) == 0, rdLam]];
rdHE2 = Simplify[(rdVL /. rdBe -> 0 /. rdLam -> rdLamL)/(3 rdMP2)]; rdM2L = \
Simplify[(D[rdVL, {rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0 /. rdLam -> rdLamL)/(12 rdMP2)];
rdDS = {rdE00, rdE11, rdE44} /. {Ha -> 1/rdR0, Hb -> 0, dHa -> 0, dHb -> 0, \
rdb -> rdR0};
check[\"S^4 with Lambda only: dS4 x S^4 with r0^2 = 9/Lambda, H^2 = 1/r0^2 = \
Lambda/9 solves the 00, 11 and 44 equations; it is a MAXIMUM of V: m^2 = -6 \
H^2 from V(beta), and m^2 = -6/r0^2 = -6 H^2 from the eight-dimensional \
radion equation\",
  Simplify[rdLamL rdR0^2] === 9 && Simplify[rdHE2 rdR0^2] === 1 && \
Simplify[rdM2L/rdHE2] === -6 &&
  Simplify[rdDS - 9/rdR0^2] === {0, 0, 0} && Simplify[rdRHS[0, 0, 0, \
9/rdR0^2] /. rdBe -> 0] === 0 &&
  Simplify[-(D[rdRHS[0, 0, 0, 9/rdR0^2], rdBe] /. rdBe -> 0) rdR0^2] === -6]
rdVF = rdV[1, rdFx] /. {rdU0 -> 0, rdU1 -> 0, rdKU -> 0}; rdSolF = \
First[Solve[{(rdVF /. rdBe -> 0) == 0, (D[rdVF, rdBe] /. rdBe -> 0) == 0}, \
{rdLam, rdFx}]];
rdStF = feStress[Function[{aa, rIIIbb}, aa^3 rIIIbb^4 rdQ2/(2 rIIIbb^8)]];
rdRhoF = (rdFx /. rdSolF)/rdKap E^(-8 rdBe);
check[\"S^4 with a 4-form flux (illustration; W = a^3 b^4 q^2/(2 b^8) gives \
eps = rho_F, pa = -rho_F, pb = +rho_F): Minkowski x S^4 needs Lambda = 9/(2 \
r0^2) and kappa rho_F = 3/(2 r0^2); m^2 = 6/r0^2 from V(beta) and from the \
eight-dimensional radion equation\",
  Simplify[rdStF - rdQ2/(2 bS^8) {1, -1, 1}] === {0, 0, 0} && Simplify[(rdLam \
/. rdSolF) rdR0^2] === 9/2 && Simplify[(rdFx /. rdSolF) rdR0^2] === 3/2 &&
  Simplify[(D[rdVF, {rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0 /. rdSolF) rdR0^2/(12 rdMP2)] === \
6 &&
  Simplify[rdRHS[rdRhoF, -rdRhoF, rdRhoF, rdLam /. rdSolF] /. rdBe -> 0] === \
0 && Simplify[-(D[rdRHS[rdRhoF, -rdRhoF, rdRhoF, rdLam /. rdSolF], rdBe] /. \
rdBe -> 0) rdR0^2] === 6]
rdGdS = Join[{rdLp[x0]^2 E^(-4 rdBt[x0])}, -rdSa[x0]^2 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) {1, 1, \
1}, -rdR0^2 E^(2 rdBt[x0]) rdGam4];
rdSqG = rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) rdR0^4 Sin[x4]^3 Sin[x5]^2 Sin[x6];
check[\"the note's Goldberger-Wise potential in eight dimensions: for a \
static profile Phi(y) (here Phi(x4, x5)) Sqrt|G| (1/2 G^AB dPhi dPhi - 1/2 \
m^2 Phi^2) == -N a^3 e^(-4 beta) Sqrt[gamma] (1/2 e^(-2 beta) |grad \
Phi|^2_gamma + 1/2 m^2 Phi^2): the Einstein-frame factor is e^(-4 beta) \
(e^(-4 beta phi) in the note's notation), not e^(+4 beta phi)\",
  Simplify[rdSqG (1/2 Sum[D[rdPhi[x4, x5], X[[i]]]^2/rdGdS[[i]], {i, 5, 8}] - \
1/2 rdMm^2 rdPhi[x4, x5]^2) +
     rdLp[x0] rdSa[x0]^3 E^(-4 rdBt[x0]) rdR0^4 Sin[x4]^3 Sin[x5]^2 Sin[x6] \
(1/2 E^(-2 rdBt[x0]) Sum[D[rdPhi[x4, x5], X[[i]]]^2/(rdR0^2 rdGam4[[i - 4]]), \
{i, 5, 8}] + 1/2 rdMm^2 rdPhi[x4, x5]^2)] === 0]
{\"sphere with U: Lambda + kappa U0, kappa U1, m_r^2 - kappa K_U/12 (units \
1/r0^2)\" -> Simplify[{((rdLam /. rdSolS2) + rdKap rdU0) rdR0^2, rdKap (rdU1 \
/. rdSolS2) rdR0^2,
    (((D[rdV[1, 0], {rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0)/(12 rdMP2) /. rdSolS2) - rdKap \
rdKU/12) rdR0^2}],
 \"sphere with Lambda only: Lambda r0^2, H^2 r0^2, m^2/H^2\" -> {rdLamL \
rdR0^2, rdHE2 rdR0^2, rdM2L/rdHE2} // Simplify,
 \"sphere with a 4-form flux: Lambda r0^2, kappa rho_F r0^2, m^2 r0^2\" -> \
N[Simplify[{(rdLam /. rdSolF) rdR0^2, (rdFx /. rdSolF) rdR0^2, (D[rdVF, \
{rdBe, 2}] /. rdBe -> 0 /. rdSolF) rdR0^2/(12 rdMP2)}]]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1275]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4187ffee-b91d-124a-9abb-4470de9d729e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the cosmological metric with the sphere of radius b(x0) (ds^2 = \
dx0^2 - a^2 dx.dx - b^2 dOmega_4^2): G^A_A = (torus value) + (6, 6, 6, 6, 3, \
3, 3, 3)/b^2 and R = (torus value) - 12/b^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918556800632`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1276]=",ExpressionUUID->"103eb2d6-5009-1d46-ba59-b16770ee049d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"radion equation on S^4 (Einstein gravity; 11 and 44 equations \
with the 00 constraint): Hb' + 3 Ha Hb + 4 Hb^2 == kappa (eps/6 - pa/2 + \
pb/3) + Lambda/3 - 3/b^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855694063*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1280]=",ExpressionUUID->"b1742379-ff39-f847-ad08-45677f778de7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"radion on T^4 with U = U0 + U1 beta + (K_U/2) beta^2: a flat \
vacuum at b = b0 needs Lambda + kappa U0 = 0 and U1 = 0, and m_r^2 = \
V''(beta)/(12 M_Pl^2) = kappa K_U/12 (section 20.3)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918556960735`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1285]=",ExpressionUUID->"66835e25-10c5-684f-8111-e99655ccab10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"radion on S^4 with U: Lambda + kappa U0 == 6/r0^2, kappa U1 == \
-12/r0^2 and m_r^2 == kappa K_U/12 - 2/r0^2 from V(beta); the \
eight-dimensional radion equation gives the same static solution and the same \
mass\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855697077*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1288]=",ExpressionUUID->"1c169e4d-13e1-ea4b-be59-0c6f35b92b59"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"S^4 with Lambda only: dS4 x S^4 with r0^2 = 9/Lambda, H^2 = \
1/r0^2 = Lambda/9 solves the 00, 11 and 44 equations; it is a MAXIMUM of V: \
m^2 = -6 H^2 from V(beta), and m^2 = -6/r0^2 = -6 H^2 from the \
eight-dimensional radion equation\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918556980705`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1292]=",ExpressionUUID->"626131ba-fb1a-814e-9794-eda79e48d8d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"S^4 with a 4-form flux (illustration; W = a^3 b^4 q^2/(2 b^8) \
gives eps = rho_F, pa = -rho_F, pb = +rho_F): Minkowski x S^4 needs Lambda = \
9/(2 r0^2) and kappa rho_F = 3/(2 r0^2); m^2 = 6/r0^2 from V(beta) and from \
the eight-dimensional radion equation\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918557000713`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1296]=",ExpressionUUID->"49be8dd3-54b4-c04e-9d89-87ce78bbfd9f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the note's Goldberger-Wise potential in eight dimensions: for a \
static profile Phi(y) (here Phi(x4, x5)) Sqrt|G| (1/2 G^AB dPhi dPhi - 1/2 \
m^2 Phi^2) == -N a^3 e^(-4 beta) Sqrt[gamma] (1/2 e^(-2 beta) |grad \
Phi|^2_gamma + 1/2 m^2 Phi^2): the Einstein-frame factor is e^(-4 beta) \
(e^(-4 beta phi) in the note's notation), not e^(+4 beta phi)\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855702072*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1299]=",ExpressionUUID->"907e9216-41ad-894c-82bf-51320cd1f159"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"sphere with U: Lambda + kappa U0, kappa U1, m_r^2 - kappa \
K_U/12 (units 1/r0^2)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"6", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "12"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"sphere with Lambda only: Lambda r0^2, H^2 r0^2, m^2/H^2\"\>", 
    "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"9", ",", "1", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "6"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"sphere with a 4-form flux: Lambda r0^2, kappa rho_F r0^2, m^2 \
r0^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"4.5`", ",", "1.5`", ",", "6.`"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918557030716`*^9},
