Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.3 The radion meets the world brane: coupling, fifth force, \
E\[ODoubleDot]t-Wash\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"21cdc6cb-ae8e-504d-b554-61bb57c95766"],

Cell["\<\
At the brane the induced metric is h = e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta]) g_E, on T\:2074 \
and on S\:2074 alike (the factor depends only on n = 4). A particle of mass M \
at rest on the brane has the action \[Minus]M \[Integral] d\[Tau] \[Sqrt](h_\
\[Mu]\[Nu] \:1e8b^\[Mu] \:1e8b^\[Nu]) = \[Minus]M \[Integral] dx0 \
e^(\[Minus]2\[Beta]) = \[Minus]M \[Integral] dx0 (1 \[Minus] 2\[Beta] + \
\[Ellipsis]): with \[Beta] = \[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]12 M_Pl) the coupling is \
(\[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl)) T^\[Mu]_\[Mu] (T^\[Mu]_\[Mu] = M for the particle), \
the coupling of section 20.3. For n extra dimensions h = e^(\[Minus]n\[Beta]) \
g_E and the coupling is \[Sqrt](n/(2(n+2)))/M_Pl. A massless radion then adds \
to Newton\[CloseCurlyQuote]s potential a force of the same range with the \
strength \[Alpha] = 2 (coupling \[Times] M_Pl)\.b2 = n/(n+2) = 2/3 \
\[LongDash] the FIFTH FORCE of the note (sections 25.4 and the factor 5/3 = 1 \
+ 2/3 of the image sum). The E\[ODoubleDot]t-Wash torsion balance (J. G. Lee \
et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 124 (2020) 101101) excludes gravitational-strength \
(|\[Alpha]| = 1) Yukawa forces with a range \[Lambda] > 38.6 \[Mu]m (95% CL); \
a radion of strength 2/3 must therefore be heavier than about \:0127c/38.6 \
\[Mu]m \[TildeTilde] 5 meV. The 10 GeV radion of sections 22\[Dash]24 has the \
range \:0127c/(10 GeV) = 2.0 \[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\:2077 m. In warped models \
the radion couples with 1/\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket] (TeV) \
and mixes with the Higgs boson through the parameter \[Gamma] = v/\
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket] (Giudice, Rattazzi and Wells); \
in 7+1 the scale is \[Sqrt]3 M_Pl, so \[Gamma] = v/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"72dd4970-d0b9-904c-94bf-d2895a7f3036"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdPP = Series[-rdMs E^(-rdNn rdBe/2), {rdBe, 0, 1}] // Normal;
check[\"the radion couples to a mass M on the brane as (phi/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl)) \
M: -M e^(-n beta/2) = -M + (n/2) M beta + ..., with beta = phi/(M_Pl Sqrt[n \
(n + 2)/2]) the coupling is Sqrt[n/(2 (n + 2))]/M_Pl = 1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl) for n \
= 4, and the fifth-force strength 2 (coupling M_Pl)^2 = n/(n + 2) = 2/3\",
  Simplify[rdPP - (-rdMs + rdNn rdMs rdBe/2)] === 0 && \
Simplify[((rdNn/2)/Sqrt[rdNn (rdNn + 2)/2])^2 - rdNn/(2 (rdNn + 2)), rdNn > \
0] === 0 &&
  ((4/2)/Sqrt[4 (4 + 2)/2])^2 == 1/3 && Simplify[2 rdNn/(2 (rdNn + 2)) - \
rdNn/(rdNn + 2)] === 0 && 4/(4 + 2) == 2/3]
rdEW = {tbHbarCm/38.6*^-6 10^9, tbHbarCm/10., vEW/(Sqrt[3] rIIMPl)};
check[\"Eot-Wash (|alpha| = 1 excluded for lambda > 38.6 micrometres): a \
radion of strength 2/3 must be heavier than about hbar c/38.6 micrometres = \
5.1 meV; the 10 GeV radion has the range 2.0 10^-17 m; Higgs-radion mixing in \
7+1 is governed by gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl) = 5.8 10^-17\",
  Abs[rdEW[[1]]/5.112*^-3 - 1] < 10^-3 && Abs[rdEW[[2]]/1.9733*^-17 - 1] < \
10^-4 && Abs[rdEW[[3]]/5.838*^-17 - 1] < 10^-3]
{\"Eot-Wash bound on the radion mass (eV), range of a 10 GeV radion (m), \
gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl)\" -> rdEW}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1301]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cf2381a8-bf7c-8042-93db-938ef7ef0a36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the radion couples to a mass M on the brane as (phi/(Sqrt[3] \
M_Pl)) M: -M e^(-n beta/2) = -M + (n/2) M beta + ..., with beta = phi/(M_Pl \
Sqrt[n (n + 2)/2]) the coupling is Sqrt[n/(2 (n + 2))]/M_Pl = 1/(Sqrt[3] \
M_Pl) for n = 4, and the fifth-force strength 2 (coupling M_Pl)^2 = n/(n + 2) \
= 2/3\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855710436*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1302]=",ExpressionUUID->"aa2edbce-a5e7-3247-88e7-ea1fa4704e85"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Eot-Wash (|alpha| = 1 excluded for lambda > 38.6 micrometres): \
a radion of strength 2/3 must be heavier than about hbar c/38.6 micrometres = \
5.1 meV; the 10 GeV radion has the range 2.0 10^-17 m; Higgs-radion mixing in \
7+1 is governed by gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl) = 5.8 10^-17\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855710436*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1304]=",ExpressionUUID->"da51ff89-cc26-824e-8f57-1119a54883a3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Eot-Wash bound on the radion mass (eV), range of a 10 GeV \
radion (m), gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "0.005112097937823834`", ",", "1.973269804`*^-17", ",", 
     "5.837986676464506`*^-17"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191855710436*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1305]=",ExpressionUUID->"72270f06-bfdb-b846-9035-4e7fcbc3df44"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.4 The 4-sphere and the 4-torus side by side: levels, the brane, \
dirac16complex\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"12ad10f2-0691-f242-b8c3-f2af4f4da2e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Kaluza\[Dash]Klein levels of a scalar. T\:2074: \[Mu] = 2\[Pi]|n|/",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] with the multiplicity r_4(k) (section 25.3). S\:2074 of radius r: \
the eigenvalues of \[Minus]\[CapitalDelta] are l(l+3)/r\.b2, l = 0, 1, 2, \
\[Ellipsis], with the multiplicity d_l = (2l+3)(l+1)(l+2)/6 (the harmonic \
polynomials of degree l in five variables: C(l+4, 4) \[Minus] C(l+2, 4)). \
Both obey Weyl\[CloseCurlyQuote]s law N(\[Mu]) \[TildeTilde] V \
\[Mu]\:2074/(32\[Pi]\.b2); for S\:2074 this is (\[Mu]r)\:2074/12. The brane \
at the north pole x4 = 0 sees, at each level l, only the ZONAL harmonic Z_l = \
\[Sqrt](d_l/V) C_l^(3/2)(cos x4)/C_l^(3/2)(1) (C the Gegenbauer polynomial, \
C_l^(3/2)(1) = (l+1)(l+2)/2); all other harmonics of the level vanish there. \
So the brane couples to ONE state per level, with the strength \[Sqrt](d_l/V) \
\[LongDash] on T\:2074 the brane couples to the combination \
\[CapitalSigma]_{|n|\.b2=k} \[Phi]_n of each level, with the strength \
\[Sqrt](r_4(k)/V). The symmetry: S\:2074 has the 10 Killing vectors of SO(5); \
the brane keeps the 6 of SO(4) (the rotations that fix the north pole) and \
breaks 4 \[LongDash] on T\:2074 the brane keeps the 384 signed permutations \
and breaks the 4 translations."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65658f2a-3cb1-c842-83d1-22b80546256a"],

Cell["\<\
dirac16complex. On T\:2074 with periodic spinors the Dirac operator of the \
extra space has zero modes: four massless brane Dirac fermions for m = 0 \
(section 25). On S\:2074 it has none: Killing spinors \[Epsilon]\[PlusMinus] \
(\[Del]_i \[Epsilon]\[PlusMinus] = \[PlusMinus](i/(2r)) \[Gamma]\:0303_i \
\[Epsilon]\[PlusMinus], \[Gamma]\:0303_a = i \[Rho]_(a+3) Hermitian, \[Gamma]\
\:0303_a\[Gamma]\:0303_b + \[Gamma]\:0303_b\[Gamma]\:0303_a = 2\[Delta]_ab) \
have D\:0338\[Epsilon]\[PlusMinus] = \[PlusMinus](2i/r) \
\[Epsilon]\[PlusMinus], the lowest eigenvalue allowed by Friedrich\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s bound \[Lambda]\.b2 \[GreaterEqual] n R/(4(n\[Minus]1)) = \
4/r\.b2; the spectrum is \[PlusMinus]i(l+2)/r with the degeneracy 4\
\[CenterDot]C(l+3, 3) for each sign (R. Camporesi and A. Higuchi, J. Geom. \
Phys. 20 (1996) 1). The Kaluza\[Dash]Klein masses of dirac16complex are \
\[Sqrt](m\.b2 + \[Lambda]\.b2) on both spaces; the lightest level on S\:2074 \
has \[Lambda] = 2/r: eight Dirac fermions of mass \[Sqrt](m\.b2 + 4/r\.b2). \
With the same volume V\[UpTee] = M_Pl\.b2/M8\:2076 (the same four-dimensional \
Newton constant) the sphere has the radius r = \
(3V\[UpTee]/(8\[Pi]\.b2))^(1/4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"775f8e5e-9077-8a49-a6ea-aa1483dd9ad1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdDl[l_] := (2 l + 3) (l + 1) (l + 2)/6;
rdZon[l_] := GegenbauerC[l, 3/2, Cos[x4]];
check[\"zonal harmonics on S^4 (l = 0..6, exact): (1/sin^3 x4) d/dx4 (sin^3 \
x4 d/dx4 C_l^(3/2)(cos x4)) == -l (l + 3) C_l^(3/2), C_l^(3/2)(1) == (l + \
1)(l + 2)/2, and Int over S^4 of (C_l/C_l(1))^2 == V/d_l (unit sphere), so \
the normalized zonal harmonic is Sqrt[d_l/V] at the north pole; d_l == \
Binomial[l + 4, 4] - Binomial[l + 2, 4] for l = 0..20\",
  And @@ Table[Simplify[D[Sin[x4]^3 D[rdZon[l], x4], x4]/Sin[x4]^3 + l (l + \
3) rdZon[l]] === 0 && GegenbauerC[l, 3/2, 1] == (l + 1) (l + 2)/2 &&
     2 Pi^2 Integrate[Expand[(rdZon[l]/GegenbauerC[l, 3/2, 1])^2 Sin[x4]^3], \
{x4, 0, Pi}] == (8 Pi^2/3)/rdDl[l], {l, 0, 6}] &&
  And @@ Table[rdDl[l] == Binomial[l + 4, 4] - Binomial[l + 2, 4], {l, 0, 20}]]
rdNS4[x_] := Total[rdDl /@ Select[Range[0, Ceiling[x] + 2], # (# + 3) <= x^2 \
&]];
rdWeyl = Table[N[rdNS4[x]/(x^4/12) - 1], {x, {10, 100, 1000}}];
check[\"Weyl's law on S^4: the number of levels with l(l + 3) <= (mu r)^2 \
approaches (mu r)^4/12 = V mu^4/(32 Pi^2) (V = 8 Pi^2 r^4/3): relative \
deviation -1.0 10^-2, -1.0 10^-4, -1.0 10^-6 at mu r = 10, 100, 1000 (like \
-1/(mu r)^2)\",
  Abs[rdWeyl[[1]] + 1/100] < 10^-6 && Abs[rdWeyl[[2]] + 1/10^4] < 10^-8 && \
Abs[rdWeyl[[3]] + 1/10^6] < 10^-10 && Simplify[(8 Pi^2/3) rdR0^4/(32 Pi^2) - \
rdR0^4/12] === 0]
rdEmb = rdR0 {Sin[x4] Sin[x5] Sin[x6] Cos[x7], Sin[x4] Sin[x5] Sin[x6] \
Sin[x7], Sin[x4] Sin[x5] Cos[x6], Sin[x4] Cos[x5], Cos[x4]};
rdJe = Table[D[rdEmb[[a]], X[[i]]], {a, 5}, {i, 5, 8}];
check[\"the brane at the north pole of S^4: the embedding (r0 sin x4 sin x5 \
sin x6 cos x7, ..., r0 cos x4) of S^4 in R^5 induces r0^2 gamma; the north \
pole x4 = 0 is (0, 0, 0, 0, r0); of the 10 rotations L_ab of R^5 (the Killing \
vectors of S^4, SO(5)) the 6 with a, b <= 4 vanish there (SO(4), kept by the \
brane) and the 4 L_a5 move it\",
  Simplify[Transpose[rdJe].rdJe - rdR0^2 DiagonalMatrix[rdGam4]] === \
ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}] && (rdEmb /. x4 -> 0) === {0, 0, 0, 0, rdR0} &&
  Count[Subsets[Range[5], {2}], {a_, b_} /; (UnitVector[5, 5][[a]] \
UnitVector[5, b] - UnitVector[5, 5][[b]] UnitVector[5, a]) == {0, 0, 0, 0, \
0}] == 6 &&
  Length[Subsets[Range[5], {2}]] == 10]
rdGt = I rhoK; rdHf = rdR0 {1, Sin[x4], Sin[x4] Sin[x5], Sin[x4] Sin[x5] \
Sin[x6]};
rdOm[mu_, i_, j_] := If[mu == i, D[rdHf[[i]], X[[4 + j]]]/rdHf[[j]], 0] - \
If[mu == j, D[rdHf[[j]], X[[4 + i]]]/rdHf[[i]], 0];
rdNab[M_, mu_] := D[M, X[[4 + mu]]] + Sum[If[i != j, rdOm[mu, i, j] \
rdGt[[i]].rdGt[[j]]/4, 0], {i, 4}, {j, 4}].M;
rdKS[s_] := (Cos[x4/2] ID4 + s I Sin[x4/2] rdGt[[1]]).(Cos[x5/2] ID4 + \
Sin[x5/2] rdGt[[1]].rdGt[[2]]).(Cos[x6/2] ID4 + Sin[x6/2] rdGt[[2]].rdGt[[3]]).
   (Cos[x7/2] ID4 + Sin[x7/2] rdGt[[3]].rdGt[[4]]);
rdZeroQ[m_] := Simplify[TrigExpand[m /. {x4 -> 2 rdv4, x5 -> 2 rdv5, x6 -> 2 \
rdv6, x7 -> 2 rdv7}]] === ConstantArray[0, Dimensions[m]];      (* half \
angles *)
check[\"Killing spinors of S^4 (radius r0, frame e^a = (r0, r0 sin x4, ...) \
dx^(a+3), gt_a = I rho_(a+3)): eps_s = exp(s (i/2) x4 gt_1) exp((1/2) x5 gt_1 \
gt_2) exp((1/2) x6 gt_2 gt_3) exp((1/2) x7 gt_3 gt_4) eps0 satisfies nabla_mu \
eps_s == s (i/(2 r0)) e_mu^a gt_a eps_s (s = +-1, all eps0), so the Dirac \
operator gives (2 s i/r0) eps_s: |lambda| = 2/r0, Friedrich's bound n R/(4(n \
- 1)) = 4/r0^2\",
  And @@ Table[rdGt[[a]] == ConjugateTranspose[rdGt[[a]]], {a, 4}] && And @@ \
Flatten[Table[rdGt[[a]].rdGt[[b]] + rdGt[[b]].rdGt[[a]] == 2 \
KroneckerDelta[a, b] ID4, {a, 4}, {b, 4}]] &&
  And @@ Flatten[Table[rdZeroQ[rdNab[rdKS[s], mu] - s I/(2 rdR0) rdHf[[mu]] \
rdGt[[mu]].rdKS[s]], {s, {1, -1}}, {mu, 4}]] &&
  And @@ Table[rdZeroQ[Sum[rdGt[[a]].rdNab[rdKS[s], a]/rdHf[[a]], {a, 4}] - s \
2 I/rdR0 rdKS[s]], {s, {1, -1}}] &&
  4 (12/rdR0^2)/(4 (4 - 1)) == (2/rdR0)^2]
rdSpW = N[Total[Table[2 4 Binomial[l + 3, 3], {l, 0, 998}]]/(1000^4/3) - 1];
check[\"Dirac spectrum on S^4: Weyl's law for spinors (4 components) \
N(|lambda| <= L/r) ~ 4 V (L/r)^4/(32 Pi^2) = L^4/3 agrees with the \
degeneracies 2 x 4 Binomial[l + 3, 3] of the eigenvalues +-i(l + 2)/r (to 2.0 \
10^-3 at L = 1000)\",
  Abs[rdSpW] < 5*^-3 && Simplify[4 (8 Pi^2/3) rdR0^4/(32 Pi^2) - rdR0^4/3] \
=== 0]
rdRS4 = (3 rIIVp/(8 Pi^2))^(1/4);
rdToday = {rdRS4, rdRS4 tbHbarCm, 2 Pi/tbLp 10^3, 2/rdRS4 10^3, 2/rdRS4 10^3, \
1 + Total[rIIr4], rdNS4[5 rdRS4], tbNmu[5.]};
check[\"the sphere with the volume of the torus today (V = M_Pl^2/M8^6): r = \
(3 V/(8 Pi^2))^(1/4) = 688.9 GeV^-1 = 1.359 10^-13 m; lowest scalar levels \
4.03 MeV (torus, 8 states) and 2.90 MeV (sphere, l = 1, 5 states); lowest \
dirac16complex level on the sphere 2/r = 2.90 MeV (8 Dirac fermions; the \
torus has 4 massless ones for m = 0); levels below 5 GeV: torus 1.17335 \
10^13, sphere 1.17375 10^13, Weyl 1.17335 10^13\",
  Abs[rdToday[[1]]/688.94 - 1] < 10^-4 && Abs[rdToday[[4]]/2.903 - 1] < 10^-3 \
&& Abs[rdToday[[7]]/rdToday[[8]] - 1] < 10^-3 && \
Abs[rdToday[[6]]/rdToday[[8]] - 1] < 10^-4 &&
  rdDl[1] == 5 && 2 4 Binomial[3, 3] == 8]
{\"S^4 multiplicities d_l, l = 0..8\" -> Table[rdDl[l], {l, 0, 8}], \"S^4 \
Weyl: N(x)/(x^4/12) - 1 at x = mu r = 10, 100, 1000\" -> rdWeyl,
 \"Dirac on S^4: degeneracy 4 Binomial[l + 3, 3] of +i(l + 2)/r, l = 0..5; \
Weyl ratio - 1 at L = 1000\" -> Join[Table[4 Binomial[l + 3, 3], {l, 0, 5}], \
{rdSpW}],
 \"today: r_S4 (GeV^-1, m), lowest masses (MeV): torus 2 Pi/l_perp, sphere \
scalar 2/r, sphere dirac16complex 2/r; levels below 5 GeV: torus lattice, \
sphere exact, Weyl\" -> rdToday}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1306]:=",ExpressionUUID->"72a6b364-3531-f141-bb21-5a482f0188b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"zonal harmonics on S^4 (l = 0..6, exact): (1/sin^3 x4) d/dx4 \
(sin^3 x4 d/dx4 C_l^(3/2)(cos x4)) == -l (l + 3) C_l^(3/2), C_l^(3/2)(1) == \
(l + 1)(l + 2)/2, and Int over S^4 of (C_l/C_l(1))^2 == V/d_l (unit sphere), \
so the normalized zonal harmonic is Sqrt[d_l/V] at the north pole; d_l == \
Binomial[l + 4, 4] - Binomial[l + 2, 4] for l = 0..20\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918570786057`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1308]=",ExpressionUUID->"e1e9db29-4a50-0146-8934-a13cae493ac8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Weyl's law on S^4: the number of levels with l(l + 3) <= (mu \
r)^2 approaches (mu r)^4/12 = V mu^4/(32 Pi^2) (V = 8 Pi^2 r^4/3): relative \
deviation -1.0 10^-2, -1.0 10^-4, -1.0 10^-6 at mu r = 10, 100, 1000 (like \
-1/(mu r)^2)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918570786057`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1311]=",ExpressionUUID->"540da1ff-60a2-7d4d-9250-e6e625be1b6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the brane at the north pole of S^4: the embedding (r0 sin x4 \
sin x5 sin x6 cos x7, ..., r0 cos x4) of S^4 in R^5 induces r0^2 gamma; the \
north pole x4 = 0 is (0, 0, 0, 0, r0); of the 10 rotations L_ab of R^5 (the \
Killing vectors of S^4, SO(5)) the 6 with a, b <= 4 vanish there (SO(4), kept \
by the brane) and the 4 L_a5 move it\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918570964375`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1314]=",ExpressionUUID->"9d69b502-e5cb-8343-8caa-995993ae08f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Killing spinors of S^4 (radius r0, frame e^a = (r0, r0 sin x4, \
...) dx^(a+3), gt_a = I rho_(a+3)): eps_s = exp(s (i/2) x4 gt_1) exp((1/2) x5 \
gt_1 gt_2) exp((1/2) x6 gt_2 gt_3) exp((1/2) x7 gt_3 gt_4) eps0 satisfies \
nabla_mu eps_s == s (i/(2 r0)) e_mu^a gt_a eps_s (s = +-1, all eps0), so the \
Dirac operator gives (2 s i/r0) eps_s: |lambda| = 2/r0, Friedrich's bound n \
R/(4(n - 1)) = 4/r0^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191857528351*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1320]=",ExpressionUUID->"e03c56c2-3c79-354d-af2c-bca2808cb300"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Dirac spectrum on S^4: Weyl's law for spinors (4 components) \
N(|lambda| <= L/r) ~ 4 V (L/r)^4/(32 Pi^2) = L^4/3 agrees with the \
degeneracies 2 x 4 Binomial[l + 3, 3] of the eigenvalues +-i(l + 2)/r (to 2.0 \
10^-3 at L = 1000)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191857530346*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1322]=",ExpressionUUID->"593dc35b-e273-404e-9305-f2ecaa3d3f5f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the sphere with the volume of the torus today (V = \
M_Pl^2/M8^6): r = (3 V/(8 Pi^2))^(1/4) = 688.9 GeV^-1 = 1.359 10^-13 m; \
lowest scalar levels 4.03 MeV (torus, 8 states) and 2.90 MeV (sphere, l = 1, \
5 states); lowest dirac16complex level on the sphere 2/r = 2.90 MeV (8 Dirac \
fermions; the torus has 4 massless ones for m = 0); levels below 5 GeV: torus \
1.17335 10^13, sphere 1.17375 10^13, Weyl 1.17335 10^13\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191857540346*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1325]=",ExpressionUUID->"399402b8-076b-e245-a191-b620ec8eaeae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"S^4 multiplicities d_l, l = 0..8\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1", ",", "5", ",", "14", ",", "30", ",", "55", ",", "91", ",", "140", ",",
       "204", ",", "285"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
