Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.5 Flat versus warped: the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Randall\[Dash]Sundrum \
example, checked\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5c95e96a-679d-9c45-a1f4-975602cd06b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s warped radion is the five-dimensional model of \
Randall and Sundrum (RS1): ds\.b2 = e^(\[Minus]2A(y)) \[Eta]_\[Mu]\[Nu] dx^\
\[Mu] dx^\[Nu] \[Minus] dy\.b2, y \[Element] [\[Minus]\[Pi]R, \[Pi]R] with y \
\[TildeEqual] \[Minus]y, branes at y = 0 (UV) and y = \[Pi]R (IR). With the \
conventions of 7+1.nb (G^A_B \[Minus] \[CapitalLambda] \[Delta]^A_B = \
\[Kappa] T^A_B) the Einstein tensor is G^\[Mu]_\[Nu] = 3A\[DoublePrime] \
\[Minus] 6A\[Prime]\.b2, G^y_y = \[Minus]6A\[Prime]\.b2. In the bulk A = k|y| \
gives \[CapitalLambda] = \[Minus]6k\.b2 (anti-de Sitter); at the branes the \
slope A\[Prime] jumps by +2k (UV: from \[Minus]k to +k) and by \[Minus]2k \
(IR), so A\[DoublePrime] = \[PlusMinus]2k \[Delta], and a brane tension f (T^\
\[Mu]_\[Nu] = f \[Delta](y) \[Delta]^\[Mu]_\[Nu]) requires f_UV = \
+6k/\[Kappa] and f_IR = \[Minus]6k/\[Kappa] \[LongDash] the UV brane has \
POSITIVE tension, as the note states first (\[Lambda]_A = \[Minus]\[Lambda]_B \
= 6k/\[Kappa]8\.b2); its later Israel-junction computation reverses both \
signs. The four-dimensional Planck mass is M_Pl\.b2 = (1 \[Minus] \
e^(\[Minus]2\[Pi]kR))/(\[Kappa]k). Promoting R to a field T(x) (ds\.b2 = e^(\
\[Minus]2kT|y|) g \[Minus] T\.b2 dy\.b2), the bulk action gives the kinetic \
term (3/(\[Kappa]k)) (\[PartialD] e^(\[Minus]k\[Pi]T))\.b2, so the canonical \
radion is \[Mu] = f e^(\[Minus]k\[Pi]T) with f = \[Sqrt](6/(\[Kappa]k)). Here \
1/(2\[Kappa]) is the coefficient of \[Sqrt]|G| R in the bulk action, \
M_Pl\.b2/2 that of \[Sqrt]|g| R\:2084 and \.bd that of \
(\[PartialD]\[Mu])\.b2. Randall and Sundrum and Goldberger and Wise write the \
bulk action as 2M\.b3\[Integral]\[Sqrt]|G| R, i.e. \[Kappa] = 1/(4M\.b3): \
then f = \[Sqrt](24M\.b3/k) and the tensions \[PlusMinus]24M\.b3k. The note \
writes S5 = M5\.b3\[Integral]\[Sqrt]|G| R5 (\[Kappa] = 1/(2M5\.b3)) together \
with the formulas f = \[Sqrt](24M5\.b3/k) and M_Pl\.b2 = (M5\.b3/k)(1 \
\[Minus] e^(\[Minus]2\[Pi]k\[LeftAngleBracket]T\[RightAngleBracket])) of \
those papers; in its own normalization they read f = \[Sqrt](12M5\.b3/k) and \
M_Pl\.b2 = (2M5\.b3/k)(1 \[Minus] e^(\[Minus]2\[Pi]k\[LeftAngleBracket]T\
\[RightAngleBracket])). Its eight-dimensional version has the right M_Pl\.b2 \
but f = \[Sqrt](12/(\[Kappa]k)) instead of \[Sqrt](6/(\[Kappa]k)). On the IR \
brane h = (\[Mu]/f)\.b2 g: the radion couples to brane matter with 1/\
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket], TeV-strong, instead of 1/(\
\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl). In EIGHT dimensions the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s equations do \
not hold: for ds\.b2 = e^(\[Minus]2A(y)) \[Eta] \[Minus] dy\.b2 \[Minus] d",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["z", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "95c3eb56-ad21-1b4a-8db3-428579464b9d"],
 "\.b2 (warping along one of four extra directions) G^y_y = \
\[Minus]6A\[Prime]\.b2 but G^z_z = 4A\[DoublePrime] \[Minus] 10A\[Prime]\.b2, \
and with only \[CapitalLambda] there is no warped solution (A\[Prime] = 0). \
7+1.nb is unwarped: its bulk is a product."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ebc8003-20e3-9d46-a82d-d0d2d08eef6c"],

Cell["\<\
The note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s warped stabilization (Goldberger and Wise, in \
five dimensions): a bulk scalar \[CapitalPhi](y) of mass m with the boundary \
values \[CapitalPhi](0) = v_A, \[CapitalPhi](\[Pi]T) = v_B obeys \
\[CapitalPhi]\[DoublePrime] \[Minus] 4k\[CapitalPhi]\[Prime] \[Minus] m\.b2\
\[CapitalPhi] = 0 between the branes (from the action \[Integral]\[Sqrt]|G| (\
\.bd G^AB \[PartialD]\[CapitalPhi]\[PartialD]\[CapitalPhi] \[Minus] \.bd \
m\.b2\[CapitalPhi]\.b2), \[Sqrt]|G| = e^(\[Minus]4ky)), solved by \
\[CapitalPhi] = e^(2ky) (C1 e^(\[Nu]ky) + C2 e^(\[Minus]\[Nu]ky)) with \[Nu] \
= \[Sqrt](4 + m\.b2/k\.b2) \[TildeTilde] 2 + \[Epsilon], \[Epsilon] = \
m\.b2/(4k\.b2). Goldberger and Wise find V \[TildeTilde] k\[Epsilon]v_A\.b2 + \
4k e^(\[Minus]4k\[Pi]T) (v_B \[Minus] v_A e^(\[Minus]\[Epsilon]k\[Pi]T))\.b2, \
i.e. V(\[Mu]) = 4k (\[Mu]/f)\:2074 [v_B \[Minus] v_A \
(\[Mu]/f)^\[Epsilon]]\.b2 + const. Its minimum is at \
(\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket]/f)^\[Epsilon] = v_B/v_A, i.e. k\
\[Pi]\[LeftAngleBracket]T\[RightAngleBracket] = (4k\.b2/m\.b2) ln(v_A/v_B), \
and its curvature there is V\[DoublePrime](\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\
\[RightAngleBracket]) = 8k\[Epsilon]\.b2v_B\.b2\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\
\[RightAngleBracket]\.b2/f\:2074 (the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s algebra is \
right). With f\.b2 = 6/(\[Kappa]k) the radion mass is m_r\.b2 = (4/3) \
\[Kappa] k\.b2 \[Epsilon]\.b2 v_B\.b2 (\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\
\[RightAngleBracket]/f)\.b2 = k\.b2 v_B\.b2 \[Epsilon]\.b2 e^(\[Minus]2\[Pi]k\
\[LeftAngleBracket]T\[RightAngleBracket])/(3M\.b3) (\[Kappa] = 1/(4M\.b3): \
the result of Goldberger and Wise, Phys. Lett. B 475 (2000) 275, whose \
footnote adds that a more careful treatment of the \[Epsilon] terms changes \
\[Epsilon]\.b2 into \[Epsilon]^(3/2)); the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s factor 2/3 \
instead of 4/3 comes from its f\.b2 = 12/(\[Kappa]k).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e281e70a-d861-b249-a212-313d7751f584"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdXs5 = {rdt, rdx1, rdx2, rdx3, rdy}; rdG5 = rdEin[{E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 \
rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -1}, rdXs5];
rdc5 = Coefficient[rdG5[[1]], rdA''[rdy]]; rdJmp = D[rdk rdy, rdy] - D[-rdk \
rdy, rdy];
rdfUV = rdf /. First[Solve[rdc5 rdJmp == rdKap rdf, rdf]]; rdfIR = rdf /. \
First[Solve[rdc5 (-rdJmp) == rdKap rdf, rdf]];
check[\"RS1 in five dimensions (mostly minus): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 A'^2, \
G^y_y = -6 A'^2; bulk A = k y needs Lambda = -6 k^2; the delta functions A'' \
= +-2 k delta at the branes need the tensions f_UV = +6 k/kappa, f_IR = -6 \
k/kappa (UV positive)\",
  Simplify[rdG5 - Join[Table[3 rdA''[rdy] - 6 rdA'[rdy]^2, {4}], {-6 \
rdA'[rdy]^2}]] === ConstantArray[0, 5] &&
  Simplify[(rdG5 /. {rdA'[rdy] -> rdk, rdA''[rdy] -> 0}) - (-6 rdk^2)] === \
ConstantArray[0, 5] &&
  rdc5 === 3 && rdJmp === 2 rdk && rdfUV === 6 rdk/rdKap && rdfIR === -6 \
rdk/rdKap]
rdKmix = Table[(1/2) D[{E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), \
-E^(-2 rdA[rdy])}[[i]], rdy]/{E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 \
rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy])}[[i]], {i, 4}];
rdKjump = Simplify[(rdKmix /. rdA'[rdy] -> rdk) - (rdKmix /. rdA'[rdy] -> \
-rdk)];
check[\"Israel junction at the UV brane of RS1: with K^mu_nu = (1/2) g^mu \
alpha d_y g_alpha nu = -A' delta^mu_nu (normal d_y), [K^mu_nu] - delta^mu_nu \
[K] = 6 k = (coefficient of A'' in G^mu_nu) x (jump of A'), the \
delta-function part of G^mu_nu; in the signature (-,+,+,+,+) of the note \
G^A_B changes sign, so there [K_mu nu - g_mu nu K] = -kappa S_mu nu (the note \
uses +kappa S_mu nu, hence its reversed tensions)\",
  Simplify[rdKmix + rdA'[rdy]] === {0, 0, 0, 0} && Simplify[rdKjump - \
Total[rdKjump]] === Table[rdc5 rdJmp, {4}] && rdc5 rdJmp === 6 rdk]
check[\"RS1: M_Pl^2 = (1/kappa) Int_(-Pi R)^(Pi R) e^(-2 k |y|) dy = (1 - \
e^(-2 Pi k R))/(kappa k)\",
  Simplify[Integrate[E^(-2 rdk Abs[rdy]), {rdy, -Pi rdRR, Pi rdRR}, \
Assumptions -> rdk > 0 && rdRR > 0]/rdKap - (1 - E^(-2 Pi rdk rdRR))/(rdKap \
rdk)] === 0]
rdR5T = rdScal[{E^(-2 rdk rdT[rdt] rdy), -E^(-2 rdk rdT[rdt] rdy), -E^(-2 rdk \
rdT[rdt] rdy), -E^(-2 rdk rdT[rdt] rdy), -rdT[rdt]^2}, rdXs5];
rdLb = 2 Integrate[Expand[(-(1/(2 rdKap)) E^(-4 rdk rdTs rdy) rdTs rdR5T) /. \
{rdT''[rdt] -> rdT2, rdT'[rdt] -> rdT1, rdT[rdt] -> rdTs}], {rdy, 0, Pi},
    Assumptions -> rdk > 0 && rdTs > 0];
rdC2 = Coefficient[Expand[rdLb], rdT2]; rdL1 = Expand[rdLb - rdC2 rdT2 - \
D[rdC2, rdTs] rdT1^2];
check[\"RS1 radion: with R promoted to T(x), the bulk action is (3/(kappa k)) \
(d e^(-k Pi T))^2 + V(T) + (a total derivative), so the canonical radion is \
mu = Sqrt[6/(kappa k)] e^(-k Pi T) (the note: Sqrt[12/(kappa k)])\",
  FreeQ[rdC2, rdT1 | rdT2] && Simplify[Coefficient[rdL1, rdT1, 2] - (3/(rdKap \
rdk)) (rdk Pi E^(-rdk Pi rdTs))^2] === 0 && Coefficient[rdL1, rdT1, 1] === 0]
rdG8w = rdEin[{E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 rdA[rdy]), -E^(-2 \
rdA[rdy]), -1, -1, -1, -1}, {rdt, rdx1, rdx2, rdx3, rdy, rdz1, rdz2, rdz3}];
check[\"eight dimensions, warped along one extra direction (ds^2 = e^(-2 \
A(y)) eta - dy^2 - dz.dz): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 A'^2, G^y_y = -6 A'^2, G^z_z = \
4 A'' - 10 A'^2; with only Lambda (all G^A_A equal) A'' = 0 and A' = 0: the \
note's five-dimensional equations do not carry over\",
  Simplify[rdG8w - Join[Table[3 rdA''[rdy] - 6 rdA'[rdy]^2, {4}], {-6 \
rdA'[rdy]^2}, Table[4 rdA''[rdy] - 10 rdA'[rdy]^2, {3}]]] === \
ConstantArray[0, 8] &&
  DeleteDuplicates[Solve[{3 rdA2 - 6 rdA1^2 == -6 rdA1^2, -6 rdA1^2 == 4 rdA2 \
- 10 rdA1^2}, {rdA1, rdA2}]] === {{rdA1 -> 0, rdA2 -> 0}}]
rdGWL = E^(-4 rdk rdy) (-(1/2) rdPhy'[rdy]^2 - (1/2) rdMg^2 rdPhy[rdy]^2);
rdGWsol = E^(2 rdk rdy) (rdC1 E^(rdNu rdk rdy) + rdC2 E^(-rdNu rdk rdy)) /. \
rdNu -> Sqrt[4 + rdMg^2/rdk^2];
check[\"Goldberger-Wise in RS1: the static bulk scalar (Sqrt|G| = e^(-4 k y), \
G^yy = -1) obeys Phi'' - 4 k Phi' - m^2 Phi = 0, solved by e^(2 k y)(C1 e^(nu \
k y) + C2 e^(-nu k y)), nu = Sqrt[4 + m^2/k^2] = 2 + eps + O(m^4), eps = \
m^2/(4 k^2)\",
  Simplify[D[rdGWL, rdPhy[rdy]] - D[D[rdGWL, rdPhy'[rdy]], rdy] - E^(-4 rdk \
rdy) (rdPhy''[rdy] - 4 rdk rdPhy'[rdy] - rdMg^2 rdPhy[rdy])] === 0 &&
  Simplify[D[rdGWsol, {rdy, 2}] - 4 rdk D[rdGWsol, rdy] - rdMg^2 rdGWsol, rdk \
> 0] === 0 &&
  Normal[Series[Sqrt[4 + rdMg^2/rdk^2], {rdMg, 0, 2}]] === 2 + rdMg^2/(4 \
rdk^2)]
rdVgw = 4 rdk (rdmu/rdfm)^4 (rdvB - rdvA (rdmu/rdfm)^rdeps)^2; rdmu0 = rdfm \
(rdvB/rdvA)^(1/rdeps);      (* all of k, f, v_A, v_B, eps, kappa positive: \
PowerExpand is exact here *)
rdV2gw = Simplify[PowerExpand[D[rdVgw, {rdmu, 2}] /. rdmu -> rdmu0]];
rdMgw = Simplify[PowerExpand[rdV2gw/(rdk^2 rdeps^2 rdvB^2 (rdmu0/rdfm)^2) /. \
rdfm -> Sqrt[6/(rdKap rdk)]]/rdKap];
rdMgwNote = Simplify[PowerExpand[rdV2gw/(rdk^2 rdeps^2 rdvB^2 (rdmu0/rdfm)^2) \
/. rdfm -> Sqrt[12/(rdKap rdk)]]/rdKap];
check[\"Goldberger-Wise radion mass: V(mu) = 4 k (mu/f)^4 (v_B - v_A \
(mu/f)^eps)^2 has V'(<mu>) = 0 at (<mu>/f)^eps = v_B/v_A (k Pi <T> = (4 \
k^2/m^2) Log[v_A/v_B]) and V''(<mu>) = 8 k eps^2 v_B^2 <mu>^2/f^4; with f^2 = \
6/(kappa k): m_r^2 = (4/3) kappa k^2 eps^2 v_B^2 (<mu>/f)^2 (the note's f^2 = \
12/(kappa k) gives 2/3)\",
  Simplify[PowerExpand[D[rdVgw, rdmu] /. rdmu -> rdmu0]] === 0 &&
  Simplify[PowerExpand[rdV2gw - 8 rdk rdeps^2 rdvB^2 rdmu0^2/rdfm^4]] === 0 &&
  Simplify[PowerExpand[-Log[rdmu0/rdfm] - (4 rdk^2/rdMg^2) (Log[rdvA] - \
Log[rdvB])] /. rdeps -> rdMg^2/(4 rdk^2)] === 0 &&
  rdMgw === 4/3 && rdMgwNote === 2/3]
{\"RS1: coefficient of A'' in G^0_0, f_UV kappa/k, f_IR kappa/k, f^2 kappa k \
(canonical radion)\" -> Simplify[{rdc5, rdfUV rdKap/rdk, rdfIR rdKap/rdk,
    2 Coefficient[rdL1, rdT1, 2] rdKap rdk/(rdk Pi E^(-rdk Pi rdTs))^2}],
 \"strength of the radion coupling: warped with <mu> = 3 TeV over 7+1, i.e. \
Sqrt[3] M_Pl/(3 TeV)\" -> Sqrt[3] rIIMPl/3000.,
 \"Goldberger-Wise: m_r^2/(kappa k^2 eps^2 v_B^2 (<mu>/f)^2) with f^2 = \
6/(kappa k) and with the note's f^2 = 12/(kappa k)\" -> N[{rdMgw, rdMgwNote}]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1327]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3371d7bd-b889-274b-8f05-2f9e89b8c610"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"RS1 in five dimensions (mostly minus): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 \
A'^2, G^y_y = -6 A'^2; bulk A = k y needs Lambda = -6 k^2; the delta \
functions A'' = +-2 k delta at the branes need the tensions f_UV = +6 \
k/kappa, f_IR = -6 k/kappa (UV positive)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918575687428`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1330]=",ExpressionUUID->"6fd4bb30-9f4d-c346-97d3-c905a7e30639"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Israel junction at the UV brane of RS1: with K^mu_nu = (1/2) \
g^mu alpha d_y g_alpha nu = -A' delta^mu_nu (normal d_y), [K^mu_nu] - \
delta^mu_nu [K] = 6 k = (coefficient of A'' in G^mu_nu) x (jump of A'), the \
delta-function part of G^mu_nu; in the signature (-,+,+,+,+) of the note \
G^A_B changes sign, so there [K_mu nu - g_mu nu K] = -kappa S_mu nu (the note \
uses +kappa S_mu nu, hence its reversed tensions)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918575707417`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1333]=",ExpressionUUID->"e6b884ea-66ef-7b46-970a-14b642d7379b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"RS1: M_Pl^2 = (1/kappa) Int_(-Pi R)^(Pi R) e^(-2 k |y|) dy = (1 \
- e^(-2 Pi k R))/(kappa k)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191857927412*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1334]=",ExpressionUUID->"8e12ef38-8393-f640-8bb6-6ebbe3193709"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"RS1 radion: with R promoted to T(x), the bulk action is \
(3/(kappa k)) (d e^(-k Pi T))^2 + V(T) + (a total derivative), so the \
canonical radion is mu = Sqrt[6/(kappa k)] e^(-k Pi T) (the note: \
Sqrt[12/(kappa k)])\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191859448145*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1338]=",ExpressionUUID->"0d196c3a-f363-9c4a-9110-bf58c2f903b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"eight dimensions, warped along one extra direction (ds^2 = \
e^(-2 A(y)) eta - dy^2 - dz.dz): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 A'^2, G^y_y = -6 A'^2, \
G^z_z = 4 A'' - 10 A'^2; with only Lambda (all G^A_A equal) A'' = 0 and A' = \
0: the note's five-dimensional equations do not carry over\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918594651394`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1340]=",ExpressionUUID->"73d83496-68b7-af41-91e8-acae6c3bfdec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Goldberger-Wise in RS1: the static bulk scalar (Sqrt|G| = e^(-4 \
k y), G^yy = -1) obeys Phi'' - 4 k Phi' - m^2 Phi = 0, solved by e^(2 k y)(C1 \
e^(nu k y) + C2 e^(-nu k y)), nu = Sqrt[4 + m^2/k^2] = 2 + eps + O(m^4), eps \
= m^2/(4 k^2)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191859475218*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1343]=",ExpressionUUID->"e43ad38e-22df-9f4e-b124-30a13049b428"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Goldberger-Wise radion mass: V(mu) = 4 k (mu/f)^4 (v_B - v_A \
(mu/f)^eps)^2 has V'(<mu>) = 0 at (<mu>/f)^eps = v_B/v_A (k Pi <T> = (4 \
k^2/m^2) Log[v_A/v_B]) and V''(<mu>) = 8 k eps^2 v_B^2 <mu>^2/f^4; with f^2 = \
6/(kappa k): m_r^2 = (4/3) kappa k^2 eps^2 v_B^2 (<mu>/f)^2 (the note's f^2 = \
12/(kappa k) gives 2/3)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191859477148*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1348]=",ExpressionUUID->"3fc592e9-22b8-4048-bc7b-a78d86ae561c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"RS1: coefficient of A'' in G^0_0, f_UV kappa/k, f_IR kappa/k, \
f^2 kappa k (canonical radion)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", "6", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", "6"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"strength of the radion coupling: warped with <mu> = 3 TeV \
over 7+1, i.e. Sqrt[3] M_Pl/(3 TeV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "1.4058479054767385`*^15"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Goldberger-Wise: m_r^2/(kappa k^2 eps^2 v_B^2 (<mu>/f)^2) \
with f^2 = 6/(kappa k) and with the note's f^2 = 12/(kappa k)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1.3333333333333333`", ",", "0.6666666666666666`"}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191859479145*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1349]=",ExpressionUUID->"933dcbc2-a8b6-e14c-9778-70a7d3ee2bcc"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
26.6 The Higgs boson on the brane and the radion: mixing (the note\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s formulas, checked), and its size in 7+1\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"82167d58-1112-4643-8a6e-f09439f92bd8"],

Cell["\<\
The Higgs doublet H lives on the world brane (section 25.4) and feels the \
induced metric h_\[Mu]\[Nu] = \[CapitalOmega]\.b2 g_E,\[Mu]\[Nu]. In 7+1 \
\[CapitalOmega] = e^(\[Minus]2\[Beta]) = e^(\[Minus]\[Phi]/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl)) \
on T\:2074 and on S\:2074 alike (section 26.3); in RS1 \[CapitalOmega] = \
\[Mu]/\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket] after the brane fields are \
rescaled so that v is the physical vacuum value. Write \[CapitalOmega] = 1 + \
r/\[CapitalLambda] + O(r\.b2) with the bare radion r (\[CapitalLambda] = \
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket] in RS1, \[CapitalLambda] = \
\[Minus]\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl in 7+1; the sign of \[CapitalLambda] can be absorbed \
into r \[RightArrow] \[Minus]r) and \[Gamma] = v/\[CapitalLambda]. In unitary \
gauge H\[Dagger]H = \[Phi]_H\.b2/2 with \[Phi]_H = v + h. The note adds the \
curvature term \[Minus]\[Xi] \[Integral]\[Sqrt]|h| R(h) H\[Dagger]H of \
Giudice, Rattazzi and Wells (Nucl. Phys. B 595 (2001) 250), written in the \
signature (\[Minus],+,+,+); in the signature (+,\[Minus],\[Minus],\[Minus]) \
of 7+1.nb the scalar curvature changes sign and the brane Lagrangian reads\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ccced63-8b0c-3345-924f-b3c4c7b88614"],

Cell["\<\
      L = \[Sqrt]|h| [ \.bd h^\[Mu]\[Nu] \[PartialD]_\[Mu]\[Phi]_H \
\[PartialD]_\[Nu]\[Phi]_H \[Minus] (\[Lambda]/4)(\[Phi]_H\.b2 \[Minus] v\.b2)\
\.b2 + \.bd \[Xi] R(h) \[Phi]_H\.b2 ] + \.bd (\[PartialD]r)\.b2 \[Minus] \.bd \
m_r0\.b2 r\.b2   (\[Xi] = 1/6: conformal coupling),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dbdea7d1-1304-9043-b287-9664b3c3697c"],

Cell["\<\
with the canonical radion kinetic term of section 26.1 and the stabilized \
radion mass m_r0 (section 26.2). The checks: (i) for h = \[CapitalOmega]\.b2\
\[Eta], \[Sqrt]|h| R(h) = \[Minus]6 \[CapitalOmega] \[EmptySquare]\
\[CapitalOmega] with \[EmptySquare] = \[PartialD]0\.b2 \[Minus] \[Del]\.b2 \
(four dimensions); (ii) to second order in the fields and up to total \
derivatives L = \.bd(\[PartialD]h)\.b2 + \.bd(1 + 6\[Xi]\[Gamma]\.b2)(\
\[PartialD]r)\.b2 + 6\[Xi]\[Gamma] \[PartialD]h\[CenterDot]\[PartialD]r \
\[Minus] \.bdm_h0\.b2 h\.b2 \[Minus] \.bdm_r0\.b2 r\.b2 (m_h0\.b2 = \
2\[Lambda]v\.b2), and the terms linear in the fields are total derivatives \
(the vacuum is a solution) \[LongDash] the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s kinetic \
Lagrangian lacks the 6\[Xi]\[Gamma]\.b2 of the radion, which its Z contains; \
(iii) the shift h = h\[Prime] \[Minus] (6\[Xi]\[Gamma]/Z) r\[Prime], r = r\
\[Prime]/Z makes the kinetic terms canonical if and only if Z\.b2 = 1 + \
6\[Xi]\[Gamma]\.b2(1 \[Minus] 6\[Xi]) (with the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
literal kinetic terms it would be Z\.b2 = 1 \[Minus] \
36\[Xi]\.b2\[Gamma]\.b2); (iv) the mass matrix of (h\[Prime], r\[Prime]) is \
diagonal in the fields (h_m, r_m) given by h\[Prime] = cos \[Theta] h_m \
\[Minus] sin \[Theta] r_m, r\[Prime] = sin \[Theta] h_m + cos \[Theta] r_m \
with tan 2\[Theta] = 12\[Gamma]\[Xi]Z m_h0\.b2/(m_r0\.b2 \[Minus] m_h0\.b2(Z\
\.b2 \[Minus] 36\[Xi]\.b2\[Gamma]\.b2)) (the note writes the same matrix with \
the primed and unprimed fields interchanged, which would reverse the sign of \
\[Theta]), and then h = C_h h_m + \[Ellipsis], r = C_r h_m + \[Ellipsis] with \
C_h = cos \[Theta] \[Minus] (6\[Xi]\[Gamma]/Z) sin \[Theta], C_r = sin \
\[Theta]/Z, the coefficients of the note. The note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s rates \
\[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] \[Gamma]\[Gamma])/\[CapitalGamma]_SM = |C_h + \
C_r \[Gamma] b_EM/F_SM|\.b2 and \[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] gg)/\
\[CapitalGamma]_SM = |C_h + C_r \[Gamma] b_QCD/F_heavy|\.b2 (its values b_EM \
= \[Minus]11/3, F_SM = \[Minus]6.5, b_QCD = 7, F_heavy = \[Minus]4/3) are \
evaluated below for 7+1. There \[Gamma] = v/(\[Sqrt]3 M_Pl) = 5.8 \[Times] 10\
\:207b\.b9\:2077: for \[Xi] = 1 and m_r0 = 10 GeV the mixing angle is 3.5 \
\[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\:2076 and the rates change by 10\:207b\.b3\.b9 \
\[LongDash] the flat radion of 7+1 (T\:2074 or S\:2074) cannot be seen \
through the Higgs boson; the note\[CloseCurlyQuote]s LHC bounds (\
\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Mu]\[RightAngleBracket] > 2.5\[Dash]3 TeV, \[Minus]0.1 < \
\[Xi] < 0.4) concern the warped radion (\[Gamma] = v/(3 TeV) = 0.082).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a19bfc8a-32c1-734f-9c83-ac6b2b74da9a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rdEL2[L_, q_] := Simplify[D[L, q[x0, x1]] - D[D[L, Derivative[1, 0][q][x0, \
x1]], x0] - D[D[L, Derivative[0, 1][q][x0, x1]], x1] +
    D[D[L, Derivative[2, 0][q][x0, x1]], {x0, 2}] + D[D[L, Derivative[1, \
1][q][x0, x1]], x0, x1] + D[D[L, Derivative[0, 2][q][x0, x1]], {x1, 2}]];
rdc4 = Simplify[rdOmg[x0, x1]^4 rdScal[rdOmg[x0, x1]^2 {1, -1, -1, -1}, {x0, \
x1, x2, x3}]/(rdOmg[x0, x1] (D[rdOmg[x0, x1], {x0, 2}] - D[rdOmg[x0, x1], \
{x1, 2}]))];
check[\"conformally flat brane metric h = Omega^2 eta (four dimensions, \
Omega(x0, x1)): Sqrt|h| R(h) == -6 Omega box Omega with box = d0^2 - d1^2 \
(curvature conventions of 7+1.nb)\",
  rdc4 === -6]
rdOmE = 1 + rdO1 rdEp rdRr[x0, x1] + rdO2 rdEp^2 rdRr[x0, x1]^2; rdPhE = rdVv \
+ rdEp rdHh[x0, x1];
rdRh = rdScal[rdOmE^2 {1, -1, -1, -1}, {x0, x1, x2, x3}];
rdLbr = rdOmE^4 ((1/2) rdOmE^-2 (D[rdPhE, x0]^2 - D[rdPhE, x1]^2) - rdLamH/4 \
(rdPhE^2 - rdVv^2)^2 + (1/2) rdXi rdRh rdPhE^2) +
   rdEp^2 ((1/2) (D[rdRr[x0, x1], x0]^2 - D[rdRr[x0, x1], x1]^2) - (1/2) \
rdMr0^2 rdRr[x0, x1]^2);
rdHL1 = Simplify[D[rdLbr, rdEp] /. rdEp -> 0]; rdHL2 = Simplify[D[rdLbr, \
{rdEp, 2}]/2 /. rdEp -> 0];
rdGam = rdO1 rdVv;
rdLq = (1/2) (D[rdHh[x0, x1], x0]^2 - D[rdHh[x0, x1], x1]^2) + (1/2) (1 + 6 \
rdXi rdGam^2) (D[rdRr[x0, x1], x0]^2 - D[rdRr[x0, x1], x1]^2) +
   6 rdXi rdGam (D[rdHh[x0, x1], x0] D[rdRr[x0, x1], x0] - D[rdHh[x0, x1], \
x1] D[rdRr[x0, x1], x1]) - (1/2) (2 rdLamH rdVv^2) rdHh[x0, x1]^2 - (1/2) \
rdMr0^2 rdRr[x0, x1]^2;
rdKhr = -Coefficient[Expand[rdEL2[rdHL2, rdRr]], Derivative[2, 0][rdHh][x0, \
x1]]; rdKrr = -Coefficient[Expand[rdEL2[rdHL2, rdRr]], Derivative[2, \
0][rdRr][x0, x1]];
check[\"the Higgs boson on the brane (h = Omega^2 eta, Omega = 1 + r/Lambda + \
a2 r^2, phi_H = v + h, gamma = v/Lambda): the terms linear in (h, r) are \
total derivatives, and to second order L == (1/2)(dh)^2 + (1/2)(1 + 6 xi \
gamma^2)(dr)^2 + 6 xi gamma dh.dr - (1/2) m_h0^2 h^2 - (1/2) m_r0^2 r^2 up to \
total derivatives (Euler-Lagrange expressions in x0 and x1); a2 drops out\",
  rdEL2[rdHL1, rdRr] === 0 && rdEL2[rdHL1, rdHh] === 0 && rdEL2[rdHL2 - rdLq, \
rdRr] === 0 && rdEL2[rdHL2 - rdLq, rdHh] === 0 &&
  Simplify[rdKhr - 6 rdXi rdGam] === 0 && Simplify[rdKrr - (1 + 6 rdXi \
rdGam^2)] === 0 && FreeQ[rdEL2[rdHL2, rdRr], rdO2] && FreeQ[rdEL2[rdHL2, \
rdHh], rdO2]]
rdKm = {{1, rdKhr}, {rdKhr, rdKrr}}; rdKnote = {{1, 6 rdXi rdGam}, {6 rdXi \
rdGam, 1}};
rdSm = {{1, -6 rdXi rdGam/rdZ}, {0, 1/rdZ}}; rdZ2 = 1 + 6 rdXi rdGam^2 (1 - 6 \
rdXi);
check[\"canonical kinetic terms: Transpose[S].K.S == 1 for S = {{1, -6 xi \
gamma/Z}, {0, 1/Z}} if and only if Z^2 = 1 + 6 xi gamma^2 (1 - 6 xi) (the \
note's Z); with the note's literal kinetic terms (no 6 xi gamma^2 for the \
radion) it would be Z^2 = 1 - 36 xi^2 gamma^2\",
  Simplify[Transpose[rdSm].rdKm.rdSm /. rdZ -> Sqrt[rdZ2]] === \
IdentityMatrix[2] && Simplify[(Transpose[rdSm].rdKm.rdSm)[[2, 2]] rdZ^2 - \
rdZ2] === 0 &&
  Simplify[(Transpose[rdSm].rdKnote.rdSm)[[2, 2]] rdZ^2 - (1 - 36 rdXi^2 \
rdGam^2)] === 0 && Simplify[(Transpose[rdSm].rdKnote.rdSm)[[1, 2]]] === 0]
rdMp = Transpose[rdSm].DiagonalMatrix[{rdMh0^2, rdMr0^2}].rdSm;
rdQ[th_] := {{Cos[th], -Sin[th]}, {Sin[th], Cos[th]}};
check[\"mass mixing: with (h', r') = Q(theta).(h_m, r_m), Q = {{cos, -sin}, \
{sin, cos}}, the off-diagonal element of Transpose[Q].M'.Q is -(1/2)(M'_11 - \
M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta, zero for tan 2 theta = 2 M'_12/(M'_11 \
- M'_22) = 12 gamma xi Z m_h0^2/(m_r0^2 - m_h0^2 (Z^2 - 36 xi^2 gamma^2)) \
(the note's formula); with the inverse matrix (the note's display) it is \
+(1/2)(M'_11 - M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta (theta -> -theta); (h, \
r) = S.Q.(h_m, r_m) gives C_h = cos theta - (6 xi gamma/Z) sin theta, C_r = \
sin theta/Z\",
  Simplify[TrigReduce[(Transpose[rdQ[rdth]].rdMp.rdQ[rdth])[[1, 2]]] + (1/2) \
(rdMp[[1, 1]] - rdMp[[2, 2]]) Sin[2 rdth] - rdMp[[1, 2]] Cos[2 rdth]] === 0 &&
  Simplify[2 rdMp[[1, 2]]/(rdMp[[1, 1]] - rdMp[[2, 2]]) - 12 rdGam rdXi rdZ \
rdMh0^2/(rdMr0^2 - rdMh0^2 (rdZ^2 - 36 rdXi^2 rdGam^2))] === 0 &&
  Simplify[TrigReduce[(rdQ[rdth].rdMp.Transpose[rdQ[rdth]])[[1, 2]]] - (1/2) \
(rdMp[[1, 1]] - rdMp[[2, 2]]) Sin[2 rdth] - rdMp[[1, 2]] Cos[2 rdth]] === 0 &&
  Simplify[(rdSm.rdQ[rdth])[[All, 1]] - {Cos[rdth] - 6 rdXi rdGam \
Sin[rdth]/rdZ, Sin[rdth]/rdZ}] === {0, 0}]
rdHRnum[gam_, xi_, mr_, mh_] := Module[{z, t, ch, cr}, z = Sqrt[1 + 6 xi \
gam^2 (1 - 6 xi)];
   t = ArcTan[12 gam xi z mh^2/(mr^2 - mh^2 (z^2 - 36 xi^2 gam^2))]/2; ch = \
Cos[t] - 6 xi gam Sin[t]/z; cr = Sin[t]/z;
   {z - 1, t, (ch + cr gam (-11/3)/(-13/2))^2 - 1, (ch + cr gam 7/(-4/3))^2 - \
1}];
rdHR71 = rdHRnum[SetPrecision[rdEW[[3]], 60], 1, 10, SetPrecision[mHb, 60]];
check[\"Higgs-radion mixing in 7+1 (gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl), xi = 1, m_r0 = \
10 GeV, m_h0 = 125.20 GeV; 60-digit arithmetic): |Z - 1| < 10^-30, |theta| = \
3.5 10^-16, the rates of h -> gamma gamma and h -> g g change by less than \
10^-30; in RS1 with <mu> = 3 TeV gamma = v/(3 TeV) = 0.082\",
  Abs[rdHR71[[1]]] < 10^-30 && Abs[Abs[rdHR71[[2]]]/3.53*^-16 - 1] < 10^-2 && \
Abs[rdHR71[[3]]] < 10^-30 && Abs[rdHR71[[4]]] < 10^-30 && Abs[vEW/3000/0.0821 \
- 1] < 10^-2]
{\"Higgs-radion mixing: c in Sqrt|h| R(h) = c Omega box Omega, K_hr/(xi \
gamma), (K_rr - 1)/(xi gamma^2)\" -> N[Simplify[{rdc4, rdKhr/(rdXi rdGam), \
(rdKrr - 1)/(rdXi rdGam^2)}]],
 \"Higgs-radion mixing in 7+1 (gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl), xi = 1, m_r0 = 10 \
GeV): Z - 1, theta, Gamma(h -> gamma gamma)/SM - 1, Gamma(h -> g g)/SM - 1; \
warped gamma = v/(3 TeV)\" ->
   Join[SetPrecision[rdHR71, MachinePrecision], {vEW/3000.}]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1350]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9a5ee75d-bce7-0945-a33c-2b9d73169f4c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"conformally flat brane metric h = Omega^2 eta (four dimensions, \
Omega(x0, x1)): Sqrt|h| R(h) == -6 Omega box Omega with box = d0^2 - d1^2 \
(curvature conventions of 7+1.nb)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918595465355`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1352]=",ExpressionUUID->"9bfe373a-1aeb-494b-94ec-b485535f0a44"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the Higgs boson on the brane (h = Omega^2 eta, Omega = 1 + \
r/Lambda + a2 r^2, phi_H = v + h, gamma = v/Lambda): the terms linear in (h, \
r) are total derivatives, and to second order L == (1/2)(dh)^2 + (1/2)(1 + 6 \
xi gamma^2)(dr)^2 + 6 xi gamma dh.dr - (1/2) m_h0^2 h^2 - (1/2) m_r0^2 r^2 up \
to total derivatives (Euler-Lagrange expressions in x0 and x1); a2 drops \
out\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002191859713545*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1360]=",ExpressionUUID->"25738905-5969-6d40-ab2f-80760e09c0b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"canonical kinetic terms: Transpose[S].K.S == 1 for S = {{1, -6 \
xi gamma/Z}, {0, 1/Z}} if and only if Z^2 = 1 + 6 xi gamma^2 (1 - 6 xi) (the \
note's Z); with the note's literal kinetic terms (no 6 xi gamma^2 for the \
radion) it would be Z^2 = 1 - 36 xi^2 gamma^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918597248707`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1363]=",ExpressionUUID->"b12ddfd0-082f-7d4f-8ed9-d0aef7bd5559"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"mass mixing: with (h', r') = Q(theta).(h_m, r_m), Q = {{cos, \
-sin}, {sin, cos}}, the off-diagonal element of Transpose[Q].M'.Q is \
-(1/2)(M'_11 - M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta, zero for tan 2 theta = \
2 M'_12/(M'_11 - M'_22) = 12 gamma xi Z m_h0^2/(m_r0^2 - m_h0^2 (Z^2 - 36 \
xi^2 gamma^2)) (the note's formula); with the inverse matrix (the note's \
display) it is +(1/2)(M'_11 - M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta (theta \
-> -theta); (h, r) = S.Q.(h_m, r_m) gives C_h = cos theta - (6 xi gamma/Z) \
sin theta, C_r = sin theta/Z\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918597248707`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1366]=",ExpressionUUID->"dbc136f9-92bd-4e45-aca6-6e7b045578c8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Higgs-radion mixing in 7+1 (gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl), xi = 1, \
m_r0 = 10 GeV, m_h0 = 125.20 GeV; 60-digit arithmetic): |Z - 1| < 10^-30, \
|theta| = 3.5 10^-16, the rates of h -> gamma gamma and h -> g g change by \
less than 10^-30; in RS1 with <mu> = 3 TeV gamma = v/(3 TeV) = 0.082\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918597248707`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1369]=",ExpressionUUID->"c4ec2719-ac38-ff45-b8bc-b65797f60d01"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"Higgs-radion mixing: c in Sqrt|h| R(h) = c Omega box Omega, \
K_hr/(xi gamma), (K_rr - 1)/(xi gamma^2)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "6.`"}], ",", "6.`", ",", "6.`"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Higgs-radion mixing in 7+1 (gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl), xi = 1, \
m_r0 = 10 GeV): Z - 1, theta, Gamma(h -> gamma gamma)/SM - 1, Gamma(h -> g \
g)/SM - 1; warped gamma = v/(3 TeV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "5.112313265186564`*^-32"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "3.525281784433871`*^-16"}], ",", 
      "9.947138056858164`*^-32", ",", "3.387862153903165`*^-31", ",", 
      "0.08207321341308735`"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021918597248707`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1370]=",ExpressionUUID->"e1c0211c-dbdb-3d4e-9400-0765d98df212"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

