    {"\<\"portal mixing: 1 - N.N^dag == mu.mu^dag/m^2 to second order \
(non-unitary light mixing)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"vacuum: P(a->b) doubly stochastic; equals delta - 4 Sum Re X sin^2 \
Delta + 2 Sum Im X sin 2Delta; CPT P(a->b) == P(bbar->abar)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"V_CC(rho Y_e = 1 g/cm^3) == 7.63 x 10^-14 eV; matter evolution \
doubly stochastic; a flavour-universal potential has no effect\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"two-flavour MSW: sin^2 theta_m from diagonalization == formula, and \
sin^2 2theta_m == 1 at 2 E V == dm^2 cos 2theta\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Sun: numerical P_ee == adiabatic MSW formula to 2 x 10^-3 at 0.3, \
1, 5 and 10 MeV; P_ee(0.3 MeV) within 0.03 of the vacuum average; P_ee falls \
with energy\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cosmic neutrino background: T_nu == 1.945 K and n == 112 cm^-3 per \
flavour\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"dirac16complex portal: non-unitary oscillations, Sum_b P(a->b) < 1 \
(zero-distance effect); decoupled limit == three-flavour vacuum result\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic Lovelock density in invariant form: L_3 == R^3 - 12 R Ric.Ric \
+ 16 Ric^3 + 24 R^ac R^bd R_abcd + 3 R Riem.Riem - 24 R^ab R_a^cde R_bcde + 4 \
R^ab_cd R^cd_ef R^ef_ab - 8 R_a^c_b^d R_c^e_d^f R_e^a_f^b (exact, four random \
integer algebraic curvature tensors)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Gauss-Bonnet density in invariant form: L_2 == R^2 - 4 Ric.Ric + \
Riem.Riem (the same tensors, exact)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"stabilizing potential: W = a^3 b^4 U(b) gives eps = U, pa = -U, pb \
= -U - (b/4) U'(b)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane tension smeared over the torus (V_perp = b^4 Lc^4): eps = \
f_W/V_perp, pa = -f_W/V_perp, pb = 0\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane fluid rho_4 = N a^(-3(1+w)), smeared: eps = rho_4/V_perp, pa \
= w eps, pb = 0\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"massless dirac16complex particle (comoving momentum (k_a, k_b)): \
eps V = omega, pa V = k_a^2/(3 a^2 omega), pb V = k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega)\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"every such source is conserved: eps' + 3Ha(eps + pa) + 4Hb(eps + \
pb) == 0 for arbitrary W(a, b), a(x0), b(x0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"minisuperspace: EL_n == (a^3 b^4/kappa)(S00 - kappa eps), EL_a == \
(3 a^2 b^4/kappa)(S11 + kappa pa), EL_b == (4 a^3 b^3/kappa)(S44 + kappa pb) \
with S = Sum alpha_k E^(k) (identities of section 12.6)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion equation of Einstein gravity: Hb' + 3 Ha Hb + 4 Hb^2 == \
kappa (eps/6 - pa/2 + pb/3) + Lambda/3 (constraint used)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion mass: U = U0 + (K_U/2) beta^2, b U' = K_U beta gives the \
restoring term -(kappa K_U/12) beta, m_r^2 = kappa K_U/12\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"static auxiliary space: (kappa/4) b U' == Lambda + kappa U + 2 \
kappa f_W/V_perp + (kappa/2)(eps - 3pa) + kappa pb - 12 alpha2 Ha^2 (Ha' + \
Ha^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"static auxiliary space: Ha' == -(kappa/2)(eps + pa) and E^(3) does \
not contribute (Hb = 0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane Friedmann equation: 3 Ha^2 == (kappa/V_perp) rho_4 + Lambda4 \
with Lambda4 = Lambda + kappa U0 + kappa f_W/V_perp, i.e. 8 Pi G4 = \
kappa/V_perp\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein-frame form of the constraint: 3 (Ha + 2 Hb)^2 == 6 Hb^2 + \
(E^(1)0_0 of section 12.6), i.e. 3 M_Pl^2 H_E^2 == phi'^2/2 + rho with phi = \
Sqrt[12] M_Pl beta\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"vacuum constraint in u = Hb/Ha, X = Ha^2 (alpha2 = 1, alpha3 = xi): \
P_E + X P_G + xi X^2 P_C == 0 with P_E = 3(2u^2 + 4u + 1), P_G = -12u(u^3 + \
12u^2 + 18u + 4), P_C = 360 u^3 (3u + 4)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kasner constants: P_E(u1) == 0, p1 == (1 + 2 Sqrt[2])/7, q1 == (2 - \
3 Sqrt[2])/14; u2 in (-1/3, 0) with P_G(u2) == 0, 3 p2 + 4 q2 == 3\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"the explicit curve solves the vacuum constraint: residual < 10^-25 \
(relative) at u = u1 + 10^-6, -0.28, u2, -0.1, -10^-4 (xi = 10^-6, 40 digits)\
\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the effective exponent along the curve: p_eff -> p1 (u -> u1), \
about p2 at u = u2 (within 10^-2), -> 1 (u -> 0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic regime: Ha = 1/tau + A0 + A1 tau, Hb = h0 + h1 tau + h2 tau^2 \
solves the 00, 11, 44 equations through order tau^-1 (11: checked, not \
used)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic regime coefficients: h1 == alpha2/(16 alpha3) - 1/(32 \
alpha2), A0 == Sqrt[30](58 alpha2^2 - 45 alpha3)/(1920 alpha2^(3/2) \
alpha3^(1/2)), A1 and h2 as in the text\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein regime: u = u1 + d1 Ha^2, d1 == alpha2 (16 - 11 \
Sqrt[2])/4; p_eff = p1 + e1 Ha^2, e1 == alpha2 (1 + 9 Sqrt[2])/7\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Gauss-Bonnet regime: p_eff = p2 + f1/Ha^2 + f2 xi Ha^2 with f1 = \
-0.69887346..., f2 = -0.7853407... (differences give the same values at Ha = \
10^4 and 10^-6 xi Ha^2 to 10^-5)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic-series data at tau = 10^-8 satisfy the vacuum constraint to < \
10^-12 (relative to 48 Ha^3 |Hb|)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the ODE solution agrees with the exact quadrature: tau at Ha(u2) to \
10^-10, and tau - p1/Ha + e1 Ha at Ha = 3 10^-3 equals s1 to 10^-6\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"regime approximations: cubic error < 10^-5 for Ha >= 10^4, \
Gauss-Bonnet < 10^-3 for 3 <= Ha <= 300, Einstein < 10^-3 for Ha <= 0.1\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"matter-dominated cubic regime: p_eff -> 3/4, Hb -> -Sqrt[alpha2/(54 \
alpha3)], kappa eps tau^3 -> 9 alpha2 |h*|, alpha2 E2 : alpha3 E3 : kappa eps \
-> 9/4 : -5/4 : 1 (Ha = 10^15)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"coupled: where the gas is a small fraction the effective exponents \
are those of the vacuum (1, p2, p1 within 10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"without the stabilizing potential the gas-dominated Einstein regime \
decompactifies: tau Ha -> 0, tau Hb -> 2/5, pb/eps -> 1/4 (Ha = 10^-14)\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"the gas fraction grows like tau^(2 - 3 p1 - 5 q1) = tau^1.160 in \
the Einstein regime (to 2 10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein + fluid power laws a ~ tau^P, b ~ tau^Q: (wa, wb) = (0, \
1/4) -> (0, 2/5); (1/3, 0) -> (1/2, 0); (1/7, 1/7) -> (1/4, 1/4) (tau^2 E^(1) \
from EKas of section 14.1)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"matter-dominated cubic regime (any fluid, b finite): leading 44 \
term p^3 (p - 1)(648 alpha3 h^2 - 12 alpha2); with h^2 = alpha2/(54 alpha3): \
p = 1/(1 + w_a) and kappa eps tau^3 = (64/3) p^3 alpha2 |h|\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein-Kasner pair creation: F(1) == 0.0107493 (section 14.3) and \
the tail F ~ K^(-(3 Sqrt[2] + 2)/2) (exponent between K = 8 and 16 to 2 \
10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane plasma at T = M8, H = M8: fraction (Pi^2 g*/30) M8^4/(3 \
M_Pl^2 M8^2) < 10^-27\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"capture: the radion oscillates like a four-dimensional massive \
field in a matter-dominated universe: with tau_E from <H_E> = 2/(3 (tau - \
tau_E)) over the last period, beta = A sin(m_r tau + vartheta)/(m_r (tau - \
tau_E)) to 2 10^-2, <H_E>(tau - tau_E) = 2/3 to 10^-2 at tau = 10^5 and 2 \
10^5, the gas share constant to 2 10^-2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"through brane fields alone a 10 GeV radion would decay far too \
late: T_RH < 10^-6 GeV (nucleosynthesis needs 4 10^-3 GeV); 10^13 \
Kaluza-Klein channels below m_r/2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the number of lattice vectors with |n|^2 = k is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) \
- 32 sigma(k/4) (direct count for k <= 60)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion decays into the bulk: the lattice sum over the \
Kaluza-Klein modes of dirac16complex (m << m_r/2) equals its continuum limit \
to 10^-6, the number of momenta to 10^-5, and Gamma_bulk/Gamma_brane > \
10^12\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"g* limits: 106.75 above the electroweak scale (to 0.1), 10.75 near \
3 MeV (to 0.1), 2 + (21/4)(4/11)^(4/3)(3.044/3) = 3.3855 after e+e- \
annihilation (to 10^-3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the time-temperature quadrature is converged: halving the grid \
changes t(10 keV) by less than 10^-5\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radiation era: t(1 MeV) = 0.74 s within 5% (1/(2 Ha) with g* = \
10.75)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"age of the universe from the brane Friedmann equation: 13.79 Gyr \
(Planck 2018: 13.787 +- 0.020)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"composite analytic solution t(a) = t_rm(a) + t_mLambda(a) - t_m(a) \
accurate to < 3 10^-4 for 10^-8 <= a <= 10^0.5\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"far future: Ha(t) = H_inf Coth[3 H_inf t/2] agrees with the full \
brane solution at a = 3 and a = 10 to 10^-4\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion in de Sitter: gamma/(3H) and m_eff^2/m_r^2 as in the text \
(beta_eq -> 0); gamma = 3H and m_eff^2 = m_r^2 for alpha2 = alpha3 = 0\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"radion equilibrium in de Sitter: 3 m_r^2 beta_eq == 3 H^2 - 12 \
alpha2 H^4 + O(beta_eq^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion relaxes to the equilibrium of the two algebraic \
equations: beta(3000) to 10^-6, Ha(3000) to 10^-8 (relative)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"eight-dimensional de Sitter (no stabilizer): all three equations \
read 21 H^2 - 420 alpha2 H^4 + 2520 alpha3 H^6 == Lambda\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the shares of the four terms of the 00 equation: Einstein > 0.99 at \
Ha = 10^-2, Gauss-Bonnet > 0.9 at Ha = 30, Gauss-Bonnet and cubic about 1/2 \
each at Ha = 3 10^5, gas > 0.1 at Ha = 10^15\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"required abundance: m Y = Omega_c h^2 (rho_c/h^2)/s0 = 4.37 10^-10 \
GeV with rho_c/h^2 = 1.053 10^-5 GeV/cm^3 and s0 = 2891 cm^-3 (to 10^-3)\"\>",
      "True"},
    {"\<\"collider bound: with M_Pl^2 = R^n M_D^(n+2) and V_perp = (2 Pi R)^4 \
= M_Pl^2/M8^6, M_D = (2 Pi)^(2/3) M8 = 34 TeV, above the strongest bound 11.2 \
TeV\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"a massive dirac16complex particle: eps V == omega, pa V == k_a^2/(3 \
a^2 omega), pb V == k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega), omega = Sqrt[m^2 + k_a^2/a^2 + \
k_b^2/b^2]\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the lightest mode (k_b = 0) is cold matter: pa/eps == k_a^2/(3 (m^2 \
a^2 + k_a^2)) -> 0, pb == 0, and eps ~ a^-3 at fixed b for k_a = 0\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"dark matter displaces the radion today by H0^2 Omega_c/(2 m_r^2) < \
10^-80 (m_r = 10 GeV): the four-dimensional Newton constant is constant\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"regime III: Omega_m a^-3/Omega_Lambda == Csch[3 H t/2]^2 for a = \
(Omega_m/Omega_Lambda)^(1/3) Sinh[3 H t/2]^(2/3), and -> 4 Exp[-3 H t]\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"couplings of the lightest mode: with V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6, \
lambda_P/V_perp == c_P M8/M_Pl^2, y/Sqrt[V_perp] == c_y M8/M_Pl, G_P/V_perp \
== c_V/M_Pl^2, g_r/V_perp == c_r/M_Pl^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"natural couplings make the lightest mode dark and collisionless: \
sigma_SI(c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV) < 10^-50 x (LZ limit 2.2 10^-48 cm^2), \
sigma/m(c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV) < 10^-70 cm^2/g (Bullet Cluster: 0.7 cm^2/g)\"\>",
      "True"},
    {"\<\"stability through the Yukawa portal: for c_y = 1 the lifetime chi \
-> 3 nu equals the age of the universe at m = 40 MeV; it scales as 1/(c_y^2 \
m^3), and Gamma(nu gamma)/Gamma(3 nu) == 27 alpha/(8 Pi)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"primordial gas: overabundance O = (f/(1 - f)) T_RH/((4/3) m Y) = \
1.5 10^7 T_RH/GeV (6 10^4 at T_RH = 4 MeV)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion puts more than 1 - 10^-12 of its decays into the bulk \
(Kaluza-Klein pairs of dirac16complex)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Boltzmann factor of production below T_RH: Int_0^Infinity t^3 \
K_1(t) dt == 3 Pi/2 (exact), S(0) = 1, S(m_h/T*) < 10^-2 with T* = \
(M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) = 13.3 GeV\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"zero mode through the Yukawa portal: the abundance (~ c_y^2 m) and \
the stability (lifetime ~ 1/(c_y^2 m^3) > age) are compatible only for m < \
m*, and m* < 5.7 keV (Lyman-alpha) for N = 1 and N = 12 channels even with S \
= 1\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kaluza-Klein tower: Sum_n (1 - mu_n^2/m_h^2)^2 -> V_perp m_h^4/(192 \
Pi^2) and Sum_n mu_n (1 - mu_n^2/m_h^2)^2 -> V_perp m_h^5/(315 Pi^2) (d^4n = \
2 Pi^2 |n|^3 d|n|: exact integrals); the lattice sums with r_4(k) for R = 100 \
equal Pi^2 R^4/12 and 16 Pi^2 R^4/315 to 10^-8\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kaluza-Klein tower through the Yukawa portal: 7.7 10^17 states \
below m_h with mean mass (192/315) m_h; at T_RH = T* it carries more energy \
than all the dark matter unless c_y < 2 10^-5 (N = 1)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Higgs portal: the zero mode gets Y < 10^-40 (c_P = 1); the pairs of \
Kaluza-Klein levels (lambda(1, u1^2, u2^2) == (1 - (u1 + u2)^2)(1 - (u1 - \
u2)^2)) give the observed abundance only for c_P between 10 and 20 (T_RH >> \
m_h, S -> 1) or between 100 and 200 (T_RH = T*)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"vector portal: gravitational strength per pair; the production rate \
of all pairs lighter than T divided by H ~ (T/T_V)^11 with T_V = \
(M8^12/M_Pl)^(1/11) = 490 GeV is below 10^-17 at T*\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kohn-Sham matter of section 8: p > 0 at low density, p < 0 below \
saturation, p = 0 at kF0, a spinodal region (dp/dkF < 0) in between, and w = \
p/eps >= -0.06 everywhere\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Epstein sum over Z^4 without 0: Sum |n|^-8 == 8 (1 - 4^-3) zeta(4) \
zeta(3), compared with the shell sum Sum r_4(k)/k^4 to k = 20000 (tail < 3 \
10^-8)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Casimir energy of dirac16complex on the auxiliary torus: massless \
16 Gamma(4) Z/(Pi^4 l^4) > 10^34 rho_Lambda, the massive sum -> the massless \
value for m l -> 0 (to 10^-4), and equals rho_Lambda at m l = 92.2\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"auxiliary torus: for the cosmological metric det(-g_kl) == b^8 (k, \
l = 4..7), and the proper volume of the fundamental domain [0, Lc)^4, \
Integrate[Sqrt[det(-g_kl)], {y, 0, Lc}^4], is b^4 Lc^4 = V_perp\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"only the product b Lc of the auxiliary torus is physical: y = \
lambda y' maps the torus of period Lc and size b to the one of period \
Lc/lambda and size lambda b; the line element b^2 dy.dy, the proper period b \
Lc and V_perp = b^4 Lc^4 are unchanged\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"symmetries of the auxiliary torus that fix y = 0 (and the brane): \
the 384 = 2^4 4! signed permutation matrices are distinct orthogonal integer \
matrices (they map Z^4 onto itself and preserve |n|^2); the shells |n|^2 = 1, \
2, 3, 4, 9 split into orbits of sizes {8}, {24}, {32}, {8, 16}, {8, 96}\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"Fourier modes of the auxiliary torus: phi_n = Exp[I \
q_n.y]/Sqrt[V_perp] with q_n = 2 Pi n/Lc (n in Z^4) are orthonormal for the \
proper volume element b^4 d^4y (exact integrals: n = m = (1, 0, -2, 3); n = \
(1, 0, -2, 3), m = (1, 1, -2, 3); n = 0, m = (0, 2, 0, 0))\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Parseval on the auxiliary torus: f(y) = Prod_k cos^2(Pi y_k/Lc) = \
Prod_k (1/2 + (1/4) e^(2 Pi I y_k/Lc) + (1/4) e^(-2 Pi I y_k/Lc)) has the 81 \
non-zero coefficients c_n = Sqrt[V_perp] Prod_k w(n_k), w(0) = 1/2, w(+-1) = \
1/4 (three of them checked by integration), and Sum_n |c_n|^2 == Int b^4 d^4y \
f^2 == (3/8)^4 V_perp\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the Laplacian of the auxiliary torus: -(1/b^2) Sum_k d^2 \
phi_n/dy_k^2 == (|q_n|^2/b^2) phi_n (n = (2, -1, 0, 3))\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"scalar Kaluza-Klein masses: for the static metric diag(1, -1, -1, \
-1, -b0^2, ..., -b0^2) the Klein-Gordon operator Box + m^2 (Box f = \
|g|^(-1/2) d_A(|g|^(1/2) g^AB d_B f)) on Exp[-I E x0 + I k.x + I q.y] gives \
(-E^2 + |k|^2 + |q|^2/b0^2 + m^2) times the wave: in ordinary spacetime a \
particle of mass Sqrt[m^2 + |q|^2/b0^2]\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Jacobi's four-square theorem: the number of n in Z^4 with |n|^2 = k \
is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) - 32 sigma(k/4) for k = 1..100 (direct count over \
{-10, ..., 10}^4)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Weyl's law: the number N(R) of n in Z^4 with |n| <= R approaches \
the volume Pi^2 R^4/2 of the four-ball: N(10) = 49689, N(100) = 493490641, \
and |N(R)/(Pi^2 R^4/2) - 1| < 10^-2, 10^-3, 3 10^-5, 5 10^-6, 10^-6 for R = \
10, 30, 100, 300, 1000\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the auxiliary torus today (M8 = 10 TeV, M_Pl = 2.435 10^18 GeV): \
V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6 = 5.929 10^12 GeV^-4, l_perp = V_perp^(1/4) = b0 Lc = \
1560.4 GeV^-1 = 3.079 10^-13 m, lowest Kaluza-Klein mass 2 Pi/l_perp = 4.027 \
MeV; N(mu) = V_perp mu^4/(32 Pi^2) = 1.17 10^13 levels below m_r/2 = 5 GeV \
(the lattice count of section 22.2 agrees to 10^-5) and N(M8) = M_Pl^2/(32 \
Pi^2 M8^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Newton's law in eight dimensions: Omega_6 = 2 Pi^(7/2)/Gamma(7/2) = \
16 Pi^3/15, r^-5 is harmonic away from r = 0 in seven space dimensions \
((1/r^6) d/dr (r^6 d/dr r^-5) = 0), and grad^2 Phi = 8 Pi G8 ((D - 3)/(D - \
2)) M delta^7 (D = 8) gives Phi = -(5/6) kappa M/(5 Omega_6 r^5) = -5 kappa \
M/(32 Pi^3 r^5); the same formula in D = 4 gives -G M/r\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"images = Kaluza-Klein modes (Poisson summation; lengths in units of \
l_perp): Sum_n (r^2 + |n|^2)^(-5/2) == (4 Pi^2/(3 r)) Sum_m Exp[-2 Pi r |m|] \
to 10^-8 at r = 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2 (left: shells with r_4(k) to k = 1.5 10^6 and \
the continuum tail Pi^2 Int k (r^2 + k)^(-5/2) dk; right: shells to k = \
20000)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"near and far field: Z(5/2) = Sum_(n != 0) |n|^-5 = Sum_k r_4(k) \
k^(-5/2) = 7 zeta(5/2) zeta(3/2) = 24.531 (shell sum with tail, to 10^-8); \
near the source r^5 S(r) - 1 -> r^5 Z(5/2) (the ratio lies between 0.98 and 1 \
at r = 1/10 and 1/20, closer to 1 at 1/20): the eight-dimensional law; far \
from it 3 r S/(4 Pi^2) - 1 -> 8 Exp[-2 Pi r], the 8 lightest Kaluza-Klein \
modes (ratio 1 to 2 10^-2 at r = 2 and 3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"graviton + radion: far from the source the images add up to (5 \
kappa M/(32 Pi^3)) (4 Pi^2/(3 V_perp r)) == (5/3) G4 M/r with G4 = kappa/(8 \
Pi V_perp); the radion of section 20.3, coupled to matter by (phi/(Sqrt[3] \
M_Pl)) T, gives the potential -(1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl))^2 M M' Exp[-m_r r]/(4 Pi \
r), and (1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl))^2/(4 Pi) == (2/3) G4 (8 Pi G4 = 1/M_Pl^2): \
graviton 1 + massless radion 2/3 = 5/3\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kaluza-Klein momentum is conserved in the bulk and not at the \
brane: Int b^4 d^4y phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == 1/Sqrt[V_perp] for l = n + m and 0 \
otherwise (exact: n = (1, 0, 0, 2), m = (0, 1, -1, 0), l = (1, 1, -1, 2) and \
(1, 1, -1, 1)); at y = 0, phi_n phi_m phi_l^* == V_perp^(-3/2) for every n, \
m, l\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the delta function of the torus: Int_(-Lc/2)^(Lc/2) Exp[-I q_n y] \
delta(y) dy == 1 for every integer n, so delta^4(y) = Lc^-4 Sum_n Exp[I \
q_n.y] (every mode with the weight 1/Lc^4); a brane source rho4 \
delta^4(y)/b^4 has Int b^4 d^4y (rho4 delta^4(y)/b^4) == rho4, i.e. the \
average rho4/V_perp over the torus\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the world brane W = {x4 = x5 = x6 = x7 = 0}: the induced metric h = \
J^T.g.J of the embedding X = (x0, x1, x2, x3, 0, 0, 0, 0) is, for the \
cosmological metric of section 11.2, the Friedmann-Robertson-Walker metric \
diag(1, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) (independent of b); for the inhomogeneous metric of \
section 11.3 it is diag(n^2, -a^2, -a^2, -a^2) at x4 = 0 with n = 1 + \
x0^2/11, a = 1 + x0/3\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane integrals in eight-dimensional form: at the brane Sqrt|det g| \
== Sqrt|det h| b^4 with b^4 = Sqrt[det(-g_kl)] (cosmological metric; \
inhomogeneous metric exactly at x0 = 1/2), so Int_W d^4x Sqrt|h| L == Int \
d^8X Sqrt|g| (delta^4(y)/b^4) L; test: Int d^4y b^4 (delta^4(y)/b^4) F(y) == \
F(0) = 1 for F = Exp[x4 + 2 x5] Cos[x6 - x7]\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"how the brane sits in the bulk: the Christoffel symbols {k mu nu} \
at the brane (k = 4..7, mu, nu = 0..3; = (1/(2 b^2)) d_k g_mu nu for these \
metrics, b times the extrinsic curvature) all vanish for the cosmological \
metric: the brane is totally geodesic, and a free particle moving along it \
stays on it. For the inhomogeneous metric at x0 = 1/2 the only non-zero one \
is {4 00} = n (d_4 n)/b^2 = 1458/58619: a free particle at rest on the brane \
is accelerated off it\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"explicit forms: every Gamma17[A] is a signed permutation matrix \
(one entry +-1 in each row and column), and 2 Sqrt[2] U has only the entries \
0, +-1, +-I, eight non-zero ones in each row and in each column\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane spinor (x) transverse spinor: Gamma17[mu].Gamma17[nu] == \
U.(gamma_mu.gamma_nu (x) 1_4).U^dag, Gamma17[k].Gamma17[l] == U.(1_4 (x) \
rho_k.rho_l).U^dag and Gamma17[mu].Gamma17[k] == U.(gamma_mu.gamma5 (x) \
rho_k).U^dag (mu, nu = 0..3, k, l = 4..7): the Lorentz group of the brane \
acts on the brane spinor index, the rotations about the brane on the \
transverse index, and the generators that mix them are broken by the \
brane\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the transverse index carries Spin(4) = SU(2) x SU(2): rho4567 == \
-gamma5 (4 x 4), it commutes with every rho_k.rho_l and anticommutes with \
every rho_k; for each even permutation (k, l, m, n) of (4, 5, 6, 7) the \
combination rho_k.rho_l + s rho_m.rho_n vanishes on the eigenspace rho4567 = \
s, and rho_k.rho_l - s rho_m.rho_n acts there with rank 2: the four values of \
a form (2, 1) + (1, 2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"chirality at the brane: PL17 == U.(P_L (x) P_+ + P_R (x) P_-).U^dag \
with P_L,R = (1 -+ gamma5)/2 and P_+- = (1 +- rho4567)/2: the left-handed \
half psi_L (chi17 = -1, 8 components) is two brane-left-handed Weyl spinors \
with rho4567 = +1 and two brane-right-handed ones with rho4567 = -1 (each \
part of rank 4)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"an explicit spinor: psi = U.(u (x) e_1) with the brane spinor u = \
(1, 2, 0, -1): psibar psi == ubar u == 4 and psibar Gamma^mu psi == ubar \
gamma^mu u (mu = 0..3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane tension: for S_W = -Int d^4x Sqrt|h| f_W and h = diag(1/u0, \
-1/u1, -1/u2, -1/u3) (h^00 = u0, h^ii = -u_i), T_mu nu = (2/Sqrt|h|) \
dS_W/dh^mu nu == f_W h_mu nu, T^0_0 == f_W (energy density) and T^1_1 == f_W \
(pressure -f_W: w = -1 along the brane)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"sources smeared over the torus (W(a, b) the comoving energy, \
section 20.2): the brane tension W = a^3 f_W/Lc^4 gives eps = f_W/V_perp, pa \
= -eps, pb = 0; brane radiation W = a^3 r0 a^-4/Lc^4 gives pa = eps/3, pb = \
0; radiation of the bulk, isotropic in the seven space directions, has <cos^2 \
theta> = 3/7 and <sin^2 theta> = 4/7 for the weight cos^2 theta sin^3 theta \
of the momentum sphere, so pa = (1/3)(3/7) eps = eps/7 and pb = (1/4)(4/7) \
eps = eps/7\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the brane in four-dimensional physics: (i) the tension is vacuum \
energy, kappa f_W/V_perp == f_W/M_Pl^2 (V_perp = kappa M_Pl^2), and f_W = \
M8^4 is between 3 10^62 and 5 10^62 times rho_Lambda = 3 H0^2 M_Pl^2 \
Omega_Lambda (section 24.5); (ii) normalcy temperature: (T^7/M8^6)/(T^2/M_Pl) \
== 1 at T* = (M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) = 13.3 GeV, and V_perp T^4 T^3/M_Pl^2 == \
T^7/M8^6; (iii) thin brane: (1/y^3) d/dy (y^3 d/dy y^-2) == 0 and 2 Pi^2 y^3 \
d/dy y^-2 == -4 Pi^2 (the Green's function -1/(4 Pi^2 |y|^2) of the four \
transverse directions), and Sqrt[kappa f_W] == 1/M8 for f_W = M8^4\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"section 26 engine for diagonal metrics: rdScal and rdEin reproduce \
curvature[] of section 11 for the cosmological metric (R and every \
G^A_A)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the 4-sphere of radius r0: Ricci_ij = 3 gamma_ij (gamma the \
unit-sphere metric), Ricci_ij = 0 for i != j, so R(S^4) = 12/r0^2 (in the \
signature of 7+1.nb the space-like block gives R = -12/r0^2, also with \
curvature[] of section 11); the volume of the unit S^4 is 8 Pi^2/3\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"radion on T^4: for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) (N^2 dx0^2 - a^2 dx.dx) - \
e^(2 beta) b0^2 dy.dy the reduced action -(1/(2 kappa)) Int(R + 2 Lambda) - \
Int U equals -(M_Pl^2/2) R_E + 6 M_Pl^2 (d beta)^2 - e^(-4 beta)(M_Pl^2 \
Lambda + V0 U) up to a total derivative (Euler-Lagrange expressions for N, a, \
beta vanish), M_Pl^2 = V0/kappa, V0 = b0^4 Lc^4\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion on S^4: the same reduction for ds^2 = e^(-4 beta) g_E - e^(2 \
beta) r0^2 gamma (unit-sphere gamma) holds with the additional potential \
-(M_Pl^2/2) e^(-4 beta) 12/(r0^2 e^(2 beta)) = -6 M_Pl^2 e^(-6 beta)/r0^2 \
from the curvature of the sphere, V0 = (8 Pi^2/3) r0^4; R is independent of \
the angles\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"n extra dimensions (torus T^n, D = 4 + n, n = 1..4, Einstein frame \
e^(-n B) g_E): the kinetic term is (M_Pl^2/2)(n(n+2)/2)(dB)^2; with the \
note's B = beta_n phi, beta_n = Sqrt[2/(n(n+2))], it is (M_Pl^2/2)(d phi)^2, \
not (M_Pl^2/2)(1/2)(d phi)^2; the form with 1/2 needs beta_n = 1/Sqrt[n(n+2)]\
\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the note's eight-dimensional values alpha = -1/Sqrt[3], beta = \
1/Sqrt[12]: 2 alpha + 4 beta == 0 (Einstein frame), 4 beta == 2/Sqrt[3] (V = \
V0 e^(4 beta phi)), and Sqrt[12] beta == 1, so M_Pl phi_note = Sqrt[12] M_Pl \
ln(b/b0) is the canonical radion of section 20.3\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the cosmological metric with the sphere of radius b(x0) (ds^2 = \
dx0^2 - a^2 dx.dx - b^2 dOmega_4^2): G^A_A = (torus value) + (6, 6, 6, 6, 3, \
3, 3, 3)/b^2 and R = (torus value) - 12/b^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion equation on S^4 (Einstein gravity; 11 and 44 equations with \
the 00 constraint): Hb' + 3 Ha Hb + 4 Hb^2 == kappa (eps/6 - pa/2 + pb/3) + \
Lambda/3 - 3/b^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion on T^4 with U = U0 + U1 beta + (K_U/2) beta^2: a flat vacuum \
at b = b0 needs Lambda + kappa U0 = 0 and U1 = 0, and m_r^2 = V''(beta)/(12 \
M_Pl^2) = kappa K_U/12 (section 20.3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion on S^4 with U: Lambda + kappa U0 == 6/r0^2, kappa U1 == \
-12/r0^2 and m_r^2 == kappa K_U/12 - 2/r0^2 from V(beta); the \
eight-dimensional radion equation gives the same static solution and the same \
mass\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"S^4 with Lambda only: dS4 x S^4 with r0^2 = 9/Lambda, H^2 = 1/r0^2 \
= Lambda/9 solves the 00, 11 and 44 equations; it is a MAXIMUM of V: m^2 = -6 \
H^2 from V(beta), and m^2 = -6/r0^2 = -6 H^2 from the eight-dimensional \
radion equation\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"S^4 with a 4-form flux (illustration; W = a^3 b^4 q^2/(2 b^8) gives \
eps = rho_F, pa = -rho_F, pb = +rho_F): Minkowski x S^4 needs Lambda = 9/(2 \
r0^2) and kappa rho_F = 3/(2 r0^2); m^2 = 6/r0^2 from V(beta) and from the \
eight-dimensional radion equation\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the note's Goldberger-Wise potential in eight dimensions: for a \
static profile Phi(y) (here Phi(x4, x5)) Sqrt|G| (1/2 G^AB dPhi dPhi - 1/2 \
m^2 Phi^2) == -N a^3 e^(-4 beta) Sqrt[gamma] (1/2 e^(-2 beta) |grad \
Phi|^2_gamma + 1/2 m^2 Phi^2): the Einstein-frame factor is e^(-4 beta) \
(e^(-4 beta phi) in the note's notation), not e^(+4 beta phi)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion couples to a mass M on the brane as (phi/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl)) \
M: -M e^(-n beta/2) = -M + (n/2) M beta + ..., with beta = phi/(M_Pl Sqrt[n \
(n + 2)/2]) the coupling is Sqrt[n/(2 (n + 2))]/M_Pl = 1/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl) for n \
= 4, and the fifth-force strength 2 (coupling M_Pl)^2 = n/(n + 2) = 2/3\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"Eot-Wash (|alpha| = 1 excluded for lambda > 38.6 micrometres): a \
radion of strength 2/3 must be heavier than about hbar c/38.6 micrometres = \
5.1 meV; the 10 GeV radion has the range 2.0 10^-17 m; Higgs-radion mixing in \
7+1 is governed by gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl) = 5.8 10^-17\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"zonal harmonics on S^4 (l = 0..6, exact): (1/sin^3 x4) d/dx4 (sin^3 \
x4 d/dx4 C_l^(3/2)(cos x4)) == -l (l + 3) C_l^(3/2), C_l^(3/2)(1) == (l + \
1)(l + 2)/2, and Int over S^4 of (C_l/C_l(1))^2 == V/d_l (unit sphere), so \
the normalized zonal harmonic is Sqrt[d_l/V] at the north pole; d_l == \
Binomial[l + 4, 4] - Binomial[l + 2, 4] for l = 0..20\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Weyl's law on S^4: the number of levels with l(l + 3) <= (mu r)^2 \
approaches (mu r)^4/12 = V mu^4/(32 Pi^2) (V = 8 Pi^2 r^4/3): relative \
deviation -1.0 10^-2, -1.0 10^-4, -1.0 10^-6 at mu r = 10, 100, 1000 (like \
-1/(mu r)^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the brane at the north pole of S^4: the embedding (r0 sin x4 sin x5 \
sin x6 cos x7, ..., r0 cos x4) of S^4 in R^5 induces r0^2 gamma; the north \
pole x4 = 0 is (0, 0, 0, 0, r0); of the 10 rotations L_ab of R^5 (the Killing \
vectors of S^4, SO(5)) the 6 with a, b <= 4 vanish there (SO(4), kept by the \
brane) and the 4 L_a5 move it\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Killing spinors of S^4 (radius r0, frame e^a = (r0, r0 sin x4, ...) \
dx^(a+3), gt_a = I rho_(a+3)): eps_s = exp(s (i/2) x4 gt_1) exp((1/2) x5 gt_1 \
gt_2) exp((1/2) x6 gt_2 gt_3) exp((1/2) x7 gt_3 gt_4) eps0 satisfies nabla_mu \
eps_s == s (i/(2 r0)) e_mu^a gt_a eps_s (s = +-1, all eps0), so the Dirac \
operator gives (2 s i/r0) eps_s: |lambda| = 2/r0, Friedrich's bound n R/(4(n \
- 1)) = 4/r0^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Dirac spectrum on S^4: Weyl's law for spinors (4 components) \
N(|lambda| <= L/r) ~ 4 V (L/r)^4/(32 Pi^2) = L^4/3 agrees with the \
degeneracies 2 x 4 Binomial[l + 3, 3] of the eigenvalues +-i(l + 2)/r (to 2.0 \
10^-3 at L = 1000)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the sphere with the volume of the torus today (V = M_Pl^2/M8^6): r \
= (3 V/(8 Pi^2))^(1/4) = 688.9 GeV^-1 = 1.359 10^-13 m; lowest scalar levels \
4.03 MeV (torus, 8 states) and 2.90 MeV (sphere, l = 1, 5 states); lowest \
dirac16complex level on the sphere 2/r = 2.90 MeV (8 Dirac fermions; the \
torus has 4 massless ones for m = 0); levels below 5 GeV: torus 1.17335 \
10^13, sphere 1.17375 10^13, Weyl 1.17335 10^13\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"RS1 in five dimensions (mostly minus): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 A'^2, \
G^y_y = -6 A'^2; bulk A = k y needs Lambda = -6 k^2; the delta functions A'' \
= +-2 k delta at the branes need the tensions f_UV = +6 k/kappa, f_IR = -6 \
k/kappa (UV positive)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Israel junction at the UV brane of RS1: with K^mu_nu = (1/2) g^mu \
alpha d_y g_alpha nu = -A' delta^mu_nu (normal d_y), [K^mu_nu] - delta^mu_nu \
[K] = 6 k = (coefficient of A'' in G^mu_nu) x (jump of A'), the \
delta-function part of G^mu_nu; in the signature (-,+,+,+,+) of the note \
G^A_B changes sign, so there [K_mu nu - g_mu nu K] = -kappa S_mu nu (the note \
uses +kappa S_mu nu, hence its reversed tensions)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"RS1: M_Pl^2 = (1/kappa) Int_(-Pi R)^(Pi R) e^(-2 k |y|) dy = (1 - \
e^(-2 Pi k R))/(kappa k)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"RS1 radion: with R promoted to T(x), the bulk action is (3/(kappa \
k)) (d e^(-k Pi T))^2 + V(T) + (a total derivative), so the canonical radion \
is mu = Sqrt[6/(kappa k)] e^(-k Pi T) (the note: Sqrt[12/(kappa k)])\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"eight dimensions, warped along one extra direction (ds^2 = e^(-2 \
A(y)) eta - dy^2 - dz.dz): G^mu_nu = 3 A'' - 6 A'^2, G^y_y = -6 A'^2, G^z_z = \
4 A'' - 10 A'^2; with only Lambda (all G^A_A equal) A'' = 0 and A' = 0: the \
note's five-dimensional equations do not carry over\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Goldberger-Wise in RS1: the static bulk scalar (Sqrt|G| = e^(-4 k \
y), G^yy = -1) obeys Phi'' - 4 k Phi' - m^2 Phi = 0, solved by e^(2 k y)(C1 \
e^(nu k y) + C2 e^(-nu k y)), nu = Sqrt[4 + m^2/k^2] = 2 + eps + O(m^4), eps \
= m^2/(4 k^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Goldberger-Wise radion mass: V(mu) = 4 k (mu/f)^4 (v_B - v_A \
(mu/f)^eps)^2 has V'(<mu>) = 0 at (<mu>/f)^eps = v_B/v_A (k Pi <T> = (4 \
k^2/m^2) Log[v_A/v_B]) and V''(<mu>) = 8 k eps^2 v_B^2 <mu>^2/f^4; with f^2 = \
6/(kappa k): m_r^2 = (4/3) kappa k^2 eps^2 v_B^2 (<mu>/f)^2 (the note's f^2 = \
12/(kappa k) gives 2/3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"conformally flat brane metric h = Omega^2 eta (four dimensions, \
Omega(x0, x1)): Sqrt|h| R(h) == -6 Omega box Omega with box = d0^2 - d1^2 \
(curvature conventions of 7+1.nb)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the Higgs boson on the brane (h = Omega^2 eta, Omega = 1 + r/Lambda \
+ a2 r^2, phi_H = v + h, gamma = v/Lambda): the terms linear in (h, r) are \
total derivatives, and to second order L == (1/2)(dh)^2 + (1/2)(1 + 6 xi \
gamma^2)(dr)^2 + 6 xi gamma dh.dr - (1/2) m_h0^2 h^2 - (1/2) m_r0^2 r^2 up to \
total derivatives (Euler-Lagrange expressions in x0 and x1); a2 drops \
out\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"canonical kinetic terms: Transpose[S].K.S == 1 for S = {{1, -6 xi \
gamma/Z}, {0, 1/Z}} if and only if Z^2 = 1 + 6 xi gamma^2 (1 - 6 xi) (the \
note's Z); with the note's literal kinetic terms (no 6 xi gamma^2 for the \
radion) it would be Z^2 = 1 - 36 xi^2 gamma^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"mass mixing: with (h', r') = Q(theta).(h_m, r_m), Q = {{cos, -sin}, \
{sin, cos}}, the off-diagonal element of Transpose[Q].M'.Q is -(1/2)(M'_11 - \
M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta, zero for tan 2 theta = 2 M'_12/(M'_11 \
- M'_22) = 12 gamma xi Z m_h0^2/(m_r0^2 - m_h0^2 (Z^2 - 36 xi^2 gamma^2)) \
(the note's formula); with the inverse matrix (the note's display) it is \
+(1/2)(M'_11 - M'_22) sin 2 theta + M'_12 cos 2 theta (theta -> -theta); (h, \
r) = S.Q.(h_m, r_m) gives C_h = cos theta - (6 xi gamma/Z) sin theta, C_r = \
sin theta/Z\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Higgs-radion mixing in 7+1 (gamma = v/(Sqrt[3] M_Pl), xi = 1, m_r0 \
= 10 GeV, m_h0 = 125.20 GeV; 60-digit arithmetic): |Z - 1| < 10^-30, |theta| \
= 3.5 10^-16, the rates of h -> gamma gamma and h -> g g change by less than \
10^-30; in RS1 with <mu> = 3 TeV gamma = v/(3 TeV) = 0.082\"\>", "True"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00219185978224*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1374]=",ExpressionUUID->"ec397cdc-fe5a-0245-99d7-1ae71fdb32f0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
